itnessed this accident."}, {"name": "~되다 (passive)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "되다 makes a 하다 verb passive: 중단하다 (to stop) → 중단되다 (to be stopped) → 중단되었어요.", "ex_ko": "사고 후 에어쇼는 중단되었어요.", "ex_en": "The air show was suspended after the accident."}, {"name": "~아/어서", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "connective ending showing reason or sequence. 무사하다 → 무사해서 = because they were safe", "ex_ko": "하지만 조종사들이 모두 무사해서 다행이었어요.", "ex_en": "However, it was fortunate that all pilots were safe."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mpaewr4racig' and md5(translation) = '242c6484de25181758a2b2847a61ea42';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["There''s something special about astronauts'' helmets. There are small pieces of Velcro attached to the inside of the helmet. This Velcro serves an important purpose. It helps astronauts scratch their noses during spacewalks. In space, you can''t take off your helmet. So even if your nose itches, you can''t scratch it with your hands. With Velcro, astronauts can rub their noses against the Velcro inside the helmet to scratch the itchy spot. It''s a small idea, but it''s very useful for astronauts.", "Korean Teacher Shortage Becomes Serious, School Classes Disrupted", "What is an \"anxiety bag\"? A Popular Trend", "The United States and China Resume Talks Over Trade Issues", "\"Talking Pig\" Becomes SNS Star", "Apple Greatly Improves iPhone Speed with New AI Chip"], "sentences": [{"text": "우주 비행사들의 헬멧에는 특별한 것이 있어요.", "translation": "Astronauts'' helmets have something special in them.", "vocab": [{"ko": "우주", "en": "space"}, {"ko": "비행사", "en": "pilot; astronaut"}, {"ko": "헬멧", "en": "helmet"}, {"ko": "특별하다", "en": "to be special"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~의 (possessive particle)", "exp": "Marks possession or association. 비행사 → 비행사의", "example_in_sentence": "비행사들의"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에는 (locative + topic particle)", "exp": "Marks location with contrastive/topic emphasis. 헬멧 → 헬멧에는", "example_in_sentence": "헬멧에는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어요 (present polite)", "exp": "Polite present ending: 있다 → 있어요 (there is).", "example_in_sentence": "있어요"}]}, {"text": "헬멧 안쪽에 작은 벨크로 조각이 붙어 있어요.", "translation": "Small pieces of velcro are attached inside the helmet.", "vocab": [{"ko": "안쪽", "en": "inside; inner side"}, {"ko": "조각", "en": "piece; scrap"}, {"ko": "붙다", "en": "to stick; to be attached"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에 (locative particle)", "exp": "Marks location where something exists or occurs. 안쪽 → 안쪽에", "example_in_sentence": "안쪽에"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~어/아 있어요 (resultative state)", "exp": "Indicates a current state resulting from a past action. 붙다 → 붙어 있어요", "example_in_sentence": "붙어 있어요"}]}, {"text": "이 벨크로는 중요한 역할을 해요.", "translation": "This velcro plays an important role.", "vocab": [{"ko": "역할", "en": "role; function"}, {"ko": "하다", "en": "to do; to play (a role)"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는 (topic particle)", "exp": "Marks the topic of the sentence. 벨크로 → 벨크로는", "example_in_sentence": "벨크로는"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "역할을 하다 (to play a role)", "exp": "Common collocation expressing function or duty. The object 역할 takes 을/를.", "example_in_sentence": "역할을 해요"}]}, {"text": "우주 비행사들이 우주 활동을 할 때 코를 긁을 수 있게 도와줘요.", "translation": "It helps astronauts scratch their noses when they are working in space.", "vocab": [{"ko": "활동", "en": "activity"}, {"ko": "코", "en": "nose"}, {"ko": "긁다", "en": "to scratch"}, {"ko": "도와주다", "en": "to help; to assist"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를 (object particle)", "exp": "Marks the direct object: 코 → 코를 (the nose).", "example_in_sentence": "코를"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를 하다 (to do [noun])", "exp": "Makes a noun into a verb phrase. 활동 → 활동을 하다", "example_in_sentence": "활동을 할"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을 수 있다 (can; be able to)", "exp": "Expresses ability or possibility. 긁다 → 긁을 수 있다", "example_in_sentence": "긁을 수 있게"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있게 도와주다", "exp": "''to help someone be able to V''. 긁다 → 긁을 수 있게 도와줘요 (helps them scratch).", "example_in_sentence": "긁을 수 있게 도와줘요"}]}, {"text": "우주에서는 헬멧을 벗을 수 없어요.", "translation": "In space, you cannot take off the helmet.", "vocab": [{"ko": "벗다", "en": "to take off; to remove"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서는 (locative + topic particle)", "exp": "Marks location with topic/contrast. 우주 → 우주에서는", "example_in_sentence": "우주에서는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를 (accusative particle)", "exp": "Marks direct object. 헬멧 → 헬멧을", "example_in_sentence": "헬멧을"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을 수 없다 (cannot; be unable to)", "exp": "Negates possibility or ability. 벗다 → 벗을 수 없어요", "example_in_sentence": "벗을 수 없어요"}]}, {"text": "그래서 코가 가려워도 손으로 긁을 수 없어요.", "translation": "So even if the nose itches, you cannot scratch it with your hands.", "vocab": [{"ko": "가렵다", "en": "to itch"}, {"ko": "손", "en": "hand"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~어/아도 (even if; even though)", "exp": "Introduces a concessive clause. 가렵다 → 가려워도", "example_in_sentence": "가려워도"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~으로 (instrumental particle)", "exp": "Marks means or tool. 손 → 손으로", "example_in_sentence": "손으로"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을 수 없다 (cannot; be unable to)", "exp": "Negates possibility. 긁다 → 긁을 수 없어요", "example_in_sentence": "긁을 수 없어요"}]}, {"text": "벨크로가 있으면 코를 헬멧 안의 벨크로에 비벼서 가려운 곳을 긁을 수 있어요.", "translation": "If there is velcro, you can rub your nose against the velcro inside the helmet and scratch the itchy spot.", "vocab": [{"ko": "있다", "en": "to exist; to have"}, {"ko": "비비다", "en": "to rub"}, {"ko": "곳", "en": "place; spot"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~으면 (if; when [conditional])", "exp": "Introduces a conditional clause. 있다 → 있으면", "example_in_sentence": "있으면"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에 (dative particle)", "exp": "Marks the target or destination of an action. 벨크로 → 벨크로에", "example_in_sentence": "벨크로에"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~어/아서 (connective: and; and then)", "exp": "Connects sequential actions or related clauses. 비비다 → 비벼서", "example_in_sentence": "비벼서"}]}, {"text": "작은 아이디어지만 우주 비행사들에게는 매우 유용해요.", "translation": "Though it is a small idea, it is very useful for astronauts.", "vocab": [{"ko": "아이디어", "en": "idea"}, {"ko": "유용하다", "en": "to be useful"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~지만 (but; although)", "exp": "''but / although''. After a noun ending in a vowel, 이지만 shortens to 지만: 아이디어 → 아이디어지만 (it''s an idea, but).", "example_in_sentence": "아이디어지만"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에게는 (dative + topic particle)", "exp": "Marks recipient/target with topic emphasis. 비행사들 → 비행사들에게는", "example_in_sentence": "비행사들에게는"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "우주", "en": "space", "note": ""}, {"ko": "비행사", "en": "pilot; astronaut", "note": ""}, {"ko": "헬멧", "en": "helmet", "note": ""}, {"ko": "특별하다", "en": "to be special", "note": ""}, {"ko": "안쪽", "en": "inside; inner side", "note": ""}, {"ko": "조각", "en": "piece; scrap", "note": ""}, {"ko": "붙다", "en": "to stick; to be attached", "note": ""}, {"ko": "역할", "en": "role; function", "note": ""}, {"ko": "하다", "en": "to do; to play (a role)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "활동", "en": "activity", "note": ""}, {"ko": "코", "en": "nose", "note": ""}, {"ko": "긁다", "en": "to scratch", "note": ""}, {"ko": "도와주다", "en": "to help; to assist", "note": ""}, {"ko": "벗다", "en": "to take off; to remove", "note": ""}, {"ko": "가렵다", "en": "to itch", "note": ""}, {"ko": "손", "en": "hand", "note": ""}, {"ko": "있다", "en": "to exist; to have", "note": ""}, {"ko": "비비다", "en": "to rub", "note": ""}, {"ko": "곳", "en": "place; spot", "note": ""}, {"ko": "아이디어", "en": "idea", "note": ""}, {"ko": "유용하다", "en": "to be useful", "note": ""}, {"ko": "작다", "en": "to be small", "note": "little in size"}, {"ko": "중요하다", "en": "to be important", "note": "significant, crucial"}, {"ko": "그래서", "en": "so, therefore", "note": "connecting word showing result"}, {"ko": "매우", "en": "very, extremely", "note": "degree adverb"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~의 (possessive particle)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Marks possession or association. 비행사 → 비행사의", "ex_ko": "우주 비행사들의 헬멧에는 특별한 것이 있어요.", "ex_en": "Astronauts'' helmets have something special in them."}, {"name": "~에는 (locative + topic particle)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Marks location with contrastive/topic emphasis. 헬멧 → 헬멧에는", "ex_ko": "우주 비행사들의 헬멧에는 특별한 것이 있어요.", "ex_en": "Astronauts'' helmets have something special in them."}, {"name": "~아/어요 (present polite)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Polite present ending: 있다 → 있어요 (there is).", "ex_ko": "우주 비행사들의 헬멧에는 특별한 것이 있어요.", "ex_en": "Astronauts'' helmets have something special in them."}, {"name": "~에 (locative particle)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Marks location where something exists or occurs. 안쪽 → 안쪽에", "ex_ko": "헬멧 안쪽에 작은 벨크로 조각이 붙어 있어요.", "ex_en": "Small pieces of velcro are attached inside the helmet."}, {"name": "~어/아 있어요 (resultative state)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Indicates a current state resulting from a past action. 붙다 → 붙어 있어요", "ex_ko": "헬멧 안쪽에 작은 벨크로 조각이 붙어 있어요.", "ex_en": "Small pieces of velcro are attached inside the helmet."}, {"name": "~은/는 (topic particle)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Marks the topic of the sentence. 벨크로 → 벨크로는", "ex_ko": "이 벨크로는 중요한 역할을 해요.", "ex_en": "This velcro plays an important role."}, {"name": "~을/를 (accusative particle)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Marks the direct object: 코 → 코를 (the nose).", "ex_ko": "우주 비행사들이 우주 활동을 할 때 코를 긁을 수 있게 도와줘요.", "ex_en": "It helps astronauts scratch their noses when they are working in space."}, {"name": "~을/를 하다 (to do [noun])", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Makes a noun into a verb phrase. 활동 → 활동을 하다", "ex_ko": "우주 비행사들이 우주 활동을 할 때 코를 긁을 수 있게 도와줘요.", "ex_en": "It helps astronauts scratch their noses when they are working in space."}, {"name": "~을 수 있다 (can; be able to)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Expresses ability or possibility. 긁다 → 긁을 수 있다", "ex_ko": "우주 비행사들이 우주 활동을 할 때 코를 긁을 수 있게 도와줘요.", "ex_en": "It helps astronauts scratch their noses when they are working in space."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있게 도와주다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "''to help someone be able to V''. 긁다 → 긁을 수 있게 도와줘요 (helps them scratch).", "ex_ko": "우주 비행사들이 우주 활동을 할 때 코를 긁을 수 있게 도와줘요.", "ex_en": "It helps astronauts scratch their noses when they are working in space."}, {"name": "~에서는 (locative + topic particle)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Marks location with topic/contrast. 우주 → 우주에서는", "ex_ko": "우주에서는 헬멧을 벗을 수 없어요.", "ex_en": "In space, you cannot take off the helmet."}, {"name": "~을 수 없다 (cannot; be unable to)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Negates possibility or ability. 벗다 → 벗을 수 없어요", "ex_ko": "우주에서는 헬멧을 벗을 수 없어요.", "ex_en": "In space, you cannot take off the helmet."}, {"name": "~어/아도 (even if; even though)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Introduces a concessive clause. 가렵다 → 가려워도", "ex_ko": "그래서 코가 가려워도 손으로 긁을 수 없어요.", "ex_en": "So even if the nose itches, you cannot scratch it with your hands."}, {"name": "~으로 (instrumental particle)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Marks means or tool. 손 → 손으로", "ex_ko": "그래서 코가 가려워도 손으로 긁을 수 없어요.", "ex_en": "So even if the nose itches, you cannot scratch it with your hands."}, {"name": "~으면 (if; when [conditional])", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Introduces a conditional clause. 있다 → 있으면", "ex_ko": "벨크로가 있으면 코를 헬멧 안의 벨크로에 비벼서 가려운 곳을 긁을 수 있어요.", "ex_en": "If there is velcro, you can rub your nose against the velcro inside the helmet and scratch the itchy spot."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mpaexycevr22' and md5(translation) = '7ee9cb23006c223052697c5f3a419d22';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["In 1945, the United States dropped leaflets before dropping the atomic bomb on Nagasaki. These leaflets warned Japanese civilians.", "The leaflets had messages written in Japanese. The US announced that it would use a new weapon.", "The US warned that cities would be destroyed if the Japanese government did not surrender. They told civilians to evacuate to safe places.", "However, many people did not believe this warning. A few days later, the second atomic bomb was dropped on Nagasaki."], "sentences": [{"text": "1945년 미국이 나가사키에 핵폭탄을 떨어뜨리기 전에 전단을 뿌렸어요.", "translation": "In 1945, the United States dropped leaflets before dropping the atomic bomb on Nagasaki.", "vocab": [{"ko": "미국", "en": "United States", "note": ""}, {"ko": "핵폭탄", "en": "nuclear bomb", "note": ""}, {"ko": "떨어뜨리다", "en": "to drop", "note": ""}, {"ko": "전단", "en": "leaflet, flyer", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~기 전에", "exp": "before V-ing. Verb stem + 기 전에 = before doing that action. 떨어뜨리다 → 떨어뜨리기 전에 (before dropping)", "example_in_sentence": "떨어뜨리기 전에"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었/였어요", "exp": "past polite ending. Verb stem + 았/었어요 = did (polite). 뿌리다 → 뿌렸어요 (dropped/scattered)", "example_in_sentence": "뿌렸어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에 (location/time)", "exp": "static location / time / direction", "example_in_sentence": "나가사키에"}]}, {"text": "이 전단들은 일본 시민들에게 경고했어요.", "translation": "These leaflets warned Japanese civilians.", "vocab": [{"ko": "시민", "en": "citizen, civilian", "note": ""}, {"ko": "경고하다", "en": "to warn", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에게", "exp": "to (person). Shows the recipient of an action. 시민들에게 = to the civilians", "example_in_sentence": "시민들에게"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었/였어요", "exp": "past polite ending. 경고하다 → 경고했어요 (warned)", "example_in_sentence": "경고했어요"}]}, {"text": "전단에는 일본어로 메시지가 적혀 있었어요.", "translation": "The leaflets had messages written in Japanese.", "vocab": [{"ko": "일본어", "en": "Japanese language", "note": ""}, {"ko": "메시지", "en": "message", "note": ""}, {"ko": "적히다", "en": "to be written", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에는", "exp": "topic marker after location particle. 전단에 (on leaflets) + 는 (topic) = as for on the leaflets", "example_in_sentence": "전단에는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)로", "exp": "means/method particle. Shows how something is done. 일본어로 = in Japanese (language)", "example_in_sentence": "일본어로"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어 있다", "exp": "Shows a state that remains after an action: 적히다 (to be written) → 적혀 있었어요 (was written).", "example_in_sentence": "적혀 있었어요"}]}, {"text": "미국은 새로운 무기를 사용할 것이라고 알렸어요.", "translation": "The US announced that it would use a new weapon.", "vocab": [{"ko": "새롭다", "en": "to be new", "note": ""}, {"ko": "무기", "en": "weapon", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사용하다", "en": "to use", "note": ""}, {"ko": "알리다", "en": "to inform, announce", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄴ/은", "exp": "past verb modifier or present adjective modifier. 새롭다 → 새로운 (new, modifying noun)", "example_in_sentence": "새로운"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를", "exp": "object marker. Shows direct object of verb. 무기를 = weapon (as object)", "example_in_sentence": "무기를"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 것이다", "exp": "Future / prediction, ''will''. 사용하다 → 사용할 것이다 (will use).", "example_in_sentence": "사용할 것이라고"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(이)라고 알리다", "exp": "Reports what was announced. After 것이다 the quote ending is 이라고: 사용할 것이다 → 사용할 것이라고 알렸어요 (announced that it would use).", "example_in_sentence": "것이라고 알렸어요"}]}, {"text": "미국은 일본 정부가 항복하지 않으면 도시들이 파괴될 것이라고 경고했어요.", "translation": "The US warned that cities would be destroyed if the Japanese government did not surrender.", "vocab": [{"ko": "정부", "en": "government", "note": ""}, {"ko": "항복하다", "en": "to surrender", "note": ""}, {"ko": "도시", "en": "city", "note": ""}, {"ko": "파괴되다", "en": "to be destroyed", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가", "exp": "subject marker. Shows subject of sentence. 정부가 = the government (as subject)", "example_in_sentence": "정부가"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~지 않다", "exp": "Makes a verb negative: 항복하다 → 항복하지 않다 (not surrender).", "example_in_sentence": "항복하지 않으면"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)면", "exp": "''if''. 않다 → 않으면 (if (they) do not ...).", "example_in_sentence": "않으면"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 것이라고 경고하다", "exp": "Reports a warning: 파괴되다 → 파괴될 것이다 (will be destroyed) → 파괴될 것이라고 경고했어요 (warned that they would be destroyed).", "example_in_sentence": "파괴될 것이라고"}]}, {"text": "시민들에게 안전한 곳으로 피하라고 했어요.", "translation": "They told civilians to evacuate to safe places.", "vocab": [{"ko": "안전하다", "en": "to be safe", "note": ""}, {"ko": "곳", "en": "place", "note": ""}, {"ko": "피하다", "en": "to avoid; to take shelter", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄴ/은", "exp": "adjective modifier. 안전하다 → 안전한 (safe, modifying noun)", "example_in_sentence": "안전한"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)로", "exp": "direction particle. Shows direction of movement. 곳으로 = to the place", "example_in_sentence": "곳으로"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)라고 하다", "exp": "Reports a command: 피하다 → 피하라 (Take shelter!) → 피하라고 했어요 (told them to take shelter).", "example_in_sentence": "피하라고 했어요"}]}, {"text": "하지만 많은 사람들이 이 경고를 믿지 않았어요.", "translation": "However, many people did not believe this warning.", "vocab": [{"ko": "많다", "en": "to be many, much", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사람", "en": "person", "note": ""}, {"ko": "믿다", "en": "to believe", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "하지만", "exp": "however, but. Connects contrasting clauses.", "example_in_sentence": "하지만"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄴ/은", "exp": "adjective modifier. 많다 → 많은 (many, modifying noun)", "example_in_sentence": "많은"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~지 않다", "exp": "negation. 믿다 → 믿지 않다 → 믿지 않았어요 (did not believe)", "example_in_sentence": "믿지 않았어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었/였어요", "exp": "past polite ending combined with negation. 믿지 않다 → 믿지 않았어요", "example_in_sentence": "않았어요"}]}, {"text": "며칠 후 나가사키에 두 번째 원자폭탄이 투하됐어요.", "translation": "A few days later, the second atomic bomb was dropped on Nagasaki.", "vocab": [{"ko": "며칠", "en": "a few days", "note": ""}, {"ko": "후", "en": "after, later", "note": ""}, {"ko": "번째", "en": "ordinal number suffix", "note": ""}, {"ko": "원자폭탄", "en": "atomic bomb", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에", "exp": "location particle. Shows where action takes place. 나가사키에 = in/on Nagasaki", "example_in_sentence": "나가사키에"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가", "exp": "subject marker. 원자폭탄이 = the atomic bomb (as subject)", "example_in_sentence": "원자폭탄이"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었/였어요", "exp": "past polite ending. 투하되다 → 투하됐어요 (was dropped)", "example_in_sentence": "투하됐어요"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "미국", "en": "United States", "note": ""}, {"ko": "핵폭탄", "en": "nuclear bomb", "note": ""}, {"ko": "떨어뜨리다", "en": "to drop", "note": ""}, {"ko": "전단", "en": "leaflet, flyer", "note": ""}, {"ko": "시민", "en": "citizen, civilian", "note": ""}, {"ko": "경고하다", "en": "to warn", "note": ""}, {"ko": "일본어", "en": "Japanese language", "note": ""}, {"ko": "메시지", "en": "message", "note": ""}, {"ko": "적히다", "en": "to be written", "note": ""}, {"ko": "새롭다", "en": "to be new", "note": ""}, {"ko": "무기", "en": "weapon", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사용하다", "en": "to use", "note": ""}, {"ko": "알리다", "en": "to inform, announce", "note": ""}, {"ko": "정부", "en": "government", "note": ""}, {"ko": "항복하다", "en": "to surrender", "note": ""}, {"ko": "도시", "en": "city", "note": ""}, {"ko": "파괴되다", "en": "to be destroyed", "note": ""}, {"ko": "안전하다", "en": "to be safe", "note": ""}, {"ko": "곳", "en": "place", "note": ""}, {"ko": "피하다", "en": "to avoid; to take shelter", "note": ""}, {"ko": "많다", "en": "to be many, much", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사람", "en": "person", "note": ""}, {"ko": "믿다", "en": "to believe", "note": ""}, {"ko": "며칠", "en": "a few days", "note": ""}, {"ko": "후", "en": "after, later", "note": ""}, {"ko": "번째", "en": "ordinal number suffix", "note": ""}, {"ko": "원자폭탄", "en": "atomic bomb", "note": ""}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~기 전에", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "before V-ing. Verb stem + 기 전에 = before doing that action. 떨어뜨리다 → 떨어뜨리기 전에 (before dropping)", "ex_ko": "1945년 미국이 나가사키에 핵폭탄을 떨어뜨리기 전에 전단을 뿌렸어요.", "ex_en": "In 1945, the United States dropped leaflets before dropping the atomic bomb on Nagasaki."}, {"name": "~았/었/였어요", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "past polite ending. Verb stem + 았/었어요 = did (polite). 뿌리다 → 뿌렸어요 (dropped/scattered)", "ex_ko": "1945년 미국이 나가사키에 핵폭탄을 떨어뜨리기 전에 전단을 뿌렸어요.", "ex_en": "In 1945, the United States dropped leaflets before dropping the atomic bomb on Nagasaki."}, {"name": "~에 (location/time)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "location particle. Shows where action takes place. 나가사키에 = in/on Nagasaki", "ex_ko": "1945년 미국이 나가사키에 핵폭탄을 떨어뜨리기 전에 전단을 뿌렸어요.", "ex_en": "In 1945, the United States dropped leaflets before dropping the atomic bomb on Nagasaki."}, {"name": "~에게", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "to (person). Shows the recipient of an action. 시민들에게 = to the civilians", "ex_ko": "이 전단들은 일본 시민들에게 경고했어요.", "ex_en": "These leaflets warned Japanese civilians."}, {"name": "~에는", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "topic marker after location particle. 전단에 (on leaflets) + 는 (topic) = as for on the leaflets", "ex_ko": "전단에는 일본어로 메시지가 적혀 있었어요.", "ex_en": "The leaflets had messages written in Japanese."}, {"name": "~(으)로", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "means/method particle. Shows how something is done. 일본어로 = in Japanese (language)", "ex_ko": "전단에는 일본어로 메시지가 적혀 있었어요.", "ex_en": "The leaflets had messages written in Japanese."}, {"name": "~아/어 있다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Shows a state that remains after an action: 적히다 (to be written) → 적혀 있었어요 (was written).", "ex_ko": "전단에는 일본어로 메시지가 적혀 있었어요.", "ex_en": "The leaflets had messages written in Japanese."}, {"name": "~ㄴ/은", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "past verb modifier or present adjective modifier. 새롭다 → 새로운 (new, modifying noun)", "ex_ko": "미국은 새로운 무기를 사용할 것이라고 알렸어요.", "ex_en": "The US announced that it would use a new weapon."}, {"name": "~을/를", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "object marker. Shows direct object of verb. 무기를 = weapon (as object)", "ex_ko": "미국은 새로운 무기를 사용할 것이라고 알렸어요.", "ex_en": "The US announced that it would use a new weapon."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 것이다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Future / prediction, ''will''. 사용하다 → 사용할 것이다 (will use).", "ex_ko": "미국은 새로운 무기를 사용할 것이라고 알렸어요.", "ex_en": "The US announced that it would use a new weapon."}, {"name": "~(이)라고 알리다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Reports what was announced. After 것이다 the quote ending is 이라고: 사용할 것이다 → 사용할 것이라고 알렸어요 (announced that it would use).", "ex_ko": "미국은 새로운 무기를 사용할 것이라고 알렸어요.", "ex_en": "The US announced that it would use a new weapon."}, {"name": "~이/가", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "subject marker. Shows subject of sentence. 정부가 = the government (as subject)", "ex_ko": "미국은 일본 정부가 항복하지 않으면 도시들이 파괴될 것이라고 경고했어요.", "ex_en": "The US warned that cities would be destroyed if the Japanese government did not surrender."}, {"name": "~지 않다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Makes a verb negative: 항복하다 → 항복하지 않다 (not surrender).", "ex_ko": "미국은 일본 정부가 항복하지 않으면 도시들이 파괴될 것이라고 경고했어요.", "ex_en": "The US warned that cities would be destroyed if the Japanese government did not surrender."}, {"name": "~(으)면", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "''if''. 않다 → 않으면 (if (they) do not ...).", "ex_ko": "미국은 일본 정부가 항복하지 않으면 도시들이 파괴될 것이라고 경고했어요.", "ex_en": "The US warned that cities would be destroyed if the Japanese government did not surrender."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 것이라고 경고하다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Reports a warning: 파괴되다 → 파괴될 것이다 (will be destroyed) → 파괴될 것이라고 경고했어요 (warned that they would be destroyed).", "ex_ko": "미국은 일본 정부가 항복하지 않으면 도시들이 파괴될 것이라고 경고했어요.", "ex_en": "The US warned that cities would be destroyed if the Japanese government did not surrender."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mpaez25dj4wo' and md5(translation) = 'f91b4827fb6d93a74f4b8b4b7fbd2a3d';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["In Mumbai, India, there is a special garbage truck. This garbage truck collects memories of ex-lovers. People bring items that hold memories with their former partners. These are things like photographs, letters, and gifts. They say that throwing away these items eases the heart. You can make a new start. Many people are using this garbage truck. It is one of the ways to soothe the difficult feelings after a breakup.", "Korea''s teacher shortage crisis becomes severe, disrupting school classes", "What is an ''anxiety bag''? A popular trend", "The United States and China are in talks again over trade issues", "\"The talking pig\" becomes an SNS star", "The ''nothing maxing'' trend of doing nothing spreads"], "sentences": [{"text": "인도 뭄바이에 특별한 쓰레기차가 있어요.", "translation": "There is a special garbage truck in Mumbai, India.", "vocab": [{"ko": "인도", "en": "India"}, {"ko": "특별하다", "en": "to be special"}, {"ko": "쓰레기차", "en": "garbage truck"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에", "exp": "Locative particle indicating location where something exists.", "example_in_sentence": "뭄바이에"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~가", "exp": "Nominative particle marking the subject of existence (있다). 특별한 쓰레기차 → 특별한 쓰레기차가.", "example_in_sentence": "쓰레기차가"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "있어요", "exp": "Present tense polite form of 있다 (to exist/be present). Base → 있어요.", "example_in_sentence": "있어요"}]}, {"text": "이 쓰레기차는 헤어진 연인들의 추억을 모아요.", "translation": "This garbage truck collects memories of couples who have broken up.", "vocab": [{"ko": "헤어지다", "en": "to separate; to break up"}, {"ko": "연인", "en": "lover; sweetheart"}, {"ko": "추억", "en": "memory"}, {"ko": "모으다", "en": "to collect; to gather"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (past verb modifier)", "exp": "Past modifier for verbs: 헤어지다 (to break up) → 헤어진 연인들 (couples who broke up).", "example_in_sentence": "헤어진"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~의", "exp": "Possessive particle indicating belonging. 연인들의 (of the lovers).", "example_in_sentence": "연인들의"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을", "exp": "Accusative particle marking direct object of action verb. 추억을 모으다 (collect memories).", "example_in_sentence": "추억을"}]}, {"text": "사람들은 옛 연인과의 추억이 담긴 물건들을 가져와요.", "translation": "People bring things that contain memories with their ex-lovers.", "vocab": [{"ko": "옛", "en": "former; old"}, {"ko": "담기다", "en": "to be contained; to be filled"}, {"ko": "물건", "en": "thing; object"}, {"ko": "가져오다", "en": "to bring; to carry"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (past verb modifier)", "exp": "담기다 (to be contained) → 담긴 물건들 (things that hold (memories)).", "example_in_sentence": "담긴"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을", "exp": "Accusative particle marking direct object. 물건들을 가져오다 (bring things).", "example_in_sentence": "물건들을"}]}, {"text": "사진, 편지, 선물 같은 것들이에요.", "translation": "They are things like photos, letters, and gifts.", "vocab": [{"ko": "사진", "en": "photograph"}, {"ko": "편지", "en": "letter"}, {"ko": "선물", "en": "gift; present"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~같은", "exp": "Modifier meaning ''like'' or ''such as''. Examples of a category follow.", "example_in_sentence": "같은"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이에요", "exp": "Polite form of 이다 ''to be'' after a consonant: 것들 → 것들이에요 (are things).", "example_in_sentence": "것들이에요"}]}, {"text": "이런 물건들을 버리면 마음이 편해진다고 해요.", "translation": "People say that throwing away such things makes them feel at ease.", "vocab": [{"ko": "버리다", "en": "to throw away; to discard"}, {"ko": "마음", "en": "heart; mind"}, {"ko": "편하다", "en": "to be comfortable; to be at ease"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)면", "exp": "''if / when''. After a vowel just add 면: 버리다 → 버리면 (if you throw away).", "example_in_sentence": "버리면"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어지다", "exp": "Passive/change auxiliary expressing becoming a state. 편하다 → 편해지다 (become comfortable). 편해지다 → 편해진다.", "example_in_sentence": "편해진다"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~다고 하다", "exp": "Reported speech pattern. Reports what people say. 편해진다 + ~다고 하다 = it is said that.", "example_in_sentence": "편해진다고 해요"}]}, {"text": "새로운 시작을 할 수 있어요.", "translation": "You can make a new start.", "vocab": [{"ko": "새롭다", "en": "to be new"}, {"ko": "시작", "en": "start; beginning"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~을", "exp": "Accusative particle marking object of action. 시작을 하다 (make a start).", "example_in_sentence": "시작을"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄹ 수 있다", "exp": "Modal expressing possibility/ability. 하다 → 할 수 있어요 (can do).", "example_in_sentence": "할 수 있어요"}]}, {"text": "많은 사람들이 이 쓰레기차를 이용하고 있어요.", "translation": "Many people are using this garbage truck.", "vocab": [{"ko": "많다", "en": "to be many; to be much"}, {"ko": "이용하다", "en": "to use; to utilize"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~를", "exp": "Accusative particle marking direct object. 쓰레기차를 이용하다 (use the truck).", "example_in_sentence": "쓰레기차를"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있다", "exp": "Progressive aspect auxiliary indicating ongoing action. 이용하다 → 이용하고 있어요 (are using).", "example_in_sentence": "이용하고 있어요"}]}, {"text": "헤어진 후 힘든 마음을 달래는 방법 중 하나예요.", "translation": "It is one way to soothe a heavy heart after a breakup.", "vocab": [{"ko": "헤어지다", "en": "to separate; to break up"}, {"ko": "힘들다", "en": "to be difficult; to be hard"}, {"ko": "달래다", "en": "to comfort; to soothe"}, {"ko": "방법", "en": "method; way"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 (verb modifier)", "exp": "Present modifier for verbs: 달래다 (to soothe) → 달래는 방법 (a way to soothe).", "example_in_sentence": "달래는"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~ 중 하나", "exp": "Expression meaning ''one of'' or ''one among''. Indicates selection from a group.", "example_in_sentence": "방법 중 하나예요"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "인도", "en": "India", "note": ""}, {"ko": "특별하다", "en": "to be special", "note": ""}, {"ko": "쓰레기차", "en": "garbage truck", "note": ""}, {"ko": "헤어지다", "en": "to separate; to break up", "note": ""}, {"ko": "연인", "en": "lover; sweetheart", "note": ""}, {"ko": "추억", "en": "memory", "note": ""}, {"ko": "모으다", "en": "to collect; to gather", "note": ""}, {"ko": "옛", "en": "former; old", "note": ""}, {"ko": "담기다", "en": "to be contained; to be filled", "note": ""}, {"ko": "물건", "en": "thing; object", "note": ""}, {"ko": "가져오다", "en": "to bring; to carry", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사진", "en": "photograph", "note": ""}, {"ko": "편지", "en": "letter", "note": ""}, {"ko": "선물", "en": "gift; present", "note": ""}, {"ko": "버리다", "en": "to throw away; to discard", "note": ""}, {"ko": "마음", "en": "heart; mind", "note": ""}, {"ko": "편하다", "en": "to be comfortable; to be at ease", "note": ""}, {"ko": "새롭다", "en": "to be new", "note": ""}, {"ko": "시작", "en": "start; beginning", "note": ""}, {"ko": "많다", "en": "to be many; to be much", "note": ""}, {"ko": "이용하다", "en": "to use; to utilize", "note": ""}, {"ko": "힘들다", "en": "to be difficult; to be hard", "note": ""}, {"ko": "달래다", "en": "to comfort; to soothe", "note": ""}, {"ko": "방법", "en": "method; way", "note": ""}, {"ko": "있다", "en": "to exist, to have", "note": "existence verb"}, {"ko": "사람", "en": "person, people", "note": "noun"}, {"ko": "같다", "en": "to be the same, to be like", "note": "adjective"}, {"ko": "이런", "en": "this kind of, such", "note": "demonstrative"}, {"ko": "하다", "en": "to do", "note": "verb"}, {"ko": "후", "en": "after", "note": "time noun"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~에", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Locative particle indicating location where something exists.", "ex_ko": "인도 뭄바이에 특별한 쓰레기차가 있어요.", "ex_en": "There is a special garbage truck in Mumbai, India."}, {"name": "~가", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Nominative particle marking the subject of existence (있다). 특별한 쓰레기차 → 특별한 쓰레기차가.", "ex_ko": "인도 뭄바이에 특별한 쓰레기차가 있어요.", "ex_en": "There is a special garbage truck in Mumbai, India."}, {"name": "있어요", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Present tense polite form of 있다 (to exist/be present). Base → 있어요.", "ex_ko": "인도 뭄바이에 특별한 쓰레기차가 있어요.", "ex_en": "There is a special garbage truck in Mumbai, India."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄴ (past verb modifier)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Past modifier for verbs: 헤어지다 (to break up) → 헤어진 연인들 (couples who broke up).", "ex_ko": "이 쓰레기차는 헤어진 연인들의 추억을 모아요.", "ex_en": "This garbage truck collects memories of couples who have broken up."}, {"name": "~의", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Possessive particle indicating belonging. 연인들의 (of the lovers).", "ex_ko": "이 쓰레기차는 헤어진 연인들의 추억을 모아요.", "ex_en": "This garbage truck collects memories of couples who have broken up."}, {"name": "~을", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Accusative particle marking direct object of action verb. 추억을 모으다 (collect memories).", "ex_ko": "이 쓰레기차는 헤어진 연인들의 추억을 모아요.", "ex_en": "This garbage truck collects memories of couples who have broken up."}, {"name": "~이에요", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Polite form of 이다 ''to be'' after a consonant: 것들 → 것들이에요 (are things).", "ex_ko": "사진, 편지, 선물 같은 것들이에요.", "ex_en": "They are things like photos, letters, and gifts."}, {"name": "~(으)면", "level": "Starter", "exp": "''if / when''. After a vowel just add 면: 버리다 → 버리면 (if you throw away).", "ex_ko": "이런 물건들을 버리면 마음이 편해진다고 해요.", "ex_en": "People say that throwing away such things makes them feel at ease."}, {"name": "~아/어지다", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Passive/change auxiliary expressing becoming a state. 편하다 → 편해지다 (become comfortable). 편해지다 → 편해진다.", "ex_ko": "이런 물건들을 버리면 마음이 편해진다고 해요.", "ex_en": "People say that throwing away such things makes them feel at ease."}, {"name": "~다고 하다", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Reported speech pattern. Reports what people say. 편해진다 + ~다고 하다 = it is said that.", "ex_ko": "이런 물건들을 버리면 마음이 편해진다고 해요.", "ex_en": "People say that throwing away such things makes them feel at ease."}, {"name": "~ㄹ 수 있다", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Modal expressing possibility/ability. 하다 → 할 수 있어요 (can do).", "ex_ko": "새로운 시작을 할 수 있어요.", "ex_en": "You can make a new start."}, {"name": "~를", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Accusative particle marking direct object. 쓰레기차를 이용하다 (use the truck).", "ex_ko": "많은 사람들이 이 쓰레기차를 이용하고 있어요.", "ex_en": "Many people are using this garbage truck."}, {"name": "~고 있다", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Progressive aspect auxiliary indicating ongoing action. 이용하다 → 이용하고 있어요 (are using).", "ex_ko": "많은 사람들이 이 쓰레기차를 이용하고 있어요.", "ex_en": "Many people are using this garbage truck."}, {"name": "~는 (verb modifier)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Present modifier for verbs: 달래다 (to soothe) → 달래는 방법 (a way to soothe).", "ex_ko": "헤어진 후 힘든 마음을 달래는 방법 중 하나예요.", "ex_en": "It is one way to soothe a heavy heart after a breakup."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mpaf0ax3r8bk' and md5(translation) = '4698e6600362c67d0c8115c49c122f36';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["In 2014, Hollywood actor Ben Affleck was permanently banned from a casino in Las Vegas. It happened while he was playing blackjack at the Hard Rock Hotel and Casino. Casino staff monitored Affleck''s game through surveillance cameras. He was using a technique called card counting in high-stakes games. The casino security team approached Affleck and explained the situation. They told him that he was ''too skilled.'' Ultimately, the casino classified Affleck as an ''advantage player.'' This refers to a player who has a favorable position in the game. As a result, he was permanently banned from playing at the blackjack table.", "Korean teacher shortage becomes serious, disrupts school classes", "What is an ''anxiety bag''? Popular trend", "The United States and China resume talks over trade issues", "\"Talking pig\" becomes SNS star", "Doing nothing: ''nothing maxing'' trend spreads"], "sentences": [{"text": "2014년 할리우드 배우 벤 애플렉이 라스베이거스의 한 카지노에서 영구 출입금지를 당했어요.", "translation": "In 2014, Hollywood actor Ben Affleck was permanently banned from a casino in Las Vegas.", "vocab": [{"ko": "할리우드", "en": "Hollywood"}, {"ko": "배우", "en": "actor"}, {"ko": "라스베이거스", "en": "Las Vegas"}, {"ko": "출입금지", "en": "ban (from entry/exit)"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를 당하다", "exp": "''to suffer N'' (something bad done to you). 출입금지를 당하다 = to be banned.", "example_in_sentence": "출입금지를 당했어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서 (location)", "exp": "Locative particle marking where an action takes place. 카지노(casino) + 에서.", "example_in_sentence": "카지노에서 영구 출입금지를 당했어요"}]}, {"text": "하드록 호텔 앤 카지노에서 블랙잭을 하던 중에 일어난 일이었어요.", "translation": "It happened while he was playing blackjack at the Hard Rock Hotel and Casino.", "vocab": [{"ko": "하드록 호텔", "en": "Hard Rock Hotel"}, {"ko": "블랙잭", "en": "blackjack"}, {"ko": "일어나다", "en": "to happen; to occur"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~던 중에", "exp": "Temporal expression marking the exact moment when an action was in progress. 하다(do) → 하던(past progressive) + 중에(during).", "example_in_sentence": "블랙잭을 하던 중에 일어난 일"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ 일이다", "exp": "''it was something that ~''. 일어나다 → 일어난 일이었어요 (it was something that happened).", "example_in_sentence": "일어난 일이었어요"}]}, {"text": "카지노 관계자들은 감시 카메라를 통해 애플렉의 게임을 지켜봤어요.", "translation": "Casino staff monitored his game through surveillance cameras.", "vocab": [{"ko": "관계자", "en": "staff; personnel; person in charge"}, {"ko": "감시", "en": "surveillance; monitoring"}, {"ko": "지켜보다", "en": "to watch; to observe"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를 통해", "exp": "''through / by means of N''. 감시 카메라를 통해 = through surveillance cameras.", "example_in_sentence": "감시 카메라를 통해"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Simple past tense. 지켜보다 → 지켜봤어요.", "example_in_sentence": "지켜봤어요"}]}, {"text": "그는 고액 게임에서 카드 카운팅이라는 기술을 사용하고 있었어요.", "translation": "He was using a technique called card counting in high-stakes games.", "vocab": [{"ko": "고액", "en": "high amount; high-stakes"}, {"ko": "카드 카운팅", "en": "card counting"}, {"ko": "기술", "en": "technique; skill"}, {"ko": "사용하다", "en": "to use"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~이라는", "exp": "Relative modifier ''called/named''. 기술(technique) + 이라는 (which is called).", "example_in_sentence": "카드 카운팅이라는 기술"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있었어요", "exp": "Past progressive aspect. 사용하다 → 사용하고(connective) + 있었어요 (was doing).", "example_in_sentence": "사용하고 있었어요"}]}, {"text": "카지노 보안팀은 애플렉에게 다가가서 상황을 설명했어요.", "translation": "The casino security team approached him and explained the situation.", "vocab": [{"ko": "보안팀", "en": "security team"}, {"ko": "다가가다", "en": "to approach; to come near"}, {"ko": "상황", "en": "situation; circumstance"}, {"ko": "설명하다", "en": "to explain"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어서 (sequential)", "exp": "Sequential connective linking two actions; the first action precedes the second. 다가가다 → 다가가서.", "example_in_sentence": "다가가서 상황을 설명했어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Simple past tense. 설명하다 → 설명했어요.", "example_in_sentence": "설명했어요"}]}, {"text": "그들은 그가 ''너무 실력이 좋다''고 말했어요.", "translation": "They said that he was ''too skilled.''", "vocab": [{"ko": "실력", "en": "skill; ability"}, {"ko": "좋다", "en": "to be good"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~다고 말하다", "exp": "Reported speech construction. Declarative ending ~다 + 고(quotative) + 말했어요 (said).", "example_in_sentence": "좋다''고 말했어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "실력이 좋다", "exp": "''to be skilled'' (literally ''skill is good'').", "example_in_sentence": "실력이 좋다"}]}, {"text": "결국 카지노는 애플렉을 ''어드밴티지 플레이어''로 분류했어요.", "translation": "Ultimately, the casino classified him as an ''advantage player.''", "vocab": [{"ko": "결국", "en": "ultimately; in the end; after all"}, {"ko": "어드밴티지 플레이어", "en": "advantage player"}, {"ko": "분류하다", "en": "to classify; to categorize"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)로 분류하다", "exp": "''to classify as N''. After a vowel just add 로: 플레이어 → 플레이어로 분류했어요 (classified as a player).", "example_in_sentence": "어드밴티지 플레이어''로 분류했어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Simple past tense. 분류하다 → 분류했어요.", "example_in_sentence": "분류했어요"}]}, {"text": "이는 게임에서 유리한 위치에 있는 플레이어를 뜻해요.", "translation": "This means a player who is in an advantageous position in a game.", "vocab": [{"ko": "유리하다", "en": "to be advantageous; to be favorable"}, {"ko": "위치", "en": "position; place"}, {"ko": "뜻하다", "en": "to mean; to signify"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 (verb modifier)", "exp": "Present modifier: 있다 → 있는 플레이어 (a player who is (in a position)).", "example_in_sentence": "있는 플레이어"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~를 뜻하다", "exp": "Object marker + mean verb. Forms definition/meaning expression.", "example_in_sentence": "플레이어를 뜻해요"}]}, {"text": "그 결과 그는 블랙잭 테이블에서 평생 게임을 할 수 없게 되었어요.", "translation": "As a result, he became unable to play games at blackjack tables for the rest of his life.", "vocab": [{"ko": "결과", "en": "result; consequence; outcome"}, {"ko": "평생", "en": "lifetime; for one''s whole life"}, {"ko": "없다", "en": "to not exist; cannot"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 수 없다", "exp": "''cannot''. 하다 → 할 수 없다 (cannot do / cannot play).", "example_in_sentence": "할 수 없게"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~게 되다", "exp": "''to end up / come to be''. 할 수 없다 → 할 수 없게 되었어요 (ended up unable to play).", "example_in_sentence": "없게 되었어요"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "할리우드", "en": "Hollywood", "note": ""}, {"ko": "배우", "en": "actor", "note": ""}, {"ko": "라스베이거스", "en": "Las Vegas", "note": ""}, {"ko": "출입금지", "en": "ban (from entry/exit)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "하드록 호텔", "en": "Hard Rock Hotel", "note": ""}, {"ko": "블랙잭", "en": "blackjack", "note": ""}, {"ko": "일어나다", "en": "to happen; to occur", "note": ""}, {"ko": "관계자", "en": "staff; personnel; person in charge", "note": ""}, {"ko": "감시", "en": "surveillance; monitoring", "note": ""}, {"ko": "지켜보다", "en": "to watch; to observe", "note": ""}, {"ko": "고액", "en": "high amount; high-stakes", "note": ""}, {"ko": "카드 카운팅", "en": "card counting", "note": ""}, {"ko": "기술", "en": "technique; skill", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사용하다", "en": "to use", "note": ""}, {"ko": "보안팀", "en": "security team", "note": ""}, {"ko": "다가가다", "en": "to approach; to come near", "note": ""}, {"ko": "상황", "en": "situation; circumstance", "note": ""}, {"ko": "설명하다", "en": "to explain", "note": ""}, {"ko": "실력", "en": "skill; ability", "note": ""}, {"ko": "좋다", "en": "to be good", "note": ""}, {"ko": "결국", "en": "ultimately; in the end; after all", "note": ""}, {"ko": "어드밴티지 플레이어", "en": "advantage player", "note": ""}, {"ko": "분류하다", "en": "to classify; to categorize", "note": ""}, {"ko": "유리하다", "en": "to be advantageous; to be favorable", "note": ""}, {"ko": "위치", "en": "position; place", "note": ""}, {"ko": "뜻하다", "en": "to mean; to signify", "note": ""}, {"ko": "결과", "en": "result; consequence; outcome", "note": ""}, {"ko": "평생", "en": "lifetime; for one''s whole life", "note": ""}, {"ko": "없다", "en": "to not exist; cannot", "note": ""}, {"ko": "하드록", "en": "Hard Rock", "note": ""}, {"ko": "카메라", "en": "camera", "note": ""}, {"ko": "지키다", "en": "to watch, to guard, to monitor", "note": ""}, {"ko": "카드", "en": "card", "note": ""}, {"ko": "보안", "en": "security", "note": ""}, {"ko": "어드밴티지", "en": "advantage", "note": "English loanword"}, {"ko": "플레이어", "en": "player", "note": "English loanword"}, {"ko": "테이블", "en": "table", "note": "English loanword"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~을/를 당하다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "''to suffer N'' (something bad done to you). 출입금지를 당하다 = to be banned.", "ex_ko": "2014년 할리우드 배우 벤 애플렉이 라스베이거스의 한 카지노에서 영구 출입금지를 당했어요.", "ex_en": "In 2014, Hollywood actor Ben Affleck was permanently banned from a casino in Las Vegas."}, {"name": "~에서 (location)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Locative particle marking where an action takes place. 카지노(casino) + 에서.", "ex_ko": "2014년 할리우드 배우 벤 애플렉이 라스베이거스의 한 카지노에서 영구 출입금지를 당했어요.", "ex_en": "In 2014, Hollywood actor Ben Affleck was permanently banned from a casino in Las Vegas."}, {"name": "~던 중에", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Temporal expression marking the exact moment when an action was in progress. 하다(do) → 하던(past progressive) + 중에(during).", "ex_ko": "하드록 호텔 앤 카지노에서 블랙잭을 하던 중에 일어난 일이었어요.", "ex_en": "It happened while he was playing blackjack at the Hard Rock Hotel and Casino."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄴ 일이다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "''it was something that ~''. 일어나다 → 일어난 일이었어요 (it was something that happened).", "ex_ko": "하드록 호텔 앤 카지노에서 블랙잭을 하던 중에 일어난 일이었어요.", "ex_en": "It happened while he was playing blackjack at the Hard Rock Hotel and Casino."}, {"name": "~을/를 통해", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "''through / by means of N''. 감시 카메라를 통해 = through surveillance cameras.", "ex_ko": "카지노 관계자들은 감시 카메라를 통해 애플렉의 게임을 지켜봤어요.", "ex_en": "Casino staff monitored his game through surveillance cameras."}, {"name": "~았/었어요", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Simple past tense. 지켜보다 → 지켜봤어요.", "ex_ko": "카지노 관계자들은 감시 카메라를 통해 애플렉의 게임을 지켜봤어요.", "ex_en": "Casino staff monitored his game through surveillance cameras."}, {"name": "~이라는", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Relative modifier ''called/named''. 기술(technique) + 이라는 (which is called).", "ex_ko": "그는 고액 게임에서 카드 카운팅이라는 기술을 사용하고 있었어요.", "ex_en": "He was using a technique called card counting in high-stakes games."}, {"name": "~고 있었어요", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Past progressive aspect. 사용하다 → 사용하고(connective) + 있었어요 (was doing).", "ex_ko": "그는 고액 게임에서 카드 카운팅이라는 기술을 사용하고 있었어요.", "ex_en": "He was using a technique called card counting in high-stakes games."}, {"name": "~아/어서 (sequential)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Sequential connective linking two actions; the first action precedes the second. 다가가다 → 다가가서.", "ex_ko": "카지노 보안팀은 애플렉에게 다가가서 상황을 설명했어요.", "ex_en": "The casino security team approached him and explained the situation."}, {"name": "~다고 말하다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Reported speech construction. Declarative ending ~다 + 고(quotative) + 말했어요 (said).", "ex_ko": "그들은 그가 ''너무 실력이 좋다''고 말했어요.", "ex_en": "They said that he was ''too skilled.''"}, {"name": "실력이 좋다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "''to be skilled'' (literally ''skill is good'').", "ex_ko": "그들은 그가 ''너무 실력이 좋다''고 말했어요.", "ex_en": "They said that he was ''too skilled.''"}, {"name": "~(으)로 분류하다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "''to classify as N''. After a vowel just add 로: 플레이어 → 플레이어로 분류했어요 (classified as a player).", "ex_ko": "결국 카지노는 애플렉을 ''어드밴티지 플레이어''로 분류했어요.", "ex_en": "Ultimately, the casino classified him as an ''advantage player.''"}, {"name": "~는 (verb modifier)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Present modifier: 있다 → 있는 플레이어 (a player who is (in a position)).", "ex_ko": "이는 게임에서 유리한 위치에 있는 플레이어를 뜻해요.", "ex_en": "This means a player who is in an advantageous position in a game."}, {"name": "~를 뜻하다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Object marker + mean verb. Forms definition/meaning expression.", "ex_ko": "이는 게임에서 유리한 위치에 있는 플레이어를 뜻해요.", "ex_en": "This means a player who is in an advantageous position in a game."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 수 없다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "''cannot''. 하다 → 할 수 없다 (cannot do / cannot play).", "ex_ko": "그 결과 그는 블랙잭 테이블에서 평생 게임을 할 수 없게 되었어요.", "ex_en": "As a result, he became unable to play games at blackjack tables for the rest of his life."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mpaf1dohirwv' and md5(translation) = '095c5a86f95cd11d2a69b94001fec468';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["Recently, a new trend called \"Scientology speedrun\" has been gaining popularity online. This trend is a game where people compete to visit Scientology centers as quickly as possible.", "The trend is also spreading to the Sandy Springs area in Georgia, USA. Young people are sharing these activities on social media.", "Scientology is known as a religious organization. However, this trend is not for religious purposes but rather for fun.", "Experts say this trend is receiving social attention. How it develops in the future is being closely watched."], "sentences": [{"text": "최근 온라인에서 ''사이언톨로지 스피드런''이라는 새로운 트렌드가 인기를 얻고 있어요.", "translation": "Recently, a new trend called ''Scientology speedrun'' is gaining popularity online.", "vocab": [{"ko": "최근", "en": "recently"}, {"ko": "인기를 얻다", "en": "to gain popularity"}, {"ko": "트렌드", "en": "trend"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~이라는", "exp": "Attributive form of 이다 (to be) meaning ''called'' or ''known as''. Connects noun phrase to following noun.", "example_in_sentence": "''사이언톨로지 스피드런''이라는 새로운 트렌드"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "인기를 얻다", "exp": "Collocation meaning ''to gain/win popularity''. Direct object 인기 + verb 얻다.", "example_in_sentence": "인기를 얻고"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있어요", "exp": "Progressive aspect marker. Shows ongoing action. Verb stem + 고 있다 + present ending ~어요.", "example_in_sentence": "얻고 있어요"}]}, {"text": "이 트렌드는 사이언톨로지 센터를 빨리 방문하는 것을 겨루는 게임이에요.", "translation": "This trend is a game where people compete to visit Scientology centers quickly.", "vocab": [{"ko": "방문하다", "en": "to visit"}, {"ko": "겨루다", "en": "to compete"}, {"ko": "게임", "en": "game"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 것을", "exp": "Nominalizes the verb phrase ''방문하는'' (visiting) into an object. Verb + 는 것 + object marker 을.", "example_in_sentence": "방문하는 것을"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 게임", "exp": "Attributive form of verb. Present participle modifying noun 게임. Verb stem + 는 + noun.", "example_in_sentence": "겨루는 게임"}]}, {"text": "미국 조지아 주 샌디 스프링스 지역에도 이 트렌드가 퍼지고 있어요.", "translation": "This trend is also spreading in the Sandy Springs area of Georgia, USA.", "vocab": [{"ko": "퍼지다", "en": "to spread"}, {"ko": "지역", "en": "area/region"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에도", "exp": "Locative particle 에 + focus/additive particle 도. Indicates ''also'' or ''even in'' a location.", "example_in_sentence": "지역에도"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있어요", "exp": "Progressive aspect showing ongoing action. Verb stem + 고 있다 + present ending ~어요.", "example_in_sentence": "퍼지고 있어요"}]}, {"text": "젊은 사람들이 소셜 미디어에서 이런 활동을 공유하고 있어요.", "translation": "Young people are sharing these activities on social media.", "vocab": [{"ko": "젊다", "en": "to be young"}, {"ko": "공유하다", "en": "to share"}, {"ko": "활동", "en": "activity"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (adjective modifier)", "exp": "Turns an adjective into a noun modifier: 젊다 → 젊은 사람들 (young people).", "example_in_sentence": "젊은 사람들"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서", "exp": "Locative particle indicating location of action. Shows where the sharing occurs.", "example_in_sentence": "소셜 미디어에서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있어요", "exp": "Progressive aspect marker showing ongoing action. Verb stem + 고 있다 + present ending ~어요.", "example_in_sentence": "공유하고 있어요"}]}, {"text": "사이언톨로지는 종교 단체로 알려져 있어요.", "translation": "Scientology is known as a religious organization.", "vocab": [{"ko": "종교", "en": "religion"}, {"ko": "단체", "en": "organization/group"}, {"ko": "알려지다", "en": "to be known"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)로 알려져 있다", "exp": "''to be known as N''. 종교 단체로 알려져 있어요 = is known as a religious group.", "example_in_sentence": "단체로 알려져 있어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어져 있다", "exp": "알리다 (to make known) → 알려지다 (to be known) → 알려져 있어요 (is known).", "example_in_sentence": "알려져 있어요"}]}, {"text": "하지만 이번 트렌드는 종교적 목적이 아니라 재미를 위한 것이에요.", "translation": "However, this trend is not for religious purposes but for fun.", "vocab": [{"ko": "하지만", "en": "however/but"}, {"ko": "목적", "en": "purpose"}, {"ko": "재미", "en": "fun"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가 아니라", "exp": "''not A but B''. 종교적 목적이 아니라 재미를 위한 것 = not for religious purposes but for fun.", "example_in_sentence": "목적이 아니라"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~을/를 위한", "exp": "Purpose marker meaning ''for'' or ''in order for''. Noun + 을/를 위하다 in attributive form.", "example_in_sentence": "재미를 위한"}]}, {"text": "전문가들은 이런 트렌드가 사회적 관심을 받고 있다고 말해요.", "translation": "Experts say that this kind of trend is receiving social attention.", "vocab": [{"ko": "전문가", "en": "expert"}, {"ko": "관심", "en": "attention/interest"}, {"ko": "받다", "en": "to receive"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~다고 말하다", "exp": "Quoted speech form. Clause + 다고 + verb 말하다. Introduces indirect speech or reported statement.", "example_in_sentence": "받고 있다고 말해요"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "관심을 받다", "exp": "Collocation meaning ''to receive attention/interest''. Direct object 관심 + verb 받다.", "example_in_sentence": "관심을 받고"}]}, {"text": "앞으로 어떻게 발전할지 주목되고 있어요.", "translation": "People are watching to see how it will develop.", "vocab": [{"ko": "앞으로", "en": "in the future/ahead"}, {"ko": "발전하다", "en": "to develop"}, {"ko": "주목되다", "en": "to draw attention"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ지", "exp": "''whether / how ... will''. 발전하다 → 어떻게 발전할지 (how it will develop).", "example_in_sentence": "발전할지"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~되다 (passive)", "exp": "주목하다 (to pay attention) → 주목되다 (to draw attention) → 주목되고 있어요 (is drawing attention).", "example_in_sentence": "주목되고"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있어요", "exp": "Progressive aspect indicating ongoing state. Verb stem + 고 있다 + present ending ~어요.", "example_in_sentence": "주목되고 있어요"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "최근", "en": "recently", "note": ""}, {"ko":