''사이언톨로지 스피드런''이라는 새로운 트렌드가 인기를 얻고 있어요.", "ex_en": "Recently, a new trend called ''Scientology speedrun'' is gaining popularity online."}, {"name": "~고 있어요", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Progressive aspect marker showing ongoing action. Verb stem + 고 있다 + present ending ~어요.", "ex_ko": "최근 온라인에서 ''사이언톨로지 스피드런''이라는 새로운 트렌드가 인기를 얻고 있어요.", "ex_en": "Recently, a new trend called ''Scientology speedrun'' is gaining popularity online."}, {"name": "~는 것을", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Nominalizes the verb phrase ''방문하는'' (visiting) into an object. Verb + 는 것 + object marker 을.", "ex_ko": "이 트렌드는 사이언톨로지 센터를 빨리 방문하는 것을 겨루는 게임이에요.", "ex_en": "This trend is a game where people compete to visit Scientology centers quickly."}, {"name": "~는 게임", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Attributive form of verb. Present participle modifying noun 게임. Verb stem + 는 + noun.", "ex_ko": "이 트렌드는 사이언톨로지 센터를 빨리 방문하는 것을 겨루는 게임이에요.", "ex_en": "This trend is a game where people compete to visit Scientology centers quickly."}, {"name": "~에도", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Locative particle 에 + focus/additive particle 도. Indicates ''also'' or ''even in'' a location.", "ex_ko": "미국 조지아 주 샌디 스프링스 지역에도 이 트렌드가 퍼지고 있어요.", "ex_en": "This trend is also spreading in the Sandy Springs area of Georgia, USA."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄴ (adjective modifier)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Turns an adjective into a noun modifier: 젊다 → 젊은 사람들 (young people).", "ex_ko": "젊은 사람들이 소셜 미디어에서 이런 활동을 공유하고 있어요.", "ex_en": "Young people are sharing these activities on social media."}, {"name": "~에서", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Locative particle indicating location of action. Shows where the sharing occurs.", "ex_ko": "젊은 사람들이 소셜 미디어에서 이런 활동을 공유하고 있어요.", "ex_en": "Young people are sharing these activities on social media."}, {"name": "~(으)로 알려져 있다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "''to be known as N''. 종교 단체로 알려져 있어요 = is known as a religious group.", "ex_ko": "사이언톨로지는 종교 단체로 알려져 있어요.", "ex_en": "Scientology is known as a religious organization."}, {"name": "~아/어져 있다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "알리다 (to make known) → 알려지다 (to be known) → 알려져 있어요 (is known).", "ex_ko": "사이언톨로지는 종교 단체로 알려져 있어요.", "ex_en": "Scientology is known as a religious organization."}, {"name": "~이/가 아니라", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "''not A but B''. 종교적 목적이 아니라 재미를 위한 것 = not for religious purposes but for fun.", "ex_ko": "하지만 이번 트렌드는 종교적 목적이 아니라 재미를 위한 것이에요.", "ex_en": "However, this trend is not for religious purposes but for fun."}, {"name": "~다고 말하다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Quoted speech form. Clause + 다고 + verb 말하다. Introduces indirect speech or reported statement.", "ex_ko": "전문가들은 이런 트렌드가 사회적 관심을 받고 있다고 말해요.", "ex_en": "Experts say that this kind of trend is receiving social attention."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ지", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "''whether / how ... will''. 발전하다 → 어떻게 발전할지 (how it will develop).", "ex_ko": "앞으로 어떻게 발전할지 주목되고 있어요.", "ex_en": "People are watching to see how it will develop."}, {"name": "~되다 (passive)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "주목하다 (to pay attention) → 주목되다 (to draw attention) → 주목되고 있어요 (is drawing attention).", "ex_ko": "앞으로 어떻게 발전할지 주목되고 있어요.", "ex_en": "People are watching to see how it will develop."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mpaf2pw7gies' and md5(translation) = '630153516f83e013066cc01a35cac9c8';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["Google''s annual developer conference began on Tuesday. This conference is called Google I/O 2026.", "Gemini Intelligence will be covered as a major topic at the conference. Android XR and more AI technologies are also expected to be announced.", "Participants can receive updates directly from the event venue. New technology announcements will continue.", "This developer conference is an important event showcasing Google''s latest technologies. Many developers are showing interest."], "sentences": [{"text": "구글의 연례 개발자 회의가 화요일에 시작되었습니다.", "translation": "Google''s annual developer conference began on Tuesday.", "vocab": [{"ko": "연례", "en": "annual", "note": "yearly, happening every year"}, {"ko": "개발자", "en": "developer", "note": "person who creates software"}, {"ko": "회의", "en": "conference, meeting", "note": "formal gathering for discussion"}, {"ko": "시작되다", "en": "to begin, to start", "note": "passive form of 시작하다"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었/였습니다 (past formal)", "exp": "formal past tense ending. 시작되다 → 시작되었습니다 (began)", "example_in_sentence": "시작되었습니다"}]}, {"text": "이번 회의는 구글 I/O 2026으로 불립니다.", "translation": "This conference is called Google I/O 2026.", "vocab": [{"ko": "이번", "en": "this time", "note": "this occasion, current"}, {"ko": "불리다", "en": "to be called", "note": "passive form of 부르다 (to call)"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)로 불리다", "exp": "''to be called N''. 구글 I/O 2026으로 불립니다 = is called Google I/O 2026.", "example_in_sentence": "2026으로 불립니다"}]}, {"text": "회의에서는 제미니 인텔리전스가 주요 주제로 다뤄질 예정입니다.", "translation": "Gemini Intelligence will be covered as a major topic at the conference.", "vocab": [{"ko": "주요", "en": "major, main", "note": "important, primary"}, {"ko": "주제", "en": "topic, subject", "note": "theme of discussion"}, {"ko": "다뤄지다", "en": "to be dealt with, to be covered", "note": "passive form of 다루다"}, {"ko": "예정", "en": "schedule, plan", "note": "something planned or expected"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서", "exp": "location particle indicating where an action takes place. 회의에서 (at the conference)", "example_in_sentence": "회의에서는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)로", "exp": "particle indicating role or capacity. 주제로 (as a topic)", "example_in_sentence": "주제로"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 예정이다", "exp": "is scheduled/planned to. 다뤄지다 → 다뤄질 예정이다 (is scheduled to be covered)", "example_in_sentence": "다뤄질 예정입니다"}]}, {"text": "안드로이드 XR과 더 많은 AI 기술도 발표될 것으로 예상됩니다.", "translation": "Android XR and more AI technologies are also expected to be announced.", "vocab": [{"ko": "기술", "en": "technology", "note": "technical knowledge or methods"}, {"ko": "발표되다", "en": "to be announced", "note": "passive form of 발표하다"}, {"ko": "예상되다", "en": "to be expected", "note": "passive form of 예상하다"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~과/와", "exp": "particle meaning ''and'' or ''with''. 안드로이드 XR과 (Android XR and)", "example_in_sentence": "안드로이드 XR과"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~도", "exp": "particle meaning ''also, too''. AI 기술도 (AI technology too)", "example_in_sentence": "기술도"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 것으로 예상되다", "exp": "is expected to. 발표되다 → 발표될 것으로 예상되다 (is expected to be announced)", "example_in_sentence": "발표될 것으로 예상됩니다"}]}, {"text": "참가자들은 행사 현장에서 직접 업데이트를 받을 수 있습니다.", "translation": "Participants can get updates in person at the event venue.", "vocab": [{"ko": "참가자", "en": "participant", "note": "person who takes part in an event"}, {"ko": "행사", "en": "event", "note": "organized activity or ceremony"}, {"ko": "현장", "en": "venue, site", "note": "actual location where something happens"}, {"ko": "직접", "en": "directly", "note": "in person, without intermediary"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다", "exp": "can, be able to. 받다 → 받을 수 있습니다 (can receive)", "example_in_sentence": "받을 수 있습니다"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서 (location/source)", "exp": "at/in (location of action) or from (source)", "example_in_sentence": "현장에서"}]}, {"text": "새로운 기술 발표가 계속 이어질 예정입니다.", "translation": "New technology announcements will continue.", "vocab": [{"ko": "새롭다", "en": "to be new", "note": "fresh, recent"}, {"ko": "발표", "en": "announcement", "note": "official statement or presentation"}, {"ko": "계속", "en": "continuously", "note": "without stopping"}, {"ko": "이어지다", "en": "to continue, to follow", "note": "to be connected in sequence"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "ㅂ irregular + ~(으)ㄴ modifier", "exp": "새롭다 (to be new): ㅂ becomes 우 before -은 → 새로운 기술 (new technology).", "example_in_sentence": "새로운"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 예정이다", "exp": "is scheduled/planned to. 이어지다 → 이어질 예정이다 (is planned to continue)", "example_in_sentence": "이어질 예정입니다"}]}, {"text": "이번 개발자 회의는 구글의 최신 기술을 선보이는 중요한 행사입니다.", "translation": "This developer conference is an important event showcasing Google''s latest technologies.", "vocab": [{"ko": "최신", "en": "latest, newest", "note": "most recent or up-to-date"}, {"ko": "선보이다", "en": "to showcase, to present", "note": "to display or introduce something new"}, {"ko": "중요하다", "en": "to be important", "note": "significant, crucial"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는", "exp": "present tense verb modifier. 선보이다 → 선보이는 (showcasing)", "example_in_sentence": "선보이는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄴ/은", "exp": "adjective modifier. 중요하다 → 중요한 (important)", "example_in_sentence": "중요한"}]}, {"text": "많은 개발자들이 관심을 보이고 있습니다.", "translation": "Many developers are showing interest.", "vocab": [{"ko": "많다", "en": "to be many, much", "note": "large in quantity or number"}, {"ko": "관심", "en": "interest", "note": "attention or curiosity about something"}, {"ko": "보이다", "en": "to show, to display", "note": "to demonstrate or exhibit"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄴ/은", "exp": "adjective modifier. 많다 → 많은 (many)", "example_in_sentence": "많은"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있다", "exp": "continuous present tense. 보이다 → 보이고 있다 (are showing)", "example_in_sentence": "보이고 있습니다"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "관심을 보이다", "exp": "idiomatic expression meaning ''to show interest''. 관심 (interest) + 을/를 + 보이다 (to show)", "example_in_sentence": "관심을 보이고"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "연례", "en": "annual", "note": "yearly, happening every year"}, {"ko": "개발자", "en": "developer", "note": "person who creates software"}, {"ko": "회의", "en": "conference, meeting", "note": "formal gathering for discussion"}, {"ko": "시작되다", "en": "to begin, to start", "note": "passive form of 시작하다"}, {"ko": "이번", "en": "this time", "note": "this occasion, current"}, {"ko": "불리다", "en": "to be called", "note": "passive form of 부르다 (to call)"}, {"ko": "주요", "en": "major, main", "note": "important, primary"}, {"ko": "주제", "en": "topic, subject", "note": "theme of discussion"}, {"ko": "다뤄지다", "en": "to be dealt with, to be covered", "note": "passive form of 다루다"}, {"ko": "예정", "en": "schedule, plan", "note": "something planned or expected"}, {"ko": "기술", "en": "technology", "note": "technical knowledge or methods"}, {"ko": "발표되다", "en": "to be announced", "note": "passive form of 발표하다"}, {"ko": "예상되다", "en": "to be expected", "note": "passive form of 예상하다"}, {"ko": "참가자", "en": "participant", "note": "person who takes part in an event"}, {"ko": "행사", "en": "event", "note": "organized activity or ceremony"}, {"ko": "현장", "en": "venue, site", "note": "actual location where something happens"}, {"ko": "직접", "en": "directly", "note": "in person, without intermediary"}, {"ko": "새롭다", "en": "to be new", "note": "fresh, recent"}, {"ko": "발표", "en": "announcement", "note": "official statement or presentation"}, {"ko": "계속", "en": "continuously", "note": "without stopping"}, {"ko": "이어지다", "en": "to continue, to follow", "note": "to be connected in sequence"}, {"ko": "최신", "en": "latest, newest", "note": "most recent or up-to-date"}, {"ko": "선보이다", "en": "to showcase, to present", "note": "to display or introduce something new"}, {"ko": "중요하다", "en": "to be important", "note": "significant, crucial"}, {"ko": "많다", "en": "to be many, much", "note": "large in quantity or number"}, {"ko": "관심", "en": "interest", "note": "attention or curiosity about something"}, {"ko": "보이다", "en": "to show, to display", "note": "to demonstrate or exhibit"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~았/었/였습니다 (past formal)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "formal past tense ending. 시작되다 → 시작되었습니다 (began)", "ex_ko": "구글의 연례 개발자 회의가 화요일에 시작되었습니다.", "ex_en": "Google''s annual developer conference began on Tuesday."}, {"name": "~(으)로 불리다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "''to be called N''. 구글 I/O 2026으로 불립니다 = is called Google I/O 2026.", "ex_ko": "이번 회의는 구글 I/O 2026으로 불립니다.", "ex_en": "This conference is called Google I/O 2026."}, {"name": "~에서 (location/source)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "location particle indicating where an action takes place. 회의에서 (at the conference)", "ex_ko": "회의에서는 제미니 인텔리전스가 주요 주제로 다뤄질 예정입니다.", "ex_en": "Gemini Intelligence will be covered as a major topic at the conference."}, {"name": "~(으)로", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "particle indicating role or capacity. 주제로 (as a topic)", "ex_ko": "회의에서는 제미니 인텔리전스가 주요 주제로 다뤄질 예정입니다.", "ex_en": "Gemini Intelligence will be covered as a major topic at the conference."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 예정이다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "is scheduled/planned to. 다뤄지다 → 다뤄질 예정이다 (is scheduled to be covered)", "ex_ko": "회의에서는 제미니 인텔리전스가 주요 주제로 다뤄질 예정입니다.", "ex_en": "Gemini Intelligence will be covered as a major topic at the conference."}, {"name": "~과/와", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "particle meaning ''and'' or ''with''. 안드로이드 XR과 (Android XR and)", "ex_ko": "안드로이드 XR과 더 많은 AI 기술도 발표될 것으로 예상됩니다.", "ex_en": "Android XR and more AI technologies are also expected to be announced."}, {"name": "~도", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "particle meaning ''also, too''. AI 기술도 (AI technology too)", "ex_ko": "안드로이드 XR과 더 많은 AI 기술도 발표될 것으로 예상됩니다.", "ex_en": "Android XR and more AI technologies are also expected to be announced."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 것으로 예상되다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "is expected to. 발표되다 → 발표될 것으로 예상되다 (is expected to be announced)", "ex_ko": "안드로이드 XR과 더 많은 AI 기술도 발표될 것으로 예상됩니다.", "ex_en": "Android XR and more AI technologies are also expected to be announced."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "can, be able to. 받다 → 받을 수 있습니다 (can receive)", "ex_ko": "참가자들은 행사 현장에서 직접 업데이트를 받을 수 있습니다.", "ex_en": "Participants can get updates in person at the event venue."}, {"name": "ㅂ irregular + ~(으)ㄴ modifier", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "새롭다 (to be new): ㅂ becomes 우 before -은 → 새로운 기술 (new technology).", "ex_ko": "새로운 기술 발표가 계속 이어질 예정입니다.", "ex_en": "New technology announcements will continue."}, {"name": "~는", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "present tense verb modifier. 선보이다 → 선보이는 (showcasing)", "ex_ko": "이번 개발자 회의는 구글의 최신 기술을 선보이는 중요한 행사입니다.", "ex_en": "This developer conference is an important event showcasing Google''s latest technologies."}, {"name": "~ㄴ/은", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "adjective modifier. 중요하다 → 중요한 (important)", "ex_ko": "이번 개발자 회의는 구글의 최신 기술을 선보이는 중요한 행사입니다.", "ex_en": "This developer conference is an important event showcasing Google''s latest technologies."}, {"name": "~고 있다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "continuous present tense. 보이다 → 보이고 있다 (are showing)", "ex_ko": "많은 개발자들이 관심을 보이고 있습니다.", "ex_en": "Many developers are showing interest."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mpbuhhnyspdl' and md5(translation) = 'd306414aa18d3347b5542a57a0c26b5b';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["Unit 684 was South Korea''s secret black operations unit. Initially, this unit had 31 members.", "Seven members died during training. This was because the training was extremely harsh and dangerous.", "The remaining 24 members staged a mutiny. They killed their guards and hijacked a bus. They tried to go to Seoul.", "The military stopped them. Twenty people died in the shootout. The remaining members were executed."], "sentences": [{"text": "684부대는 한국의 비밀 작전 부대였어요.", "translation": "Unit 684 was a secret South Korean military operations unit.", "vocab": [{"ko": "부대", "en": "unit, troops", "note": "military unit"}, {"ko": "비밀", "en": "secret", "note": "classified information"}, {"ko": "작전", "en": "operation", "note": "military operation"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~였어요 (past of 이다)", "exp": "Past polite form of 이다 (to be). After a vowel, 이었어요 shortens to 였어요: 부대 + 였어요 = was a unit.", "example_in_sentence": "부대였어요"}]}, {"text": "이 부대에는 처음에 31명의 대원이 있었어요.", "translation": "Initially, this unit had 31 members.", "vocab": [{"ko": "처음", "en": "beginning, first", "note": "initially"}, {"ko": "대원", "en": "member", "note": "member of a group or organization"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에는", "exp": "Location marker 에 + topic marker 는. Shows location with emphasis or contrast.", "example_in_sentence": "부대에는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요 (past polite)", "exp": "Past tense polite ending. 있다 (to exist) → 있었다 → 있었어요 (existed/had).", "example_in_sentence": "있었어요"}]}, {"text": "훈련 과정에서 7명의 대원이 죽었어요.", "translation": "Seven members died during training.", "vocab": [{"ko": "훈련", "en": "training", "note": "military or physical training"}, {"ko": "과정", "en": "process, course", "note": "course of events"}, {"ko": "죽다", "en": "to die", "note": "to pass away"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서", "exp": "Location/context marker. Shows where action takes place. 과정에서 (during the process).", "example_in_sentence": "과정에서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요 (past polite)", "exp": "Past tense polite ending. 죽다 (to die) → 죽었다 → 죽었어요 (died).", "example_in_sentence": "죽었어요"}]}, {"text": "훈련이 매우 힘들고 위험했기 때문이에요.", "translation": "This was because the training was extremely harsh and dangerous.", "vocab": [{"ko": "매우", "en": "very, extremely", "note": "intensifier"}, {"ko": "힘들다", "en": "to be difficult, hard", "note": "physically or mentally challenging"}, {"ko": "위험하다", "en": "to be dangerous", "note": "risky, hazardous"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고", "exp": "Connective ending meaning ''and''. Connects two adjectives or verbs. 힘들다 + 위험하다.", "example_in_sentence": "힘들고"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~기 때문이에요", "exp": "Gives the reason at the end of a sentence: ''it is because ~''. 위험하다 → 위험했기 때문이에요 (it was because it was dangerous).", "example_in_sentence": "위험했기 때문이에요"}]}, {"text": "남은 24명의 대원들이 반란을 일으켰어요.", "translation": "The remaining 24 members staged a mutiny.", "vocab": [{"ko": "남다", "en": "to remain, be left", "note": "to be remaining"}, {"ko": "반란", "en": "rebellion, mutiny", "note": "revolt against authority"}, {"ko": "일으키다", "en": "to cause, start", "note": "to raise up, initiate"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄴ/은", "exp": "Past verb modifier or present adjective modifier. 남다 (remain) → 남은 (remaining).", "example_in_sentence": "남은"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요 (past polite)", "exp": "Past tense polite ending. 일으키다 (to cause) → 일으켰다 → 일으켰어요 (caused/started).", "example_in_sentence": "일으켰어요"}]}, {"text": "그들은 경비병들을 죽이고 버스를 탈취했어요.", "translation": "They killed their guards and hijacked a bus.", "vocab": [{"ko": "경비병", "en": "guard", "note": "security guard, sentry"}, {"ko": "탈취하다", "en": "to hijack, seize", "note": "to take by force"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고", "exp": "Connective ending meaning ''and''. Connects sequential actions. 죽이고 + 탈취했어요.", "example_in_sentence": "죽이고"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요 (past polite)", "exp": "Past tense polite ending. 탈취하다 (to hijack) → 탈취했다 → 탈취했어요 (hijacked).", "example_in_sentence": "탈취했어요"}]}, {"text": "서울로 가려고 했어요.", "translation": "They tried to go to Seoul.", "vocab": [{"ko": "서울", "en": "Seoul", "note": "capital city of South Korea"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)로", "exp": "Direction marker indicating destination or means. 서울로 (to Seoul).", "example_in_sentence": "서울로"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)려고 하다", "exp": "Shows an intention or attempt: ''try / plan to''. 가다 → 가려고 했어요 (tried to go).", "example_in_sentence": "가려고 했어요"}]}, {"text": "군대가 이들을 막았어요.", "translation": "The military stopped them.", "vocab": [{"ko": "군대", "en": "military, army", "note": "armed forces"}, {"ko": "막다", "en": "to block, stop", "note": "to prevent, obstruct"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요 (past polite)", "exp": "Past tense polite ending. 막다 (to stop) → 막았다 → 막았어요 (stopped).", "example_in_sentence": "막았어요"}]}, {"text": "총격전에서 20명이 죽었어요.", "translation": "Twenty people died in the shootout.", "vocab": [{"ko": "총격전", "en": "shootout, gunfight", "note": "armed battle with guns"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서", "exp": "Location/context marker. Shows where action takes place. 총격전에서 (in the shootout).", "example_in_sentence": "총격전에서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요 (past polite)", "exp": "Past tense polite ending. 죽다 (to die) → 죽었다 → 죽었어요 (died).", "example_in_sentence": "죽었어요"}]}, {"text": "나머지 대원들은 처형되었어요.", "translation": "The remaining members were executed.", "vocab": [{"ko": "나머지", "en": "the rest, remainder", "note": "what is left over"}, {"ko": "처형되다", "en": "to be executed", "note": "to be put to death as punishment"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~되다", "exp": "Passive marker. 처형하다 (execute) → 처형되다 (be executed).", "example_in_sentence": "처형되었어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요 (past polite)", "exp": "Past tense polite ending. 처형되다 (be executed) → 처형되었다 → 처형되었어요 (were executed).", "example_in_sentence": "처형되었어요"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "부대", "en": "unit, troops", "note": "military unit"}, {"ko": "비밀", "en": "secret", "note": "classified information"}, {"ko": "작전", "en": "operation", "note": "military operation"}, {"ko": "처음", "en": "beginning, first", "note": "initially"}, {"ko": "대원", "en": "member", "note": "member of a group or organization"}, {"ko": "훈련", "en": "training", "note": "military or physical training"}, {"ko": "과정", "en": "process, course", "note": "course of events"}, {"ko": "죽다", "en": "to die", "note": "to pass away"}, {"ko": "매우", "en": "very, extremely", "note": "intensifier"}, {"ko": "힘들다", "en": "to be difficult, hard", "note": "physically or mentally challenging"}, {"ko": "위험하다", "en": "to be dangerous", "note": "risky, hazardous"}, {"ko": "남다", "en": "to remain, be left", "note": "to be remaining"}, {"ko": "반란", "en": "rebellion, mutiny", "note": "revolt against authority"}, {"ko": "일으키다", "en": "to cause, start", "note": "to raise up, initiate"}, {"ko": "경비병", "en": "guard", "note": "security guard, sentry"}, {"ko": "탈취하다", "en": "to hijack, seize", "note": "to take by force"}, {"ko": "서울", "en": "Seoul", "note": "capital city of South Korea"}, {"ko": "군대", "en": "military, army", "note": "armed forces"}, {"ko": "막다", "en": "to block, stop", "note": "to prevent, obstruct"}, {"ko": "총격전", "en": "shootout, gunfight", "note": "armed battle with guns"}, {"ko": "나머지", "en": "the rest, remainder", "note": "what is left over"}, {"ko": "처형되다", "en": "to be executed", "note": "to be put to death as punishment"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~였어요 (past of 이다)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Past polite form of 이다 (to be). After a vowel, 이었어요 shortens to 였어요: 부대 + 였어요 = was a unit.", "ex_ko": "684부대는 한국의 비밀 작전 부대였어요.", "ex_en": "Unit 684 was a secret South Korean military operations unit."}, {"name": "~에는", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Location marker 에 + topic marker 는. Shows location with emphasis or contrast.", "ex_ko": "이 부대에는 처음에 31명의 대원이 있었어요.", "ex_en": "Initially, this unit had 31 members."}, {"name": "~았/었어요 (past polite)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Past tense polite ending. 처형되다 (be executed) → 처형되었다 → 처형되었어요 (were executed).", "ex_ko": "이 부대에는 처음에 31명의 대원이 있었어요.", "ex_en": "Initially, this unit had 31 members."}, {"name": "~에서", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Location/context marker. Shows where action takes place. 과정에서 (during the process).", "ex_ko": "훈련 과정에서 7명의 대원이 죽었어요.", "ex_en": "Seven members died during training."}, {"name": "~고", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Connective ending meaning ''and''. Connects two adjectives or verbs. 힘들다 + 위험하다.", "ex_ko": "훈련이 매우 힘들고 위험했기 때문이에요.", "ex_en": "This was because the training was extremely harsh and dangerous."}, {"name": "~기 때문이에요", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Gives the reason at the end of a sentence: ''it is because ~''. 위험하다 → 위험했기 때문이에요 (it was because it was dangerous).", "ex_ko": "훈련이 매우 힘들고 위험했기 때문이에요.", "ex_en": "This was because the training was extremely harsh and dangerous."}, {"name": "~ㄴ/은", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Past verb modifier or present adjective modifier. 남다 (remain) → 남은 (remaining).", "ex_ko": "남은 24명의 대원들이 반란을 일으켰어요.", "ex_en": "The remaining 24 members staged a mutiny."}, {"name": "~(으)로", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Direction marker indicating destination or means. 서울로 (to Seoul).", "ex_ko": "서울로 가려고 했어요.", "ex_en": "They tried to go to Seoul."}, {"name": "~(으)려고 하다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Shows an intention or attempt: ''try / plan to''. 가다 → 가려고 했어요 (tried to go).", "ex_ko": "서울로 가려고 했어요.", "ex_en": "They tried to go to Seoul."}, {"name": "~되다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Passive marker. 처형하다 (execute) → 처형되다 (be executed).", "ex_ko": "나머지 대원들은 처형되었어요.", "ex_en": "The remaining members were executed."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mpbuii7abzls' and md5(translation) = '8abf2457b289347ab5ba7cb5c53864e2';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["In 1743, something interesting happened in France. At that time, male surgeons wanted to work as midwives. The doctors tried not to provide education to female midwives.", "There was a woman named Angélique du Coudray. She became angry when she saw this situation. So she started a campaign to stop the doctors.", "The French king gave Angélique a special task. The king told her to teach midwifery throughout the entire country. This was a very important job.", "Angélique taught countless students. She worked hard for midwife education. Thanks to her efforts, many women were able to become midwives."], "sentences": [{"text": "1743년에 프랑스에서 흥미로운 일이 있었어요.", "translation": "In 1743, something interesting happened in France.", "vocab": [{"ko": "흥미롭다", "en": "to be interesting", "note": "흥미(interest) + -롭다(suffix forming adjectives)"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서", "exp": "location marker. indicates where an action takes place. 프랑스에서 (in France)", "example_in_sentence": "프랑스에서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었/였어요 (past polite)", "exp": "past tense polite form. 있다 + 었어요 = 있었어요 (there was/were)", "example_in_sentence": "있었어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~롭다", "exp": "adjective suffix meaning ''having the quality of''. 흥미(interest) + 롭다 → 흥미롭다 (interesting)", "example_in_sentence": "흥미로운"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에 (location/time)", "exp": "static location / time / direction", "example_in_sentence": "년에"}]}, {"text": "그때 남자 의사들이 조산사 일을 하고 싶어했어요.", "translation": "At that time, male doctors wanted to do the work of midwives.", "vocab": [{"ko": "의사", "en": "doctor", "note": "medical doctor"}, {"ko": "조산사", "en": "midwife", "note": "person who assists in childbirth"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가", "exp": "subject marker. marks the grammatical subject of the sentence. 의사들이 (the doctors)", "example_in_sentence": "의사들이"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를", "exp": "object marker. marks the direct object. 일을 (work/job)", "example_in_sentence": "일을"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 싶어하다", "exp": "Says what someone else wants to do (used for third persons). 하다 → 하고 싶어했어요 (they wanted to do).", "example_in_sentence": "하고 싶어했어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었/였어요 (past polite)", "exp": "Past polite ending. 싶어하다 → 싶어했어요 (wanted).", "example_in_sentence": "싶어했어요"}]}, {"text": "의사들은 여자 조산사들에게 교육을 주지 않으려고 했어요.", "translation": "The doctors tried not to provide education to female midwives.", "vocab": [{"ko": "여자", "en": "woman", "note": "female person"}, {"ko": "교육", "en": "education", "note": "teaching and training"}, {"ko": "주다", "en": "to give", "note": "basic verb for giving"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는", "exp": "topic marker. indicates what the sentence is about. 의사들은 (as for the doctors)", "example_in_sentence": "의사들은"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에게", "exp": "dative marker for people. indicates the recipient of an action. 조산사들에게 (to the midwives)", "example_in_sentence": "조산사들에게"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~지 않다", "exp": "negation. verb stem + 지 않다 = negative form. 주다 → 주지 않다 (not give)", "example_in_sentence": "주지 않으려고"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)려고 하다", "exp": "Shows an intention or attempt: ''try to''. 않다 → 않으려고 했어요 (tried not to).", "example_in_sentence": "않으려고 했어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었/였어요 (past polite)", "exp": "past tense polite form. 하다 + 었어요 = 했어요 (did/tried)", "example_in_sentence": "했어요"}]}, {"text": "앙젤리크 뒤 쿠드레라는 여자가 있었어요.", "translation": "There was a woman named Angélique du Coudray.", "vocab": [{"ko": "여자", "en": "woman", "note": "female person"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(이)라는", "exp": "called/named. indicates someone''s name or what something is called. 뒤 쿠드레라는 (named du Coudray)", "example_in_sentence": "뒤 쿠드레라는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가", "exp": "subject marker. marks the grammatical subject. 여자가 (a woman)", "example_in_sentence": "여자가"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었/였어요 (past polite)", "exp": "past tense polite form. 있다 + 었어요 = 있었어요 (there was/existed)", "example_in_sentence": "있었어요"}]}, {"text": "그녀는 이 상황을 보고 화가 났어요.", "translation": "She became angry when she saw this situation.", "vocab": [{"ko": "그녀", "en": "she", "note": "third person feminine pronoun"}, {"ko": "상황", "en": "situation", "note": "circumstances or condition"}, {"ko": "보다", "en": "to see", "note": "basic verb for seeing"}, {"ko": "화", "en": "anger", "note": "feeling of anger or rage"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는", "exp": "topic marker. indicates what the sentence is about. 그녀는 (as for her)", "example_in_sentence": "그녀는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를", "exp": "object marker. marks the direct object. 상황을 (the situation)", "example_in_sentence": "상황을"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고", "exp": "connective ending. connects two actions in sequence. 보고 (seeing and)", "example_in_sentence": "보고"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었/였어요 (past polite)", "exp": "past tense polite form. 나다 + 았어요 = 났어요 (arose/came out)", "example_in_sentence": "났어요"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "화가 나다", "exp": "idiomatic expression meaning ''to get angry''. literally ''anger comes out''", "example_in_sentence": "화가 났어요"}]}, {"text": "그래서 의사들을 막으려고 캠페인을 시작했어요.", "translation": "So she started a campaign to stop the doctors.", "vocab": [{"ko": "그래서", "en": "so, therefore", "note": "conjunctive adverb showing result"}, {"ko": "막다", "en": "to block, to stop", "note": "prevent something from happening"}, {"ko": "캠페인", "en": "campaign", "note": "organized effort for a cause"}, {"ko": "시작하다", "en": "to start", "note": "begin something"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를", "exp": "object marker. marks the direct object. 의사들을 (the doctors), 캠페인을 (the campaign)", "example_in_sentence": "의사들을"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)려고", "exp": "intention. expresses purpose or attempt. 막으려고 (in order to stop)", "example_in_sentence": "막으려고"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었/였어요 (past polite)", "exp": "Past polite ending. 시작하다 → 시작했어요 (started).", "example_in_sentence": "시작했어요"}]}, {"text": "프랑스 왕이 앙젤리크에게 특별한 일을 맡겼어요.", "translation": "The French king gave Angélique a special task.", "vocab": [{"ko": "왕", "en": "king", "note": "monarch or ruler"}, {"ko": "특별하다", "en": "to be special", "note": "different from ordinary"}, {"ko": "맡기다", "en": "to entrust", "note": "give responsibility to someone"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가", "exp": "subject marker. marks the grammatical subject. 왕이 (the king)", "example_in_sentence": "왕이"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에게", "exp": "dative marker for people. indicates the recipient. 앙젤리크에게 (to Angélique)", "example_in_sentence": "앙젤리크에게"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄴ/은", "exp": "adnominal ending for past/completed action or present state of adjectives. 특별하다 → 특별한 (special)", "example_in_sentence": "특별한"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를", "exp": "object marker. marks the direct object. 일을 (work/task)", "example_in_sentence": "일을"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었/였어요 (past polite)", "exp": "past tense polite form. 맡기다 + 었어요 = 맡겼어요 (entrusted)", "example_in_sentence": "맡겼어요"}]}, {"text": "왕은 그녀에게 나라 전체에서 조산사를 가르치라고 했어요.", "translation": "The king told her to teach midwives throughout the whole country.", "vocab": [{"ko": "나라", "en": "country", "note": "nation or state"}, {"ko": "전체", "en": "whole, entire", "note": "all parts together"}, {"ko": "가르치다", "en": "to teach", "note": "provide instruction or education"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는", "exp": "topic marker. indicates what the sentence is about. 왕은 (as for the king)", "example_in_sentence": "왕은"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에게", "exp": "dative marker for people. indicates the recipient. 그녀에게 (to her)", "example_in_sentence": "그녀에게"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서", "exp": "location marker. indicates where an action takes place. 전체에서 (throughout)", "example_in_sentence": "전체에서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를", "exp": "Object marker. Marks the direct object. 조산사를 (midwives).", "example_in_sentence": "조산사를"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)라고 하다", "exp": "indirect imperative. reports someone''s command or instruction. 가르치라고 (told to teach)", "example_in_sentence": "가르치라고"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었/였어요 (past polite)", "exp": "past tense polite form. 하다 + 었어요 = 했어요 (said/told)", "example_in_sentence": "했어요"}]}, {"text": "이것은 매우 중요한 일이었어요.", "translation": "This was a very important job.", "vocab": [{"ko": "이것", "en": "this", "note": "demonstrative pronoun for nearby object"}, {"ko": "매우", "en": "very", "note": "adverb intensifying degree"}, {"ko": "중요하다", "en": "to be important", "note": "having great significance"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는", "exp": "topic marker. indicates what the sentence is about. 이것은 (as for this)", "example_in_sentence": "이것은"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄴ/은", "exp": "adnominal ending for present state of adjectives. 중요하다 → 중요한 (important)", "example_in_sentence": "중요한"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었/였어요 (past polite)", "exp": "past tense polite form. 이다 + 었어요 = 이었어요 (was)", "example_in_sentence": "이었어요"}]}, {"text": "앙젤리크는 수많은 학생들을 가르쳤어요.", "translation": "Angélique taught countless students.", "vocab": [{"ko": "수많다", "en": "to be countless", "note": "extremely many in number"}, {"ko": "학생", "en": "student", "note": "person who studies"}, {"ko": "가르치다", "en": "to teach", "note": "provide instruction or education"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는", "exp": "topic marker. indicates what the sentence is about. 앙젤리크는 (as for Angélique)", "example_in_sentence": "앙젤리크는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄴ/은", "exp": "adnominal ending for present state of adjectives. 수많다 → 수많은 (countless)", "example_in_sentence": "수많은"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를", "exp": "object marker. marks the direct object. 학생들을 (the students)", "example_in_sentence": "학생들을"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었/였어요 (past polite)", "exp": "past tense polite form. 가르치다 + 었어요 = 가르쳤어요 (taught)", "example_in_sentence": "가르쳤어요"}]}, {"text": "그녀는 조산사 교육을 위해 열심히 일했어요.", "translation": "She worked hard for midwife education.", "vocab": [{"ko": "교육", "en": "education", "note": "teaching and training"}, {"ko": "열심히", "en": "diligently, hard", "note": "with great effort and dedication"}, {"ko": "일하다", "en": "to work", "note": "perform labor or job"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는", "exp": "topic marker. indicates what the sentence is about. 그녀는 (as for her)", "example_in_sentence": "그녀는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를 위해(서)", "exp": "for the sake of. indicates purpose or benefit. 교육을 위해 (for education)", "example_in_sentence": "교육을 위해"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~히 (adverb ending)", "exp": "Turns a word into an adverb. 열심 (hard work) + 히 → 열심히 (hard, diligently).", "example_in_sentence": "열심히"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었/였어요 (past polite)", "exp": "Past polite ending. 일하다 → 일했어요 (worked).", "example_in_sentence": "일했어요"}]}, {"text": "덕분에 많은 여자들이 조산사가 될 수 있었어요.", "translation": "Thanks to her efforts, many women were able to become midwives.", "vocab": [{"ko": "덕분", "en": "thanks to; credit", "note": "benefit or help from someone"}, {"ko": "많다", "en": "to be many", "note": "large in number or amount"}, {"ko": "되다", "en": "to become", "note": "change into a different state"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "덕분에", "exp": "''Thanks to (that)'' — gives a good reason for a result. At the start of a sentence it means ''thanks to her (work)''.", "example_in_sentence": "덕분에"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄴ/은", "exp": "adnominal ending for present state of adjectives. 많다 → 많은 (many)", "example_in_sentence": "많은"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가", "exp": "subject marker. marks the grammatical subject. 여자들이 (the women)", "example_in_sentence": "여자들이"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다", "exp": "ability/possibility. can do or be able to do. 될 수 있다 (can become)", "example_in_sentence": "될 수 있었어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었/였어요 (past polite)", "exp": "past tense polite form. 있다 + 었어요 = 있었어요 (was able to)", "example_in_sentence": "있었어요"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "흥미롭다", "en": "to be interesting", "note": "흥미(interest) + -롭다(suffix forming adjectives)"}, {"ko": "의사", "en": "doctor", "note": "medical doctor"}, {"ko": "조산사", "en": "midwife", "note": "person who assists in childbirth"}, {"ko": "여자", "en": "woman", "note": "female person"}, {"ko": "교육", "en": "education", "note": "teaching and training"}, {"ko": "주다", "en": "to give", "note": "basic verb for giving"}, {"ko": "그녀", "en": "she", "note": "third person feminine pronoun"}, {"ko": "상황", "en": "situation", "note": "circumstances or condition"}, {"ko": "보다", "en": "to see", "note": "basic verb for seeing"}, {"ko": "화", "en": "anger", "note": "feeling of anger or rage"}, {"ko": "그래서", "en": "so, therefore", "note": "conjunctive adverb showing result"}, {"ko": "막다", "en": "to block, to stop", "note": "prevent something from happening"}, {"ko": "캠페인", "en": "campaign", "note": "organized effort for a cause"}, {"ko": "시작하다", "en": "to start", "note": "begin something"}, {"ko": "왕", "en": "king", "note": "monarch or ruler"}, {"ko": "특별하다", "en": "to be special", "note": "different from ordinary"}, {"ko": "맡기다", "en": "to entrust", "note": "give responsibility to someone"}, {"ko": "나라", "en": "country", "note": "nation or state"}, {"ko": "전체", "en": "whole, entire", "note": "all parts together"}, {"ko": "가르치다", "en": "to teach", "note": "provide instruction or education"}, {"ko": "이것", "en": "this", "note": "demonstrative pronoun for nearby object"}, {"ko": "매우", "en": "very", "note": "adverb intensifying degree"}, {"ko": "중요하다", "en": "to be important", "note": "having great significance"}, {"ko": "수많다", "en": "to 