cision was made due to safety concerns rather than the robots'' personalities or behavior."}, {"name": "~는 것", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Turns a verb phrase into a noun: ''what one ~s''. 우려하다 → 우려하는 것 (what it worries about).", "ex_ko": "항공사가 가장 우려하는 것은 리튬이온 배터리예요.", "ex_en": "The airline''s main concern is lithium-ion batteries."}, {"name": "~ㄴ/는 데(에)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "in V-ing / for V-ing. 작동하는 데 (for operating)", "ex_ko": "이 배터리는 로봇이 작동하는 데 필요하지만 항공기 운항에 위험을 줄 수 있어요.", "ex_en": "These batteries are needed for robots to operate, but they can pose a risk to flights."}, {"name": "~지만", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "but / although. Shows contrast between clauses", "ex_ko": "이 배터리는 로봇이 작동하는 데 필요하지만 항공기 운항에 위험을 줄 수 있어요.", "ex_en": "These batteries are needed for robots to operate, but they can pose a risk to flights."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다/없다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "ability/possibility. 주다 (give) → 줄 수 있어요 (can give/pose)", "ex_ko": "이 배터리는 로봇이 작동하는 데 필요하지만 항공기 운항에 위험을 줄 수 있어요.", "ex_en": "These batteries are needed for robots to operate, but they can pose a risk to flights."}, {"name": "~(으)로", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "means/direction. 최우선으로 (as top priority / prioritizing)", "ex_ko": "사우스웨스트 항공은 승객의 안전을 최우선으로 고려해서 이런 정책을 만들었다고 설명했어요.", "ex_en": "Southwest Airlines explained that it created this policy by prioritizing passenger safety above all else."}, {"name": "~아/어서", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "cause / sequence. 고려하다 (consider) → 고려해서 (by considering)", "ex_ko": "사우스웨스트 항공은 승객의 안전을 최우선으로 고려해서 이런 정책을 만들었다고 설명했어요.", "ex_en": "Southwest Airlines explained that it created this policy by prioritizing passenger safety above all else."}, {"name": "~다고 설명하다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Reports an explanation: ''explain that ~''. 만들다 → 만들었다고 설명했어요 (explained that it made).", "ex_ko": "사우스웨스트 항공은 승객의 안전을 최우선으로 고려해서 이런 정책을 만들었다고 설명했어요.", "ex_en": "Southwest Airlines explained that it created this policy by prioritizing passenger safety above all else."}, {"name": "~고 있다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "continuous. 검토하다 (review) → 검토하고 있다 (is reviewing)", "ex_ko": "다른 항공사들도 비슷한 조치를 검토하고 있을 것으로 예상돼요.", "ex_en": "Other airlines are expected to be considering similar measures."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 것으로 예상되다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "''Is expected to ~'', common in news. 검토하고 있다 → 검토하고 있을 것으로 예상돼요 (are expected to be reviewing).", "ex_ko": "다른 항공사들도 비슷한 조치를 검토하고 있을 것으로 예상돼요.", "ex_en": "Other airlines are expected to be considering similar measures."}, {"name": "~되다 (passive)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Many 하다 verbs become passive with 되다. 예상하다 (expect) → 예상되다 → 예상돼요 (is expected).", "ex_ko": "다른 항공사들도 비슷한 조치를 검토하고 있을 것으로 예상돼요.", "ex_en": "Other airlines are expected to be considering similar measures."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mpbuo1b52c4d' and md5(translation) = '032a5c2a507fb240abc5e80d912fe8c0';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["A man deliberately gets bitten by a snake. This man helps other people with snake venom. He uses it for researching snake venom. This man does dangerous work. But he does it for other people. There are people like this.", "Korea faces serious teacher shortage, disrupting school classes", "What is an ''anxiety bag''? A popular trend", "The US and China resume talks over trade issues", "\"Talking pig\" becomes an SNS star", "The ''nothing maxing'' trend of doing nothing spreads"], "sentences": [{"text": "한 남자가 일부러 뱀에 물려요.", "translation": "A man gets bitten by a snake on purpose.", "vocab": [{"ko": "남자", "en": "man"}, {"ko": "일부러", "en": "on purpose; deliberately"}, {"ko": "뱀", "en": "snake"}, {"ko": "물리다", "en": "to be bitten"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에 물리다", "exp": "Passive form of ''물다'' (to bite). The particle ''에'' marks the agent (snake) causing the action.", "example_in_sentence": "뱀에 물려요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어요 (present polite)", "exp": "Polite present ending. 물리다 (to be bitten) → 물려요 (gets bitten).", "example_in_sentence": "물려요"}]}, {"text": "이 남자는 뱀 독으로 다른 사람을 도와요.", "translation": "This man helps other people with snake venom.", "vocab": [{"ko": "독", "en": "venom; poison"}, {"ko": "다르다", "en": "to be different; other"}, {"ko": "돕다", "en": "to help"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)로", "exp": "Marks the means or tool: ''with, by''. 독 ends in a consonant, so 으로: 독으로 (with venom).", "example_in_sentence": "독으로"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어요 (present polite)", "exp": "Polite present ending. 돕다 is irregular: 돕다 → 도와요 (helps).", "example_in_sentence": "도와요"}]}, {"text": "뱀 독을 연구하는 데 써요.", "translation": "It is used for researching snake venom.", "vocab": [{"ko": "연구하다", "en": "to research"}, {"ko": "쓰다", "en": "to use; to write"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 데 쓰다", "exp": "''Use (it) for doing ~'' — says what something is used for. 연구하다 → 연구하는 데 써요 (use it for research).", "example_in_sentence": "연구하는 데"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어요 (present polite)", "exp": "Polite present ending. 쓰다 → 써요 (uses); the ㅡ drops before 어.", "example_in_sentence": "써요"}]}, {"text": "이 남자는 위험한 일을 해요.", "translation": "This man does dangerous work.", "vocab": [{"ko": "위험하다", "en": "to be dangerous"}, {"ko": "일", "en": "work; job; task"}, {"ko": "하다", "en": "to do"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (adjective + noun)", "exp": "Lets an adjective describe a noun. 위험하다 → 위험한 일 (dangerous work).", "example_in_sentence": "위험한 일"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어요 (present polite)", "exp": "Polite present ending. 하다 → 해요 (does).", "example_in_sentence": "해요"}]}, {"text": "하지만 다른 사람을 위해서 해요.", "translation": "However, he does it for other people.", "vocab": [{"ko": "하지만", "en": "but; however"}, {"ko": "위하다", "en": "to be for; to do for someone''s sake"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를 위해서", "exp": "''For (the sake of)'' someone or something. 사람 → 사람을 위해서 (for people).", "example_in_sentence": "사람을 위해서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어요 (present polite)", "exp": "Polite present ending. 하다 → 해요 (does).", "example_in_sentence": "해요"}]}, {"text": "이런 사람이 있어요.", "translation": "There are people like this.", "vocab": [{"ko": "이런", "en": "like this; such; this kind of"}, {"ko": "있다", "en": "to be; to exist"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가 있다", "exp": "''There is / there are.'' 사람 + 이 있어요 = there are people.", "example_in_sentence": "사람이 있어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어요 (present polite)", "exp": "Polite present ending. 있다 → 있어요 (there is/are).", "example_in_sentence": "있어요"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "남자", "en": "man", "note": ""}, {"ko": "일부러", "en": "on purpose; deliberately", "note": ""}, {"ko": "뱀", "en": "snake", "note": ""}, {"ko": "물리다", "en": "to be bitten", "note": ""}, {"ko": "독", "en": "venom; poison", "note": ""}, {"ko": "다르다", "en": "to be different; other", "note": ""}, {"ko": "돕다", "en": "to help", "note": ""}, {"ko": "연구하다", "en": "to research", "note": ""}, {"ko": "쓰다", "en": "to use; to write", "note": ""}, {"ko": "위험하다", "en": "to be dangerous", "note": ""}, {"ko": "일", "en": "work; job; task", "note": ""}, {"ko": "하다", "en": "to do", "note": ""}, {"ko": "하지만", "en": "but; however", "note": ""}, {"ko": "위하다", "en": "to be for; to do for someone''s sake", "note": ""}, {"ko": "이런", "en": "like this; such; this kind of", "note": ""}, {"ko": "있다", "en": "to be; to exist", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사람", "en": "person; people", "note": ""}, {"ko": "이렇다", "en": "to be like this", "note": "adjective; 이런 is the modifier form"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~에 물리다", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Passive form of ''물다'' (to bite). The particle ''에'' marks the agent (snake) causing the action.", "ex_ko": "한 남자가 일부러 뱀에 물려요.", "ex_en": "A man gets bitten by a snake on purpose."}, {"name": "~아/어요 (present polite)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Polite present ending. 물리다 (to be bitten) → 물려요 (gets bitten).", "ex_ko": "한 남자가 일부러 뱀에 물려요.", "ex_en": "A man gets bitten by a snake on purpose."}, {"name": "~(으)로", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Marks the means or tool: ''with, by''. 독 ends in a consonant, so 으로: 독으로 (with venom).", "ex_ko": "이 남자는 뱀 독으로 다른 사람을 도와요.", "ex_en": "This man helps other people with snake venom."}, {"name": "~는 데 쓰다", "level": "Starter", "exp": "''Use (it) for doing ~'' — says what something is used for. 연구하다 → 연구하는 데 써요 (use it for research).", "ex_ko": "뱀 독을 연구하는 데 써요.", "ex_en": "It is used for researching snake venom."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄴ (adjective + noun)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Lets an adjective describe a noun. 위험하다 → 위험한 일 (dangerous work).", "ex_ko": "이 남자는 위험한 일을 해요.", "ex_en": "This man does dangerous work."}, {"name": "~을/를 위해서", "level": "Starter", "exp": "''For (the sake of)'' someone or something. 사람 → 사람을 위해서 (for people).", "ex_ko": "하지만 다른 사람을 위해서 해요.", "ex_en": "However, he does it for other people."}, {"name": "~이/가 있다", "level": "Starter", "exp": "''There is / there are.'' 사람 + 이 있어요 = there are people.", "ex_ko": "이런 사람이 있어요.", "ex_en": "There are people like this."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mpckotho2g2i' and md5(translation) = 'fa0a9405dd3cad82c81f268615586ec3';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["Greece is scheduled to repay 6.9 billion euros in June. Once this amount is fully repaid, Greece will no longer be the most indebted nation in the Eurozone.", "Greece had long been the most indebted nation in the Eurozone. However, this repayment brings that record to an end.", "6.9 billion euros is a very large sum. Greece is able to repay this amount in June.", "This repayment is an important change for Greece. Greece is now no longer the Eurozone''s most indebted nation."], "sentences": [{"text": "그리스는 6월에 69억 유로를 갚을 예정이에요.", "translation": "Greece is scheduled to repay 6.9 billion euros in June.", "vocab": [{"ko": "갚다", "en": "to repay, to pay back", "note": "used for repaying debts or loans"}, {"ko": "예정", "en": "schedule, plan", "note": "noun meaning something that is planned or scheduled"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를 (object marker)", "exp": "Object particle. Attaches to the noun that receives the action of the verb. 유로 + 를 = 유로를 (euros [as the object of repaying]).", "example_in_sentence": "유로를"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 예정이다", "exp": "''Is scheduled / planned to ~''. 갚다 → 갚을 예정이에요 (is scheduled to repay).", "example_in_sentence": "갚을 예정이에요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에 (location/time)", "exp": "Time particle. Attaches to a time expression to mark when something happens. 6월 + 에 = 6월에 (in June).", "example_in_sentence": "6월에"}]}, {"text": "이 돈을 다 갚으면 그리스는 유로존에서 빚이 가장 많은 나라가 아니에요.", "translation": "Once this amount is fully repaid, Greece will no longer be the most indebted nation in the Eurozone.", "vocab": [{"ko": "갚다", "en": "to repay, to pay back", "note": "repaying a debt"}, {"ko": "빚", "en": "debt", "note": "money owed to others"}, {"ko": "많다", "en": "to be many, to be much", "note": "adjective describing a large quantity or amount"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)면 (if/when)", "exp": "Conditional connective. Verb stem + (으)면 = ''if/when ~''. 갚다 → 갚으면 (if/when [one] repays). Used here to express a condition that leads to a result.", "example_in_sentence": "갚으면"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서 (location/source)", "exp": "Location particle indicating where something takes place or a source. 유로존 + 에서 = 유로존에서 (in/within the Eurozone).", "example_in_sentence": "유로존에서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄴ/은 (past verb / present adj modifier)", "exp": "Adnominal (modifier) ending for adjectives in present tense. 많다 (to be many/much) → 많은 + 나라 = ''a country with the most [debt]''. The adjective stem 많- + 은 modifies the noun 나라.", "example_in_sentence": "많은 나라"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가 아니다", "exp": "''Is not'' — the negative of 이다. 나라가 아니에요 (is not the country).", "example_in_sentence": "나라가 아니에요"}]}, {"text": "그리스는 오랫동안 유로존에서 빚이 가장 많은 나라였어요.", "translation": "Greece had long been the most indebted nation in the Eurozone.", "vocab": [{"ko": "오랫동안", "en": "for a long time", "note": "adverb indicating a long duration"}, {"ko": "빚", "en": "debt", "note": "money owed"}, {"ko": "많다", "en": "to be many, to be much", "note": "adjective"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었/였어요 (past polite)", "exp": "Past tense polite ending. 나라이다 (to be a country) → 나라였어요 (was a country). The copula 이다 contracts: 이었어요 → 였어요 after a vowel-final noun (나라).", "example_in_sentence": "나라였어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄴ/은 (past verb / present adj modifier)", "exp": "Adnominal ending for adjectives. 많다 → 많은 + 나라 = ''a country that has the most (debt)''. The adjective modifies the noun that follows.", "example_in_sentence": "많은 나라"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서 (location/source)", "exp": "Location particle marking where a state exists or an action takes place. 유로존 + 에서 = 유로존에서 (in the Eurozone).", "example_in_sentence": "유로존에서"}]}, {"text": "하지만 이번 상환으로 그 기록이 끝났어요.", "translation": "However, with this repayment, that record came to an end.", "vocab": [{"ko": "상환", "en": "repayment (of debt)", "note": "formal noun for paying back borrowed money"}, {"ko": "기록", "en": "record", "note": "here meaning a long-held status or streak"}, {"ko": "끝나다", "en": "to end, to finish", "note": "intransitive verb; the subject ends on its own"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)로 (means/direction)", "exp": "Particle indicating means or cause. 상환 + 으로 = 상환으로 (by means of / through this repayment). Used here to show what caused the record to end.", "example_in_sentence": "상환으로"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었/였어요 (past polite)", "exp": "Past tense polite ending. 끝나다 (to end) → stem 끝나- + 았어요 = 끝났어요 (ended). The ㅏ vowel in the stem triggers 았.", "example_in_sentence": "끝났어요"}]}, {"text": "69억 유로는 매우 큰 금액이에요.", "translation": "6.9 billion euros is a very large sum.", "vocab": [{"ko": "매우", "en": "very, extremely", "note": "adverb intensifying an adjective"}, {"ko": "크다", "en": "to be big, to be large", "note": "adjective"}, {"ko": "금액", "en": "amount of money, sum", "note": "formal noun for a monetary amount"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는 (topic marker)", "exp": "Topic particle. Marks 69억 유로 as the topic of the sentence. 69억 유로 + 는 = 69억 유로는 (As for 6.9 billion euros, …).", "example_in_sentence": "69억 유로는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄴ/은 (adjective + noun)", "exp": "Lets an adjective describe a noun. Vowel stems take ㄴ: 크다 → 큰 금액 (a large sum).", "example_in_sentence": "큰 금액"}]}, {"text": "그리스는 이 금액을 6월에 갚을 수 있어요.", "translation": "Greece is able to repay this amount in June.", "vocab": [{"ko": "갚다", "en": "to repay, to pay back", "note": ""}, {"ko": "금액", "en": "amount of money, sum", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다/없다 (ability/possibility)", "exp": "Ability/possibility construction. Verb stem + (으)ㄹ 수 있다 = ''can / is able to''. 갚다 → 갚을 수 있어요 (can repay). The ㄹ is added to the stem 갚- (consonant-final) with 을.", "example_in_sentence": "갚을 수 있어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를 (object marker)", "exp": "Object particle. Marks the noun receiving the action. 금액 + 을 = 금액을 (this amount [as the object]).", "example_in_sentence": "금액을"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에 (location/time)", "exp": "Time particle. 6월 + 에 = 6월에 (in June), marking when the repayment happens.", "example_in_sentence": "6월에"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어/여요 (present polite)", "exp": "present polite informal ending", "example_in_sentence": "있어요"}]}, {"text": "이번 상환은 그리스에게 중요한 변화예요.", "translation": "This repayment is an important change for Greece.", "vocab": [{"ko": "상환", "en": "repayment (of debt)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "중요하다", "en": "to be important", "note": "adjective"}, {"ko": "변화", "en": "change", "note": "noun meaning a shift or transformation in a situation"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에게/한테 (to person)", "exp": "Dative particle for people or organizations. 그리스 + 에게 = 그리스에게 (for/to Greece). Marks the beneficiary or the entity for which something is relevant.", "example_in_sentence": "그리스에게"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄴ/은 (past verb / present adj modifier)", "exp": "Adnominal ending for adjectives. 중요하다 (to be important) → 중요한 + 변화 = ''an important change''. Stem 중요하- + ㄴ = 중요한.", "example_in_sentence": "중요한 변화"}]}, {"text": "이제 그리스는 유로존 최대 채무국이 아니에요.", "translation": "Greece is now no longer the Eurozone''s most indebted nation.", "vocab": [{"ko": "이제", "en": "now, from now on", "note": "adverb marking a new present state"}, {"ko": "최대", "en": "largest, greatest, maximum", "note": "prefix/noun used before a noun to mean ''biggest'' or ''most''"}, {"ko": "채무국", "en": "debtor nation", "note": "a country that owes large amounts of debt"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가 (subject marker)", "exp": "Subject particle. 채무국 + 이 = 채무국이, marking 채무국 as the subject complement of the negated copula 아니에요.", "example_in_sentence": "채무국이"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가 아니다", "exp": "''Is not'' — the negative of 이다. 채무국이 아니에요 (is not the debtor nation).", "example_in_sentence": "채무국이 아니에요"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "갚다", "en": "to repay, to pay back", "note": "used for repaying debts or loans"}, {"ko": "예정", "en": "schedule, plan", "note": "noun meaning something that is planned or scheduled"}, {"ko": "빚", "en": "debt", "note": "money owed to others"}, {"ko": "많다", "en": "to be many, to be much", "note": "adjective describing a large quantity or amount"}, {"ko": "오랫동안", "en": "for a long time", "note": "adverb indicating a long duration"}, {"ko": "상환", "en": "repayment (of debt)", "note": "formal noun for paying back borrowed money"}, {"ko": "기록", "en": "record", "note": "here meaning a long-held status or streak"}, {"ko": "끝나다", "en": "to end, to finish", "note": "intransitive verb; the subject ends on its own"}, {"ko": "매우", "en": "very, extremely", "note": "adverb intensifying an adjective"}, {"ko": "크다", "en": "to be big, to be large", "note": "adjective"}, {"ko": "금액", "en": "amount of money, sum", "note": "formal noun for a monetary amount"}, {"ko": "중요하다", "en": "to be important", "note": "adjective"}, {"ko": "변화", "en": "change", "note": "noun meaning a shift or transformation in a situation"}, {"ko": "이제", "en": "now, from now on", "note": "adverb marking a new present state"}, {"ko": "최대", "en": "largest, greatest, maximum", "note": "prefix/noun used before a noun to mean ''biggest'' or ''most''"}, {"ko": "채무국", "en": "debtor nation", "note": "a country that owes large amounts of debt"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~을/를 (object marker)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Object particle. Attaches to the noun that receives the action of the verb. 유로 + 를 = 유로를 (euros [as the object of repaying]).", "ex_ko": "그리스는 6월에 69억 유로를 갚을 예정이에요.", "ex_en": "Greece is scheduled to repay 6.9 billion euros in June."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 예정이다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "''Is scheduled / planned to ~''. 갚다 → 갚을 예정이에요 (is scheduled to repay).", "ex_ko": "그리스는 6월에 69억 유로를 갚을 예정이에요.", "ex_en": "Greece is scheduled to repay 6.9 billion euros in June."}, {"name": "~에서 (location/source)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Location particle indicating where something takes place or a source. 유로존 + 에서 = 유로존에서 (in/within the Eurozone).", "ex_ko": "그리스는 6월에 69억 유로를 갚을 예정이에요.", "ex_en": "Greece is scheduled to repay 6.9 billion euros in June."}, {"name": "~(으)면 (if/when)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Conditional connective. Verb stem + (으)면 = ''if/when ~''. 갚다 → 갚으면 (if/when [one] repays). Used here to express a condition that leads to a result.", "ex_ko": "이 돈을 다 갚으면 그리스는 유로존에서 빚이 가장 많은 나라가 아니에요.", "ex_en": "Once this amount is fully repaid, Greece will no longer be the most indebted nation in the Eurozone."}, {"name": "~ㄴ/은 (past verb / present adj modifier)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Adnominal (modifier) ending for adjectives in present tense. 많다 (to be many/much) → 많은 + 나라 = ''a country with the most [debt]''. The adjective stem 많- + 은 modifies the noun 나라.", "ex_ko": "이 돈을 다 갚으면 그리스는 유로존에서 빚이 가장 많은 나라가 아니에요.", "ex_en": "Once this amount is fully repaid, Greece will no longer be the most indebted nation in the Eurozone."}, {"name": "~이/가 아니다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "''Is not'' — the negative of 이다. 채무국이 아니에요 (is not the debtor nation).", "ex_ko": "이 돈을 다 갚으면 그리스는 유로존에서 빚이 가장 많은 나라가 아니에요.", "ex_en": "Once this amount is fully repaid, Greece will no longer be the most indebted nation in the Eurozone."}, {"name": "~았/었/였어요 (past polite)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Past tense polite ending. 나라이다 (to be a country) → 나라였어요 (was a country). The copula 이다 contracts: 이었어요 → 였어요 after a vowel-final noun (나라).", "ex_ko": "그리스는 오랫동안 유로존에서 빚이 가장 많은 나라였어요.", "ex_en": "Greece had long been the most indebted nation in the Eurozone."}, {"name": "~(으)로 (means/direction)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Particle indicating means or cause. 상환 + 으로 = 상환으로 (by means of / through this repayment). Used here to show what caused the record to end.", "ex_ko": "하지만 이번 상환으로 그 기록이 끝났어요.", "ex_en": "However, with this repayment, that record came to an end."}, {"name": "~은/는 (topic marker)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Topic particle. Marks 69억 유로 as the topic of the sentence. 69억 유로 + 는 = 69억 유로는 (As for 6.9 billion euros, …).", "ex_ko": "69억 유로는 매우 큰 금액이에요.", "ex_en": "6.9 billion euros is a very large sum."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다/없다 (ability/possibility)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Ability/possibility construction. Verb stem + (으)ㄹ 수 있다 = ''can / is able to''. 갚다 → 갚을 수 있어요 (can repay). The ㄹ is added to the stem 갚- (consonant-final) with 을.", "ex_ko": "그리스는 이 금액을 6월에 갚을 수 있어요.", "ex_en": "Greece is able to repay this amount in June."}, {"name": "~아/어/여요 (present polite)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "present polite informal ending", "ex_ko": "그리스는 이 금액을 6월에 갚을 수 있어요.", "ex_en": "Greece is able to repay this amount in June."}, {"name": "~에게/한테 (to person)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Dative particle for people or organizations. 그리스 + 에게 = 그리스에게 (for/to Greece). Marks the beneficiary or the entity for which something is relevant.", "ex_ko": "이번 상환은 그리스에게 중요한 변화예요.", "ex_en": "This repayment is an important change for Greece."}, {"name": "~이/가 (subject marker)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Subject particle. 채무국 + 이 = 채무국이, marking 채무국 as the subject complement of the negated copula 아니에요.", "ex_ko": "이제 그리스는 유로존 최대 채무국이 아니에요.", "ex_en": "Greece is now no longer the Eurozone''s most indebted nation."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mpckq31v2rbr' and md5(translation) = 'a2d39d97811280641c0c6a45b3cd870c';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["Some people don''t have electricity or the internet. So they can''t enjoy entertainment. There is a way for these people. There are places on the street that show movies or videos. People call this the \"Netflix for poor people.\" They watch videos on the street, not at home. People without electricity and the internet can enjoy entertainment this way too. Street cinemas are an important place for these people.", "Korean Teacher Shortage Becomes Serious, School Classes Disrupted", "What is an \"anxiety bag\"? A Popular Trend", "The United States and China Resume Talks Over Trade Issues", "\"Talking Pig\" Becomes SNS Star", "Apple Greatly Improves iPhone Speed with New AI Chip"], "sentences": [{"text": "어떤 사람들은 전기도 없고 인터넷도 없어요.", "translation": "Some people have neither electricity nor internet.", "vocab": [{"ko": "어떤", "en": "some; certain"}, {"ko": "전기", "en": "electricity"}, {"ko": "인터넷", "en": "internet"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~도 없고 ~도 없어요", "exp": "Parallel negation structure meaning ''neither A nor B''. The particle 도 (also/even) with 없다 (to not have) creates listing of multiple absent items.", "example_in_sentence": "전기도 없고 인터넷도 없어요"}]}, {"text": "그래서 오락을 즐기지 못해요.", "translation": "Therefore, they cannot enjoy entertainment.", "vocab": [{"ko": "그래서", "en": "therefore; so"}, {"ko": "오락", "en": "entertainment; recreation"}, {"ko": "즐기다", "en": "to enjoy"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~지 못하다", "exp": "''Cannot do.'' 즐기다 → 즐기지 못하다 → 즐기지 못해요 (cannot enjoy).", "example_in_sentence": "즐기지 못해요"}]}, {"text": "이런 사람들을 위한 방법이 있어요.", "translation": "There is a method for such people.", "vocab": [{"ko": "이런", "en": "such; like this"}, {"ko": "방법", "en": "method; way"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~을/를 위한 N", "exp": "''For'' before a noun. 사람들을 위하다 → 사람들을 위한 방법 (a way for people).", "example_in_sentence": "사람들을 위한 방법"}]}, {"text": "거리에서 영화나 영상을 보여 주는 곳이 있어요.", "translation": "There is a place that shows movies or videos on the street.", "vocab": [{"ko": "거리", "en": "street; road"}, {"ko": "영화", "en": "movie"}, {"ko": "영상", "en": "video; image"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~나", "exp": "Listing particle indicating alternatives or multiple items (A or B). Shows inclusive or exclusive choice. Example: 사과나 배 (apples or pears).", "example_in_sentence": "영화나 영상을"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 곳", "exp": "Present verb modifier + 곳 (place): ''a place that ~''. 보여 주다 → 보여 주는 곳 (a place that shows).", "example_in_sentence": "보여 주는 곳"}]}, {"text": "사람들은 이것을 ''가난한 사람들의 넷플릭스''라고 불러요.", "translation": "People call this the ''Netflix for poor people.''", "vocab": [{"ko": "가난하다", "en": "to be poor"}, {"ko": "부르다", "en": "to call; to name"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~라고 부르다", "exp": "Expression meaning ''to call/name something as.'' The quotative particle 라고 indicates what something is called, used with the verb 부르다.", "example_in_sentence": "''가난한 사람들의 넷플릭스''라고 불러요"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~의 (possessive/descriptive particle)", "exp": "Genitive particle showing possession or descriptive relationship. Here: ''가난한 사람들의 넷플릭스'' = Netflix belonging to/for poor people.", "example_in_sentence": "가난한 사람들의 넷플릭스"}]}, {"text": "집이 아니라 거리에서 영상을 봐요.", "translation": "They watch videos on the street, not at home.", "vocab": [{"ko": "집", "en": "house; home"}, {"ko": "아니다", "en": "to not be; to be not"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~이 아니라", "exp": "Contrast particle meaning ''not... but rather.'' Shows negation of one thing while introducing an alternative. Chain: 집이다 → 집이 아니다 → 집이 아니라.", "example_in_sentence": "집이 아니라"}]}, {"text": "전기와 인터넷이 없는 사람들도 이렇게 오락을 즐길 수 있어요.", "translation": "Even people without electricity and internet can enjoy entertainment like this.", "vocab": [{"ko": "이렇게", "en": "in this way; like this"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가 없는 N", "exp": "''Without'' before a noun. 인터넷이 없다 → 인터넷이 없는 사람들 (people without internet).", "example_in_sentence": "전기와 인터넷이 없는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다", "exp": "''Can / be able to.'' 즐기다 → 즐길 수 있어요 (can enjoy).", "example_in_sentence": "즐길 수 있어요"}]}, {"text": "거리 영화관은 이 사람들에게 중요한 곳이에요.", "translation": "The street cinema is an important place for these people.", "vocab": [{"ko": "거리 영화관", "en": "street cinema; outdoor theater"}, {"ko": "중요하다", "en": "to be important"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~에게 (dative particle for animate)", "exp": "Dative particle marking the recipient or target of an action/state. Used with animate objects. Here: 이 사람들에게 (for/to these people).", "example_in_sentence": "이 사람들에게"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "어떤", "en": "some; certain", "note": ""}, {"ko": "전기", "en": "electricity", "note": ""}, {"ko": "인터넷", "en": "internet", "note": ""}, {"ko": "그래서", "en": "therefore; so", "note": ""}, {"ko": "오락", "en": "entertainment; recreation", "note": ""}, {"ko": "즐기다", "en": "to enjoy", "note": ""}, {"ko": "이런", "en": "such; like this", "note": ""}, {"ko": "방법", "en": "method; way", "note": ""}, {"ko": "거리", "en": "street; road", "note": ""}, {"ko": "영화", "en": "movie", "note": ""}, {"ko": "영상", "en": "video; image", "note": ""}, {"ko": "가난하다", "en": "to be poor", "note": ""}, {"ko": "부르다", "en": "to call; to name", "note": ""}, {"ko": "집", "en": "house; home", "note": ""}, {"ko": "아니다", "en": "to not be; to be not", "note": ""}, {"ko": "이렇게", "en": "in this way; like this", "note": ""}, {"ko": "거리 영화관", "en": "street cinema; outdoor theater", "note": ""}, {"ko": "중요하다", "en": "to be important", "note": ""}, {"ko": "보여 주다", "en": "to show (to someone)", "note": "보여 주다 = 보이다 + 아/어 주다; the ~아/어 주다 form means doing something for someone"}, {"ko": "보다", "en": "to watch; to see", "note": ""}, {"ko": "영화관", "en": "cinema; movie theater", "note": ""}, {"ko": "곳", "en": "place; spot", "note": ""}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~도 없고 ~도 없어요", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Parallel negation structure meaning ''neither A nor B''. The particle 도 (also/even) with 없다 (to not have) creates listing of multiple absent items.", "ex_ko": "어떤 사람들은 전기도 없고 인터넷도 없어요.", "ex_en": "Some people have neither electricity nor internet."}, {"name": "~지 못하다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "''Cannot do.'' 즐기다 → 즐기지 못하다 → 즐기지 못해요 (cannot enjoy).", "ex_ko": "그래서 오락을 즐기지 못해요.", "ex_en": "Therefore, they cannot enjoy entertainment."}, {"name": "~나", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Listing particle indicating alternatives or multiple items (A or B). Shows inclusive or exclusive choice. Example: 사과나 배 (apples or pears).", "ex_ko": "거리에서 영화나 영상을 보여 주는 곳이 있어요.", "ex_en": "There is a place that shows movies or videos on the street."}, {"name": "~는 곳", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Present verb modifier + 곳 (place): ''a place that ~''. 보여 주다 → 보여 주는 곳 (a place that shows).", "ex_ko": "거리에서 영화나 영상을 보여 주는 곳이 있어요.", "ex_en": "There is a place that shows movies or videos on the street."}, {"name": "~라고 부르다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Expression meaning ''to call/name something as.'' The quotative particle 라고 indicates what something is called, used with the verb 부르다.", "ex_ko": "사람들은 이것을 ''가난한 사람들의 넷플릭스''라고 불러요.", "ex_en": "People call this the ''Netflix for poor people.''"}, {"name": "~이 아니라", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Contrast particle meaning ''not... but rather.'' Shows negation of one thing while introducing an alternative. Chain: 집이다 → 집이 아니다 → 집이 아니라.", "ex_ko": "집이 아니라 거리에서 영상을 봐요.", "ex_en": "They watch videos on the street, not at home."}, {"name": "~이/가 없는 N", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "''Without'' before a noun. 인터넷이 없다 → 인터넷이 없는 사람들 (people without internet).", "ex_ko": "전기와 인터넷이 없는 사람들도 이렇게 오락을 즐길 수 있어요.", "ex_en": "Even people without electricity and internet can enjoy entertainment like this."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "''Can / be able to.'' 즐기다 → 즐길 수 있어요 (can enjoy).", "ex_ko": "전기와 인터넷이 없는 사람들도 이렇게 오락을 즐길 수 있어요.", "ex_en": "Even people without electricity and internet can enjoy entertainment like this."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mpckreuuvvui' and md5(translation) = '3cc03b53dd016cce5c5c3e63818e20a6';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["A recent decision made by Starbucks Korea has been causing controversy online. The decision has been drawing questions from many people, regardless of their political point of view.", "On online communities, reactions have emerged saying it is hard to understand what Starbucks Korea was thinking when it made this decision. People across different political positions appear to be reacting the same way on this point.", "This controversy has come to receive attention in overseas communities as well. Discussion continues over what context led to Starbucks Korea''s decision."], "sentences": [{"text": "최근 스타벅스 코리아가 내린 한 결정이 온라인에서 논란이 되고 있어요.", "translation": "A recent decision made by Starbucks Korea has been causing controversy online.", "vocab": [{"ko": "내리다", "en": "to make (a decision); to hand down", "note": "used with 결정 to mean ''make a decision''"}, {"ko": "결정", "en": "decision", "note": ""}, {"ko": "논란", "en": "controversy; dispute", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있다", "exp": "Shows something ongoing. 되다 → 되고 있어요; 논란이 되고 있어요 = is becoming controversial.", "example_in_sentence": "논란이 되고 있어요"}]}, {"text": "해당 결정은 정치적 관점과 무관하게 많은 사람들의 의문을 사고 있어요.", "translation": "The decision has been drawing questions from many people, regardless of their political point of view.", "vocab": [{"ko": "해당", "en": "relevant; corresponding; said (referring to something just mentioned)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "관점", "en": "point of view; perspective", "note": ""}, {"ko": "무관하다", "en": "to be unrelated; to have nothing to do with", "note": "무관하게 is the adverbial form"}, {"ko": "의문", "en": "question; doubt", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~게 (adverbializer suffix)", "exp": "Turns an adjective stem into an adverb. 무관하다 (to be unrelated) → 무관하게 (regardless; in an unrelated way). The adverb modifies the whole predicate.", "example_in_sentence": "무관하게"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있다", "exp": "Expresses a continuing state or action. 사다 (to buy/draw) → 사고 있다 → 사고 있어요 (is drawing/garnering).", "example_in_sentence": "의문을 사고 있어요"}]}, {"text": "온라인 커뮤니티에서는 스타벅스 코리아가 무슨 생각으로 이런 결정을 했는지 이해하기 어렵다는 반응이 나오고 있어요.", "translation": "On online communities, reactions have emerged saying it is hard to understand what Starbucks Korea was thinking when it made this decision.", "vocab": [{"ko": "커뮤니티", "en": "community (online forum/community)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "이해하다", "en": "to understand", "note": ""}, {"ko": "반응", "en": "reaction; response", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~기 어렵다", "exp": "''Hard to do ~''. 이해하다 → 이해하기 어렵다 (hard to understand).", "example_in_sentence": "이해하기 어렵다"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~다는 N", "exp": "Quotes content to describe a noun: ''the N that says ~''. 어렵다 → 어렵다는 반응 (reactions saying it is hard).", "example_in_sentence": "어렵다는 반응"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있다", "exp": "Ongoing action. 나오다 (to come out) → 나오고 있어요 (is coming out / are emerging).", "example_in_sentence": "나오고 있어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었는지", "exp": "Embeds a question inside a sentence: ''what / whether ~''. 하다 → 했는지 (what (they) did).", "example_in_sentence": "했는지"}]}, {"text": "정치적 입장이 다른 사람들도 이 점에서는 같은 반응을 보이는 것 같아요.", "translation": "People across different political positions appear to be reacting the same way on this point.", "vocab": [{"ko": "입장", "en": "position; stance", "note": ""}, {"ko": "다르다", "en": "to be different", "note": "르 불규칙: 다르다 → 다른 (modifier form)"}, {"ko": "반응을 보이다", "en": "to show a reaction; to react", "note": "fixed collocation"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄴ/는/(으)ㄹ 것 같다 (seems)", "exp": "Expresses the speaker''s inference or conjecture. <present verb modifier ~는> + 것 같다. 보이다 → 보이는 것 같아요 = ''it seems (they) show''.", "example_in_sentence": "보이는 것 같아요"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~을/를 보이다", "exp": "Fixed collocation meaning ''to show / display (a reaction, attitude, etc.)''. 반응을 보이다 = ''to show a reaction''. Commonly used in news writing.", "example_in_sentence": "같은 반응을 보이는"}]}, {"text": "이 논란은 해외 커뮤니티에서도 주목을 받게 되었어요.", "translation": "This controversy has come to receive attention in overseas communities as well.", "vocab": [{"ko": "해외", "en": "overseas; abroad", "note": ""}, {"ko": "주목", "en": "attention; notice", "note": "주목을 받다 = to receive attention"}, {"ko": "받다", "en": "to receive", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~게 되다", "exp": "Expresses a change of state or a situation that came about (often beyond the subject''s control). <verb stem> + 게 되다. 받다 → 받게 되다 → 받게 되었어요 = ''came to receive''.", "example_in_sentence": "주목을 받게 되었어요"}]}, {"text": "스타벅스 코리아의 결정이 어떤 맥락에서 나온 것인지에 대한 논의가 이어지고 있어요.", "translation": "Discussion continues over what context led to Starbucks Korea''s decision.", "vocab": [{"ko": "맥락", "en": "context; background", "note": ""}, {"ko": "논의", "en": "discussion; debate", "note": ""}, {"ko": "이어지다", "en": "to continue; to be connected", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~에 대한 N", "exp": "''About / regarding'' before a noun. 나온 것인지에 대한 논의 = discussion about where (the decision) came from.", "example_in_sentence": "나온 것인지에 대한 논의"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있다", "exp": "Ongoing state. 이어지다 (to continue) → 이어지고 있어요 = ''is continuing / is ongoing''.", "example_in_sentence": "이어지고 있어요"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "내리다", "en": "to make (a decision); to hand down", "note": "used with 결정 to mean ''make a decision''"}, {"ko": "결정", "en": "decision", "note": ""}, {"ko": "논란", "en": "controversy; dispute", "note": ""}, {"ko": "해당", "en": "relevant; corresponding; said (referring to something just mentioned)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "관점", "en": "point of view; perspective", "note": ""}, {"ko": "무관하다", "en": "to be unrelated; to have nothing to do with", "note": "무관하게 is the adverbial form"}, {"ko": "의문", "en": "question; doubt", "note": ""}, {"ko": "커뮤니티", "en": "community (online forum/community)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "이해하다", "en": "to understand", "note": ""}, {"ko": "반응", "en": "reaction; response", "note": ""}, {"ko": "입장", "en": "position; stance", "note": ""}, {"ko": "다르다", "en": "to be different", "note": "르 불규칙: 다르다 → 다른 (modifier form)"}, {"ko": "반응을 보이다", "en": "to show a reaction; to react", "note": "fixed collocation"}, {"ko": "해외", "en": "overseas; abroad", "note": ""}, {"ko": "주목", "en": "attention; notice", "note": "주목을 받다 = to receive attention"}, {"ko": "받다", "en": "to receive", "note": ""}, {"ko": "맥락", "en": "context; background", "note": ""}, {"ko": "논의", "en": "discussion; debate", "note": ""}, {"ko": "이어지다", "en": "to continue; to be connected", "note": ""}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~고 있다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Expresses a continuing state or action. 사다 (to buy/draw) → 사고 있다 → 사고 있어요 (is drawing/garnering).", "ex_ko": "최근 스타벅스 코리아가 내린 한 결정이 온라인에서 논란이 되고 있어요.", "ex_en": "A recent decision made by Starbucks Korea has been causing controversy online."}, {"name": "~게 (adverbializer suffix)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Turns an adjective stem into an adverb. 무관하다 (to be unrelated) → 무관하게 (regardless; in an unrelated way). The adverb modifies the whole predicate.", "ex_ko": "해당 결정은 정치적 관점과 무관하게 많은 사람들의 의문을 사고 있어요.", "ex_en": "The decision has been drawing questions from many people, regardless of their political point of view."}, {"name": "~기 어렵다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "''Hard to do ~''. 이해하다 → 이해하기 어렵다 (hard to understand).", "ex_ko": "온라인 커뮤니티에서는 스타벅스 코리아가 무슨 생각으로 이런 결정을 했는지 이해하기 어렵다는 반응이 나오고 있어요.", "ex_en": "On online communities, reactions have emerged saying it is hard to understand what Starbucks Korea was thinking when it made this decision."}, {"name": "~다는 N", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Quotes content to describe a noun: ''the N that says ~''. 어렵다 → 어렵다는 반응 (reactions saying it is hard).", "ex_ko": "온라인 커뮤니티에서는 스타벅스 코리아가 무슨 생각으로 이런 결정을 했는지 이해하기 어렵다는 반응이 나오고 있어요.", "ex_en": "On online communities, reactions have emerged saying it is hard to understand what Starbucks Korea was thinking when it made this decision."}, {"name": "~았/었는지", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Embeds a question inside a sentence: ''what / whether ~''. 하다 → 했는지 (what (they) did).", "ex_ko": "온라인 커뮤니티에서는 스타벅스 코리아가 무슨 생각으로 이런 결정을 했는지 이해하기 어렵다는 반응이 나오고 있어요.", "ex_en": "On online communities, reactions have emerged saying it is hard to understand what Starbucks Korea was thinking when it made this decision."}, {"name": "~ㄴ/는/(으)ㄹ 것 같다 (seems)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Expresses the speaker''s inference or conjecture. <present verb modifier ~는> + 것 같다. 보이다 → 보이는 것 같아요 = ''it seems (they) show''.", "ex_ko": "정치적 입장이 다른 사람들도 이 점에서는 같은 반응을 보이는 것 같아요.", "ex_en": "People across different political positions appear to be reacting the same way on this point."}, {"name": "~게 되다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Expresses a change of state or a situation that came about (often beyond the subject''s control). <verb stem> + 게 되다. 받다 → 받게 되다 → 받게 되었어요 = ''came to receive''.", "ex_ko": "이 논란은 해외 커뮤니티에서도 주목을 받게 되었어요.", "ex_en": "This controversy has come to receive attention in overseas communities as well."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mpcksibvjjw6' and md5(translation) = 'ec1b33c6cab47823fe23eeda3fa46580';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["A woman caught a thief herself. She made sure the thief could not escape.", "The woman grabbed the thief. Then she applied a choke hold around his neck.", "The thief could not escape. It was because the woman did not let go.", "The woman held onto the thief until the very end."], "sentences": [{"text": "한 여성이 도둑을 직접 잡았다.", "translation": "A woman caught a thief herself.", "vocab": [{"ko": "여성", "en": "woman", "note": "adult female"}, {"ko": "도둑", "en": "thief", "note": "person who steals"}, {"ko": "직접", "en": "directly; oneself; in person", "note": "adverb meaning ''by one''s own action''"}, {"ko": "잡다", "en": "to catch; to grab", "note": "physical apprehension"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가", "exp": "Subject marker. 여성 ends in a consonant, so 이 is used: 여성이 (a woman).", "example_in_sentence": "여성이"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를", "exp": "Object marker. Attaches to the object noun. 도둑 ends in a consonant, so ~을 is used: 도둑을 (the thief [object]).", "example_in_sentence": "도둑을"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었다 (past, plain)", "exp": "Past tense in plain written (news) style. 잡다 → 잡았다 (caught).", "example_in_sentence": "잡았다"}]}, {"text": "여성은 도둑이 도망치지 못하게 했다.", "translation": "She made sure the thief could not escape.", "vocab": [{"ko": "도망치다", "en": "to run away; to escape", "note": "flee from a place or situation"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는", "exp": "Topic marker. 여성 ends in a consonant, so ~은 is used: 여성은 (as for the woman / the woman [topic]).", "example_in_sentence": "여성은"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~지 못하다", "exp": "Inability negation. Verb stem + 지 못하다 = cannot do (due to inability or prevention). 도망치다 → 도망치지 못하다 (cannot escape). Here embedded before ~게 하다.", "example_in_sentence": "도망치지 못하게"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~게 하다", "exp": "Causative construction meaning ''make/let someone do/be (a certain way)''. [V/A] + 게 하다. Here: 도망치지 못하게 하다 = make it so (the thief) cannot escape. Past: 했다.", "example_in_sentence": "도망치지 못하게 했다"}]}, {"text": "여성은 도둑을 붙잡았다.", "translation": "The woman grabbed the thief.", "vocab": [{"ko": "붙잡다", "en": "to grab; to seize; to hold onto", "note": "stronger/firmer form of 잡다"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를", "exp": "Object marker. 도둑 ends in a consonant, so ~을 is used: 도둑을 (the thief [object]).", "example_in_sentence": "도둑을"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었다 (past, plain)", "exp": "Past tense in plain written style. 붙잡다 → 붙잡았다 (grabbed).", "example_in_sentence": "붙잡았다"}]}, {"text": "그리고 도둑의 목을 조였다.", "translation": "Then she applied a choke hold around his neck.", "vocab": [{"ko": "목", "en": "neck; throat", "note": "body part"}, {"ko": "조이다", "en": "to tighten; to constrict; to squeeze", "note": "applied to neck here = choke"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~의", "exp": "Possessive marker. Noun + 의 = ''s / of. 도둑의 목 = the thief''s neck.", "example_in_sentence": "도둑의"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를", "exp": "Object marker. 목 ends in a consonant, so ~을: 목을 (the neck [object]).", "example_in_sentence": "목을"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었다 (past, plain)", "exp": "Past tense in plain written style. 조이다 → 조였다 (tightened); 이 + 었 combine into 였.", "example_in_sentence": "조였다"}]}, {"text": "도둑은 도망치지 못했다.", "translation": "The thief could not escape.", "vocab": [{"ko": "도둑", "en": "thief", "note": "person who steals"}, {"ko": "도망치다", "en": "to run away; to escape", "note": "flee from a place or situation"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는", "exp": "Topic marker. 도둑 ends in a consonant, so ~은: 도둑은 (as for the thief / the thief [topic]).", "example_in_sentence": "도둑은"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~지 못하다", "exp": "Inability negation. Verb stem + 지 못하다 = cannot (due to inability or external prevention). 도망치다 → 도망치지 못하다. Past plain style: 도망치지 못했다 (could not escape).", "example_in_sentence": "도망치지 못했다"}]}, {"text": "여성이 놓아 주지 않았기 때문이다.", "translation": "It was because the woman did not let go.", "vocab": [{"ko": "놓다", "en": "to let go; to release; to put down", "note": "release grip here"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어 주다", "exp": "Doing something for someone. 놓다 → 놓아 주다 (let go, release); here it is negated: 놓아 주지 않았다.", "example_in_sentence": "놓아 주지 않았기"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~지 않다", "exp": "Standard negation. Verb stem + 지 않다 = do not. 놓아 주다 → 놓아 주지 않다 (did not let go). Past: 놓아 주지 않았다.", "example_in_sentence": "놓아 주지 않았기"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~기 때문이다", "exp": "Gives the reason at the end of a sentence: ''it is because ~''. 않다 → 않았기 때문이다 (because she did not).", "example_in_sentence": "않았기 때문이다"}]}, {"text": "여성은 도둑을 끝까지 잡고 있었다.", "translation": "The woman held onto the thief until the very end.", "vocab": [{"ko": "끝까지", "en": "until the very end; all the way", "note": "끝 (end) + 까지 (until)"}, {"ko": "잡다", "en": "to catch; to hold; to grab", "note": "here: to hold onto"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있다", "exp": "Continuous / progressive aspect. Verb stem + 고 있다 = to be doing. 잡다 → 잡고 있다 (is holding). Past continuous: 잡고 있었다 (was holding / was holding on).", "example_in_sentence": "잡고 있었다"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~까지", "exp": "''Until / up to / as far as''. Noun + 까지. 끝까지 = until the end / all the way to the end.", "example_in_sentence": "끝까지"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "여성", "en": "woman", "note": "adult female"}, {"ko": "도둑", "en": "thief", "note": "person who steals"}, {"ko": "직접", "en": "directly; oneself; in person", "note": "adverb meaning ''by one''s own action''"}, {"ko": "잡다", "en": "to catch; to grab", "note": "physical apprehension"}, {"ko": "도망치다", "en": "to run away; to escape", "note": "flee from a place or situation"}, {"ko": "붙잡다", "en": "to grab; to seize; to hold onto", "note": "stronger/firmer form of 잡다"}, {"ko": "목", "en": "neck; throat", "note": "body part"}, {"ko": "조이다", "en": "to tighten; to constrict; to squeeze", "note": "applied to neck here = choke"}, {"ko": "놓다", "en": "to let go; to release; to put down", "note": "release grip here"}, {"ko": "끝까지", "en": "until the very end; all the way", "note": "끝 (end) + 까지 (until)"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~이/가", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Subject marker. 여성 ends in a consonant, so 이 is used: 여성이 (a woman).", "ex_ko": "한 여성이 도둑을 직접 잡았다.", "ex_en": "A woman caught a thief herself."}, {"name": "~을/를", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Object marker. Attaches to the object noun. 도둑 ends in a consonant, so ~을 is used: 도둑을 (the thief [object]).", "ex_ko": "한 여성이 도둑을 직접 잡았다.", "ex_en": "A woman caught a thief herself."}, {"name": "~았/었다 (past, plain)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Past tense in plain written style. 조이다 → 조였다 (tightened); 이 + 었 combine into 였.", "ex_ko": "한 여성이 도둑을 직접 잡았다.", "ex_en": "A woman caught a thief herself."}, {"name": "~은/는", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Topic marker. 여성 ends in a consonant, so ~은 is used: 여성은 (as for the woman / the woman [topic]).", "ex_ko": "여성은 도둑이 도망치지 못하게 했다.", "ex_en": "She made sure the thief could not escape."}, {"name": "~지 못하다", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Inability negation. Verb stem + 지 못하다 = cannot (due to inability or external prevention). 도망치다 → 도망치지 못하다. Past plain style: 도망치지 못했다 (could not escape).", "ex_ko": "여성은 도둑이 도망치지 못하게 했다.", "ex_en": "She made sure the thief could not escape."}, {"name": "~게 하다", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Causative construction meaning ''make/let someone do/be (a certain way)''. [V/A] + 게 하다. Here: 도망치지 못하게 하다 = make it so (the thief) cannot escape. Past: 했다.", "ex_ko": "여성은 도둑이 도망치지 못하게 했다.", "ex_en": "She made sure the thief could not escape."}, {"name": "~의", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Possessive marker. Noun + 의 = ''s / of. 도둑의 목 = the thief''s neck.", "ex_ko": "그리고 도둑의 목을 조였다.", "ex_en": "Then she applied a choke hold around his neck."}, {"name": "~아/어 주다", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Doing something for someone. 놓다 → 놓아 주다 (let go, release); here it is negated: 놓아 주지 않았다.", "ex_ko": "여성이 놓아 주지 않았기 때문이다.", "ex_en": "It was because the woman did not let go."}, {"name": "~지 않다", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Standard negation. Verb stem + 지 않다 = do not. 놓아 주다 → 놓아 주지 않다 (did not let go). Past: 놓아 주지 않았다.", "ex_ko": "여성이 놓아 주지 않았기 때문이다.", "ex_en": "It was because the woman did not let go."}, {"name": "~기 때문이다", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Gives the reason at the end of a sentence: ''it is because ~''. 않다 → 않았기 때문이다 (because she did not).", "ex_ko": "여성이 놓아 주지 않았기 때문이다.", "ex_en": "It was because the woman did not let go."}, {"name": "~고 있다", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Continuous / progressive aspect. Verb stem + 고 있다 = to be doing. 잡다 → 잡고 있다 (is holding). Past continuous: 잡고 있었다 (was holding / was holding on).", "ex_ko": "여성은 도둑을 끝까지 잡고 있었다.", "ex_en": "The woman held onto the thief until the very end."}, {"name": "~까지", "level": "Starter", "exp": "''Until / up to / as far as''. Noun + 까지. 끝까지 = until the end / all the way to the end.", "ex_ko": "여성은 도둑을 끝까지 잡고 있었다.", "ex_en": "The woman held onto the thief until the very end."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mpe7p1czwop8' and md5(translation) = '42006c43e770137228c1a1b7a1f85618';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["In 1921, there was a police officer in Warsaw, Poland. That police officer wore experimental body armor.", "The experimental body armor was different from regular armor. It was a new kind of protective equipment.", "Warsaw is a city in Poland. 1921 was about 100 years ago.", "The photograph is a historical record. Through that photograph, we can see the equipment of a police officer from long ago."], "sentences": [{"text": "1921년, 폴란드 바르샤바에 경찰관이 있었다.", "translation": "In 1921, there was a police officer in Warsaw, Poland.", "vocab": [{"ko": "경찰관", "en": "police officer", "note": "경찰 (police) + 관 (official)"}, {"ko": "있다", "en": "to exist / to be (there)", "note": "existential verb"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에", "exp": "location particle. Marks where something exists. Noun + 에 indicates a place. 바르샤바 (Warsaw) + 에 = in Warsaw.", "example_in_sentence": "바르샤바에"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가", "exp": "subject marker. Attaches to the subject of the sentence. 경찰관 ends in a consonant (ㄴ), so 이 is used: 경찰관 + 이 = 경찰관이.", "example_in_sentence": "경찰관이"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었다 (past, plain)", "exp": "Past tense in plain written style. 있다 → 있었다 (there was).", "example_in_sentence": "있었다"}]}, {"text": "그 경찰관은 실험용 방어구를 입었다.", "translation": "That police officer wore experimental body armor.", "vocab": [{"ko": "실험용", "en": "experimental / for testing", "note": "실험 (experiment) + 용 (for use)"}, {"ko": "방어구", "en": "body armor / protective gear", "note": "방어 (defense) + 구 (equipment)"}, {"ko": "입다", "en": "to wear (clothing)", "note": "used for clothing worn on the body"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는", "exp": "topic marker. Marks the topic of the sentence. 경찰관 ends in a consonant, so 은 is used: 경찰관 + 은 = 경찰관은.", "example_in_sentence": "경찰관은"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를", "exp": "object marker. Marks the direct object. 방어구 ends in a vowel, so 를 is used: 방어구 + 를 = 방어구를.", "example_in_sentence": "방어구를"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었다 (past, plain)", "exp": "Past tense in plain written style. 입다 → 입었다 (wore).", "example_in_sentence": "입었다"}]}, {"text": "실험용 방어구는 일반 방어구와 달랐다.", "translation": "The experimental body armor was different from regular armor.", "vocab": [{"ko": "일반", "en": "regular / ordinary / general", "note": ""}, {"ko": "다르다", "en": "to be different", "note": "르 irregular verb"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~과/와", "exp": "comitative/comparative particle meaning ''with'' or ''from.'' 방어구 ends in a vowel, so 와 is used: 방어구 + 와 = 방어구와. Used here in comparison: ''different from regular armor.''", "example_in_sentence": "방어구와"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "르 불규칙 (르 irregular)", "exp": "다르다 is 르-irregular: before 아/어 the ㅡ drops and an extra ㄹ appears. 다르다 → 달랐다 (was different).", "example_in_sentence": "달랐다"}]}, {"text": "그것은 새로운 종류의 보호 장비였다.", "translation": "It was a new kind of protective equipment.", "vocab": [{"ko": "새롭다", "en": "to be new", "note": "ㅂ-irregular adjective"}, {"ko": "종류", "en": "kind / type / sort", "note": ""}, {"ko": "보호", "en": "protection", "note": ""}, {"ko": "장비", "en": "equipment / gear", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "ㅂ 불규칙 (ㅂ → 우/오)", "exp": "ㅂ-irregular adjective. When 새롭다 is followed by a vowel ending (~은), the ㅂ changes to 우: 새롭 + 은 → 새로운. Here it modifies the noun 종류.", "example_in_sentence": "새로운"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄴ/은", "exp": "adnominal (modifier) ending for adjectives. Attaches to an adjective stem to modify a noun. 새롭다 (ㅂ-irregular) → 새로운 종류 (a new kind).", "example_in_sentence": "새로운 종류"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~의", "exp": "possessive/linking particle. Connects two nouns. 종류 + 의 = 종류의, linking 종류 (kind) to 보호 장비 (protective equipment).", "example_in_sentence": "종류의"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~였다 (past of 이다)", "exp": "Past of 이다 (to be) in plain style. After a vowel, 이었다 shortens to 였다: 장비였다 (was equipment).", "example_in_sentence": "장비였다"}]}, {"text": "바르샤바는 폴란드의 도시다.", "translation": "Warsaw is a city in Poland.", "vocab": [{"ko": "도시", "en": "city", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~의", "exp": "possessive particle. Connects two nouns. 폴란드 + 의 = 폴란드의, meaning ''of Poland'' or ''Poland''s.''", "example_in_sentence": "폴란드의"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는", "exp": "topic marker. Marks the topic of the sentence. 바르샤바 ends in a vowel, so 는 is used: 바르샤바 + 는 = 바르샤바는.", "example_in_sentence": "바르샤바는"}]}, {"text": "1921년은 약 100년 전이다.", "translation": "1921 was about 100 years ago.", "vocab": [{"ko": "약", "en": "about / approximately", "note": "used before numbers"}, {"ko": "전", "en": "before / ago", "note": "시간 전 = time ago"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는", "exp": "topic marker. 1921년 ends in ㄴ (consonant), so 은 is used: 1921년 + 은 = 1921년은.", "example_in_sentence": "1921년은"}]}, {"text": "그 사진은 역사적인 기록이다.", "translation": "The photograph is a historical record.", "vocab": [{"ko": "사진", "en": "photograph / photo", "note": ""}, {"ko": "역사적", "en": "historical", "note": "역사 (history) + 적 (-ic/-al suffix)"}, {"ko": "기록", "en": "record", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~적", "exp": "Sino-Korean adjectival suffix meaning ''-ic'' or ''-al.'' Attaches to a noun stem: 역사 (history) + 적 = 역사적 (historical). To modify a noun, add 인: 역사적 + 인 = 역사적인 기록.", "example_in_sentence": "역사적인"}]}, {"text": "우리는 그 사진으로 옛날 경찰관의 장비를 볼 수 있다.", "translation": "Through that photograph, we can see the equipment of a police officer from long ago.", "vocab": [{"ko": "옛날", "en": "the old days / long ago", "note": ""}, {"ko": "보다", "en": "to see / to look at", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)로", "exp": "means/instrument particle. Indicates the means or method. 사진 ends in a consonant (ㄴ), so 으로 is used: 사진 + 으로 = 사진으로 (through/by means of the photograph).", "example_in_sentence": "사진으로"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~의", "exp": "possessive particle. 경찰관 + 의 = 경찰관의 (the police officer''s). Connects 경찰관 to 장비 (equipment).", "example_in_sentence": "경찰관의"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를", "exp": "object marker. 장비 ends in a vowel, so 를 is used: 장비 + 를 = 장비를. Marks 장비 as the direct object of 보다.", "example_in_sentence": "장비를"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다/없다 (ability/possibility)", "exp": "expresses ability or possibility: ''can / is able to.'' V-stem + ㄹ/을 수 있다. 보다 → 볼 + 수 있다 = 볼 수 있다 (can see).", "example_in_sentence": "볼 수 있다"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "경찰관", "en": "police officer", "note": "경찰 (police) + 관 (official)"}, {"ko": "있다", "en": "to exist / to be (there)", "note": "existential verb"}, {"ko": "실험용", "en": "experimental / for testing", "note": "실험 (experiment) + 용 (for use)"}, {"ko": "방어구", "en": "body armor / protective gear", "note": "방어 (defense) + 구 (equipment)"}, {"ko": "입다", "en": "to wear (clothing)", "note": "used for clothing worn on the body"}, {"ko": "일반", "en": "regular / ordinary / general", "note": ""}, {"ko": "다르다", "en": "to be different", "note": "르 irregular verb"}, {"ko": "새롭다", "en": "to be new", "note": "ㅂ-irregular adjective"}, {"ko": "종류", "en": "kind / type / sort", "note": ""}, {"ko": "보호", "en": "protection", "note": ""}, {"ko": "장비", "en": "equipment / gear", "note": ""}, {"ko": "도시", "en": "city", "note": ""}, {"ko": "약", "en": "about / approximately", "note": "used before numbers"}, {"ko": "전", "en": "before / ago", "note": "시간 전 = time ago"}, {"ko": "사진", "en": "photograph / photo", "note": ""}, {"ko": "역사적", "en": "historical", "note": "역사 (history) + 적 (-ic/-al suffix)"}, {"ko": "기록", "en": "record", "note": ""}, {"ko": "옛날", "en": "the old days / long ago", "note": ""}, {"ko": "보다", "en": "to see / to look at", "note": ""}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~에", "level": "Starter", "exp": "location particle. Marks where something exists. Noun + 에 indicates a place. 바르샤바 (Warsaw) + 에 = in Warsaw.", "ex_ko": "1921년, 폴란드 바르샤바에 경찰관이 있었다.", "ex_en": "In 1921, there was a police officer in Warsaw, Poland."}, {"name": "~이/가", "level": "Starter", "exp": "subject marker. Attaches to the subject of the sentence. 경찰관 ends in a consonant (ㄴ), so 이 is used: 경찰관 + 이 = 경찰관이.", "ex_ko": "1921년, 폴란드 바르샤바에 경찰관이 있었다.", "ex_en": "In 1921, there was a police officer in Warsaw, Poland."}, {"name": "~았/었다 (past, plain)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Past tense in plain written style. 있다 → 있었다 (there was).", "ex_ko": "1921년, 폴란드 바르샤바에 경찰관이 있었다.", "ex_en": "In 1921, there was a police officer in Warsaw, Poland."}, {"name": "~은/는", "level": "Starter", "exp": "topic marker. Marks the topic of the sentence. 경찰관 ends in a consonant, so 은 is used: 경찰관 + 은 = 경찰관은.", "ex_ko": "그 경찰관은 실험용 방어구를 입었다.", "ex_en": "That police officer wore experimental body armor."}, {"name": "~을/를", "level": "Starter", "exp": "object marker. 장비 ends in a vowel, so 를 is used: 장비 + 를 = 장비를. Marks 장비 as the direct object of 보다.", "ex_ko": "그 경찰관은 실험용 방어구를 입었다.", "ex_en": "That police officer wore experimental body armor."}, {"name": "~과/와", "level": "Starter", "exp": "comitative/comparative particle meaning ''with'' or ''from.'' 방어구 ends in a vowel, so 와 is used: 방어구 + 와 = 방어구와. Used here in comparison: ''different from regular armor.''", "ex_ko": "실험용 방어구는 일반 방어구와 달랐다.", "ex_en": "The experimental body armor was different from regular armor."}, {"name": "르 불규칙 (르 irregular)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "다르다 is 르-irregular: before 아/어 the ㅡ drops and an extra ㄹ appears. 다르다 → 달랐다 (was different).", "ex_ko": "실험용 방어구는 일반 방어구와 달랐다.", "ex_en": "The experimental body armor was different from regular armor."}, {"name": "ㅂ 불규칙 (ㅂ → 우/오)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "ㅂ-irregular adjective. When 새롭다 is followed by a vowel ending (~은), the ㅂ changes to 우: 새롭 + 은 → 새로운. Here it modifies the noun 종류.", "ex_ko": "그것은 새로운 종류의 보호 장비였다.", "ex_en": "It was a new kind of protective equipment."}, {"name": "~ㄴ/은", "level": "Starter", "exp": "adnominal (modifier) ending for adjectives. Attaches to an adjective stem to modify a noun. 새롭다 (ㅂ-irregular) → 새로운 종류 (a new kind).", "ex_ko": "그것은 새로운 종류의 보호 장비였다.", "ex_en": "It was a new kind of protective equipment."}, {"name": "~의", "level": "Starter", "exp": "possessive/linking particle. Connects two nouns. 종류 + 의 = 종류의, linking 종류 (kind) to 보호 장비 (protective equipment).", "ex_ko": "그것은 새로운 종류의 보호 장비였다.", "ex_en": "It was a new kind of protective equipment."}, {"name": "~였다 (past of 이다)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Past of 이다 (to be) in plain style. After a vowel, 이었다 shortens to 였다: 장비였다 (was equipment).", "ex_ko": "그것은 새로운 종류의 보호 장비였다.", "ex_en": "It was a new kind of protective equipment."}, {"name": "~적", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Sino-Korean adjectival suffix meaning ''-ic'' or ''-al.'' Attaches to a noun stem: 역사 (history) + 적 = 역사적 (historical). To modify a noun, add 인: 역사적 + 인 = 역사적인 기록.", "ex_ko": "그 사진은 역사적인 기록이다.", "ex_en": "The photograph is a historical record."}, {"name": "~(으)로", "level": "Starter", "exp": "means/instrument particle. Indicates the means or method. 사진 ends in a consonant (ㄴ), so 으로 is used: 사진 + 으로 = 사진으로 (through/by means of the photograph).", "ex_ko": "우리는 그 사진으로 옛날 경찰관의 장비를 볼 수 있다.", "ex_en": "Through that photograph, we can see the equipment of a police officer from long ago."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다/없다 (ability/possibility)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "expresses ability or possibility: ''can / is able to.'' V-stem + ㄹ/을 수 있다. 보다 → 볼 + 수 있다 = 볼 수 있다 (can see).", "ex_ko": "우리는 그 사진으로 옛날 경찰관의 장비를 볼 수 있다.", "ex_en": "Through that photograph, we can see the equipment of a police officer from long ago."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mpe7qbqw84j0' and md5(translation) = 'b897626a0639f7143654b15f1cba3777';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["SS United States is the fastest passenger ship in history. This ship operated from 1952 to 1969.", "The ship''s first voyage was from New York to England. The voyage took 3 days, and the average speed was approximately 66 kilometers per hour.", "This record has never been broken. SS United States remains the fastest passenger ship to this day."], "sentences": [{"text": "SS 유나이티드 스테이츠는 역사상 가장 빠른 여객선이다.", "translation": "SS United States is the fastest passenger ship in history.", "vocab": [{"ko": "여객선", "en": "passenger ship", "note": ""}, {"ko": "빠르다", "en": "fast; quick", "note": ""}, {"ko": "역사", "en": "history", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는 (topic marker)", "exp": "topic particle marking the subject of the sentence as the topic of discussion. attaches to noun. 유나이티드 스테이츠 → 유나이티드 스테이츠는", "example_in_sentence": "SS 유나이티드 스테이츠는"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "역사상 가장 ~", "exp": "collocation meaning ''the most ~ in history''. 역사상 (in history) + 가장 (most) + superlative adjective.", "example_in_sentence": "역사상 가장 빠른"}]}, {"text": "이 배는 1952년부터 1969년까지 운항했다.", "translation": "This ship operated from 1952 to 1969.", "vocab": [{"ko": "배", "en": "ship", "note": ""}, {"ko": "운항하다", "en": "to operate (ship/vessel)", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는 (topic marker)", "exp": "topic particle. attaches to noun to mark topic of sentence. 배 → 배는", "example_in_sentence": "이 배는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~부터 (from)", "exp": "particle indicating starting point in time or sequence. 1952년 → 1952년부터 (from 1952)", "example_in_sentence": "1952년부터"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~까지 (until)", "exp": "particle indicating endpoint in time or sequence. 1969년 → 1969년까지 (until 1969)", "example_in_sentence": "1969년까지"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~부터 ~까지", "exp": "paired particles expressing a time range or duration. from X to Y. 1952년부터 1969년까지 = from 1952 to 1969.", "example_in_sentence": "1952년부터 1969년까지"}]}, {"text": "이 배의 첫 번째 항해는 뉴욕에서 영국까지였다.", "translation": "The ship''s first voyage was from New York to England.", "vocab": [{"ko": "항해", "en": "voyage; sail", "note": ""}, {"ko": "첫 번째", "en": "first", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~의 (possessive)", "exp": "possessive / attributive particle. attaches to noun to show possession or modification. 배 → 배의", "example_in_sentence": "이 배의"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는 (topic marker)", "exp": "topic particle. attaches to noun to mark sentence topic. 항해 → 항해는", "example_in_sentence": "첫 번째 항해는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서 (location/source)", "exp": "particle marking location where action occurs or source of movement. 뉴욕 → 뉴욕에서 (from New York)", "example_in_sentence": "뉴욕에서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~까지 (until)", "exp": "particle marking destination or endpoint. 영국 → 영국까지 (to/until England)", "example_in_sentence": "영국까지"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~에서 ~까지", "exp": "paired particles expressing direction/route from location to location. from X to Y. 뉴욕에서 영국까지 = from New York to England.", "example_in_sentence": "뉴욕에서 영국까지"}]}, {"text": "그 항해는 3일이 걸렸고, 평균 속도는 시속 약 66킬로미터였다.", "translation": "The voyage took 3 days, and the average speed was approximately 66 kilometers per hour.", "vocab": [{"ko": "걸리다", "en": "to take (time); to hang", "note": ""}, {"ko": "평균", "en": "average", "note": ""}, {"ko": "속도", "en": "speed", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는 (topic marker)", "exp": "Topic particle. 항해 → 항해는; 속도 → 속도는 (as for the speed).", "example_in_sentence": "그 항해는"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~이/가 걸리다", "exp": "''It takes (time).'' The time is the subject: 3일이 걸리다 (it takes 3 days) → 3일이 걸렸고 (it took 3 days, and).", "example_in_sentence": "3일이 걸렸고"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 (conjunction)", "exp": "coordinating conjunction joining two clauses of equal weight. 걸렸고 = took (and then...). 걸리다 → 걸렸고", "example_in_sentence": "걸렸고"}]}, {"text": "이 기록은 지금까지 깨지지 않았다.", "translation": "This record has never been broken.", "vocab": [{"ko": "기록", "en": "record", "note": ""}, {"ko": "깨지다", "en": "to break; to be broken", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는 (topic marker)", "exp": "topic particle. attaches to noun. 기록 → 기록은", "example_in_sentence": "이 기록은"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~지 않다 (long-form negation)", "exp": "negation marker. stem + 지 않다 = ''not/do not''. 깨지다 → 깨지지 않다 → 깨지지 않았다 (was not broken).", "example_in_sentence": "깨지지 않았다"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "지금까지 ~지 않았다", "exp": "''Has not ~ until now / to this day''. 지금까지 깨지지 않았다 (has not been broken to this day).", "example_in_sentence": "지금까지 깨지지 않았다"}]}, {"text": "SS 유나이티드 스테이츠는 아직도 가장 빠른 여객선으로 남아 있다.", "translation": "SS United States remains the fastest passenger ship to this day.", "vocab": [{"ko": "남다", "en": "to remain; to stay", "note": ""}, {"ko": "아직", "en": "still; yet", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는 (topic marker)", "exp": "topic particle. attaches to noun. 유나이티드 스테이츠 → 유나이티드 스테이츠는", "example_in_sentence": "SS 유나이티드 스테이츠는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어 있다 (resulting state)", "exp": "Shows a state that continues after an action. 남다 → 남아 있다 (remains, is still there).", "example_in_sentence": "남아 있다"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~로 남다", "exp": "collocation meaning ''to remain as / to stay as''. indicates the state or role something maintains. 가장 빠른 여객선으로 남다 = to remain as the fastest passenger ship.", "example_in_sentence": "가장 빠른 여객선으로 남아"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "아직도 ~", "exp": "adverbial expression meaning ''still'' or ''yet to this day''. emphasizes continuation to the present. 아직 → 아직도 (emphatic form).", "example_in_sentence": "아직도 가장 빠른"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "여객선", "en": "passenger ship", "note": ""}, {"ko": "빠르다", "en": "fast; quick", "note": ""}, {"ko": "역사", "en": "history", "note": ""}, {"ko": "배", "en": "ship", "note": ""}, {"ko": "운항하다", "en": "to operate (ship/vessel)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "항해", "en": "voyage; sail", "note": ""}, {"ko": "첫 번째", "en": "first", "note": ""}, {"ko": "걸리다", "en": "to take (time); to hang", "note": ""}, {"ko": "평균", "en": "average", "note": ""}, {"ko": "속도", "en": "speed", "note": ""}, {"ko": "기록", "en": "record", "note": ""}, {"ko": "깨지다", "en": "to break; to be broken", "note": ""}, {"ko": "남다", "en": "to remain; to stay", "note": ""}, {"ko": "아직", "en": "still; yet", "note": ""}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~은/는 (topic marker)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "topic particle marking the subject of the sentence as the topic of discussion. attaches to noun. 유나이티드 스테이츠 → 유나이티드 스테이츠는", "ex_ko": "SS 유나이티드 스테이츠는 역사상 가장 빠른 여객선이다.", "ex_en": "SS United States is the fastest passenger ship in history."}, {"name": "~부터 (from)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "particle indicating starting point in time or sequence. 1952년 → 1952년부터 (from 1952)", "ex_ko": "이 배는 1952년부터 1969년까지 운항했다.", "ex_en": "This ship operated from 1952 to 1969."}, {"name": "~까지 (until)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "particle indicating endpoint in time or sequence. 1969년 → 1969년까지 (until 1969)", "ex_ko": "이 배는 1952년부터 1969년까지 운항했다.", "ex_en": "This ship operated from 1952 to 1969."}, {"name": "~의 (possessive)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "possessive / attributive particle. attaches to noun to show possession or modification. 배 → 배의", "ex_ko": "이 배의 첫 번째 항해는 뉴욕에서 영국까지였다.", "ex_en": "The ship''s first voyage was from New York to England."}, {"name": "~에서 (location/source)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "particle marking location where action occurs or source of movement. 뉴욕 → 뉴욕에서 (from New York)", "ex_ko": "이 배의 첫 번째 항해는 뉴욕에서 영국까지였다.", "ex_en": "The ship''s first voyage was from New York to England."}, {"name": "~고 (conjunction)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "coordinating conjunction joining two clauses of equal weight. 걸렸고 = took (and then...). 걸리다 → 걸렸고", "ex_ko": "그 항해는 3일이 걸렸고, 평균 속도는 시속 약 66킬로미터였다.", "ex_en": "The voyage took 3 days, and the average speed was approximately 66 kilometers per hour."}, {"name": "~지 않다 (long-form negation)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "negation marker. stem + 지 않다 = ''not/do not''. 깨지다 → 깨지지 않다 → 깨지지 않았다 (was not broken).", "ex_ko": "이 기록은 지금까지 깨지지 않았다.", "ex_en": "This record has never been broken."}, {"name": "~아/어 있다 (resulting state)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Shows a state that continues after an action. 남다 → 남아 있다 (remains, is still there).", "ex_ko": "SS 유나이티드 스테이츠는 아직도 가장 빠른 여객선으로 남아 있다.", "ex_en": "SS United States remains the fastest passenger ship to this day."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mpe7rlsp6aca' and md5(translation) = '85d4963f7c695dc12021a90d277cbaf0';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["Biddy Mason was born in 1818 and came to California in 1851 as an enslaved person. She filed a lawsuit in court to gain her freedom and finally obtained it.", "After gaining her freedom, Biddy purchased land in Los Angeles. She is known as one of the first Black women to own land in that area.", "As the city grew, the value of Biddy''s land increased significantly. As a result, she became a very wealthy woman.", "Biddy Mason passed away in 1891. She not only accumulated wealth but also worked as a renowned philanthropist."], "sentences": [{"text": "비디 메이슨은 1818년에 태어나 1851년 노예 신분으로 캘리포니아에 오게 되었다.", "translation": "Biddy Mason was born in 1818 and came to California in 1851 as an enslaved person.", "vocab": [{"ko": "태어나다", "en": "be born", "note": ""}, {"ko": "노예", "en": "enslaved person / slave", "note": ""}, {"ko": "신분", "en": "status / condition", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~게 되다", "exp": "Shows how a situation came about, often not by one''s own choice. 오다 → 오게 되었다 (came to / ended up coming).", "example_in_sentence": "캘리포니아에 오게 되었다"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)로", "exp": "means / manner / capacity. Marks how or in what capacity something occurs. 신분 (status) + 으로 = 신분으로 (as / in the capacity of enslaved person).", "example_in_sentence": "노예 신분으로"}]}, {"text": "그는 법원에서 자유를 얻기 위해 직접 소송을 제기했고, 마침내 자유를 얻었다.", "translation": "She filed a lawsuit in court to gain her freedom and finally obtained it.", "vocab": [{"ko": "법원", "en": "court", "note": ""}, {"ko": "자유", "en": "freedom", "note": ""}, {"ko": "소송", "en": "lawsuit", "note": ""}, {"ko": "제기하다", "en": "file / lodge", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서", "exp": "location of action. Marks where an action takes place. 법원 (court) + 에서 = 법원에서 (in/at court).", "example_in_sentence": "법원에서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~기 위해(서)", "exp": "purpose / in order to. Infinitive stem + 기 위해 marks the purpose of an action. 얻다 → 얻기 위해 (in order to obtain).", "example_in_sentence": "자유를 얻기 위해"}]}, {"text": "자유를 얻은 후에 비디는 로스앤젤레스에서 토지를 구입했다.", "translation": "After gaining her freedom, Biddy purchased land in Los Angeles.", "vocab": [{"ko": "구입하다", "en": "purchase / buy", "note": ""}, {"ko": "토지", "en": "land", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄴ/은 후에", "exp": "after V-ing. Past participle + 후에 marks a time point after an action is completed. 얻다 → 얻은 후에 (after having obtained).", "example_in_sentence": "자유를 얻은 후에"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서", "exp": "location of action. Marks where an action takes place. 로스앤젤레스 (Los Angeles) + 에서 = 로스앤젤레스에서 (in Los Angeles).", "example_in_sentence": "로스앤젤레스에서"}]}, {"text": "그는 그 지역에서 토지를 소유한 최초의 흑인 여성 중 한 명으로 알려져 있다.", "translation": "She is known as one of the first Black women to own land in that area.", "vocab": [{"ko": "소유하다", "en": "own", "note": ""}, {"ko": "최초", "en": "first / earliest", "note": ""}, {"ko": "흑인", "en": "Black person", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서", "exp": "location / scope of action. Marks the spatial or contextual domain where something occurs. 그 지역 (that area) + 에서 = 그 지역에서 (in that area).", "example_in_sentence": "그 지역에서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄴ/은 (relative clause modifier)", "exp": "relative clause marker. Transforms a clause into a modifier for the following noun. 소유한 (that owns) modifies 여성 (woman).", "example_in_sentence": "토지를 소유한 최초의"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~ 중 한 명", "exp": "''One of (a group of people)''. 최초의 흑인 여성 중 한 명 (one of the first Black women).", "example_in_sentence": "최초의 흑인 여성 중 한 명"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)로 알려져 있다", "exp": "''Is known as''. 알리다 → passive 알려지다 → 알려져 있다 (is known). 한 명으로 = as one (of them).", "example_in_sentence": "한 명으로 알려져 있다"}]}, {"text": "도시가 성장하면서 비디의 토지 가치는 크게 올랐다.", "translation": "As the city grew, the value of Biddy''s land increased significantly.", "vocab": [{"ko": "성장하다", "en": "grow / develop", "note": ""}, {"ko": "가치", "en": "value", "note": ""}, {"ko": "오르다", "en": "rise / increase", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)면서", "exp": "while / as. Simultaneous action marker. Indicates two actions occurring concurrently. 성장하다 + 면서 = 성장하면서 (while growing / as it grows).", "example_in_sentence": "도시가 성장하면서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~게", "exp": "adverbializer suffix. Forms adverbs from adjectives. 크다 (big) → 크게 (greatly / significantly). Modifies the following verb.", "example_in_sentence": "크게 올랐다"}]}, {"text": "그 결과 그는 매우 부유한 여성이 되었다.", "translation": "As a result, she became a very wealthy woman.", "vocab": [{"ko": "결과", "en": "result / consequence", "note": ""}, {"ko": "부유하다", "en": "wealthy / rich", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "그 결과", "exp": "as a result / as a consequence. Fixed expression connecting cause and effect between sentences or clauses.", "example_in_sentence": "그 결과"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가 되다", "exp": "''Become (something)''. 여성 + 이 되다 → 여성이 되었다 (became a woman).", "example_in_sentence": "여성이 되었다"}]}, {"text": "비디 메이슨은 1891년에 세상을 떠났다.", "translation": "Biddy Mason passed away in 1891.", "vocab": [{"ko": "세상", "en": "world / life", "note": ""}, {"ko": "떠나다", "en": "leave / pass away", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "세상을 떠나다", "exp": "pass away / die. Euphemistic idiom for death. Literally ''leave the world.''", "example_in_sentence": "세상을 떠났다"}]}, {"text": "그는 부를 쌓는 것에 그치지 않고 저명한 자선 사업가로도 활동했다.", "translation": "She not only accumulated wealth but also worked as a renowned philanthropist.", "vocab": [{"ko": "부", "en": "wealth", "note": ""}, {"ko": "쌓다", "en": "accumulate / build up", "note": ""}, {"ko": "자선", "en": "charity / philanthropy", "note": ""}, {"ko": "자선 사업가", "en": "philanthropist", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 것", "exp": "Turns a verb phrase into a noun. 쌓다 → 쌓는 것 (building up, accumulating).", "example_in_sentence": "부를 쌓는 것"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에 그치다", "exp": "only / merely / stop at. Limitation marker. <action/state> + 에 그치다 = stops at / is limited to. 쌓는 것에 그치다 (only stopped at accumulating).", "example_in_sentence": "부를 쌓는 것에 그치지 않고"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)로", "exp": "capacity / role / means. Marks the role or capacity in which someone acts. 사업가 (businessperson) + 로 = as a businessperson.", "example_in_sentence": "사업가로도"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~에 그치지 않고 ~도", "exp": "not only... but also. Contrastive structure emphasizing multiple achievements. First clause negated with 그치지 않고, second added with 도.", "example_in_sentence": "부를 쌓는 것에 그치지 않고 저명한 자선 사업가로도 활동했다"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "태어나다", "en": "be born", "note": ""}, {"ko": "노예", "en": "enslaved person / slave", "note": ""}, {"ko": "신분", "en": "status / condition", "note": ""}, {"ko": "법원", "en": "court", "note": ""}, {"ko": "자유", "en": "freedom", "note": ""}, {"ko": "소송", "en": "lawsuit", "note": ""}, {"ko": "제기하다", "en": "file / lodge", "note": ""}, {"ko": "구입하다", "en": "purchase / buy", "note": ""}, {"ko": "토지", "en": "land", "note": ""}, {"ko": "소유하다", "en": "own", "note": ""}, {"ko": "최초", "en": "first / earliest", "note": ""}, {"ko": "흑인", "en": "Black person", "note": ""}, {"ko": "성장하다", "en": "grow / develop", "note": ""}, {"ko": "가치", "en": "value", "note": ""}, {"ko": "오르다", "en": "rise / increase", "note": ""}, {"ko": "결과", "en": "result / consequence", "note": ""}, {"ko": "부유하다", "en": "wealthy / rich", "note": ""}, {"ko": "세상", "en": "world / life", "note": ""}, {"ko": "떠나다", "en": "leave / pass away", "note": ""}, {"ko": "부", "en": "wealth", "note": ""}, {"ko": "쌓다", "en": "accumulate / build up", "note": ""}, {"ko": "자선", "en": "charity / philanthropy", "note": ""}, {"ko": "자선 사업가", "en": "philanthropist", "note": ""}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~게 되다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Shows how a situation came about, often not by one''s own choice. 오다 → 오게 되었다 (came to / ended up coming).", "ex_ko": "비디 메이슨은 1818년에 태어나 1851년 노예 신분으로 캘리포니아에 오게 되었다.", "ex_en": "Biddy Mason was born in 1818 and came to California in 1851 as an enslaved person."}, {"name": "~(으)로", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "means / manner / capacity. Marks how or in what capacity something occurs. 신분 (status) + 으로 = 신분으로 (as / in the capacity of enslaved person).", "ex_ko": "비디 메이슨은 1818년에 태어나 1851년 노예 신분으로 캘리포니아에 오게 되었다.", "ex_en": "Biddy Mason was born in 1818 and came to California in 1851 as an enslaved person."}, {"name": "~에서", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "location / scope of action. Marks the spatial or contextual domain where something occurs. 그 지역 (that area) + 에서 = 그 지역에서 (in that area).", "ex_ko": "그는 법원에서 자유를 얻기 위해 직접 소송을 제기했고, 마침내 자유를 얻었다.", "ex_en": "She filed a lawsuit in court to gain her freedom and finally obtained it."}, {"name": "~기 위해(서)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "purpose / in order to. Infinitive stem + 기 위해 marks the purpose of an action. 얻다 → 얻기 위해 (in order to obtain).", "ex_ko": "그는 법원에서 자유를 얻기 위해 직접 소송을 제기했고, 마침내 자유를 얻었다.", "ex_en": "She filed a lawsuit in court to gain her freedom and finally obtained it."}, {"name": "~ㄴ/은 후에", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "after V-ing. Past participle + 후에 marks a time point after an action is completed. 얻다 → 얻은 후에 (after having obtained).", "ex_ko": "자유를 얻은 후에 비디는 로스앤젤레스에서 토지를 구입했다.", "ex_en": "After gaining her freedom, Biddy purchased land in Los Angeles."}, {"name": "~ㄴ/은 (relative clause modifier)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "relative clause marker. Transforms a clause into a modifier for the following noun. 소유한 (that owns) modifies 여성 (woman).", "ex_ko": "그는 그 지역에서 토지를 소유한 최초의 흑인 여성 중 한 명으로 알려져 있다.", "ex_en": "She is known as one of the first Black women to own land in that area."}, {"name": "~ 중 한 명", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "''One of (a group of people)''. 최초의 흑인 여성 중 한 명 (one of the first Black women).", "ex_ko": "그는 그 지역에서 토지를 소유한 최초의 흑인 여성 중 한 명으로 알려져 있다.", "ex_en": "She is known as one of the first Black women to own land in that area."}, {"name": "~(으)로 알려져 있다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "''Is known as''. 알리다 → passive 알려지다 → 알려져 있다 (is known). 한 명으로 = as one (of them).", "ex_ko": "그는 그 지역에서 토지를 소유한 최초의 흑인 여성 중 한 명으로 알려져 있다.", "ex_en": "She is known as one of the first Black women to own land in that area."}, {"name": "~(으)면서", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "while / as. Simultaneous action marker. Indicates two actions occurring concurrently. 성장하다 + 면서 = 성장하면서 (while growing / as it grows).", "ex_ko": "도시가 성장하면서 비디의 토지 가치는 크게 올랐다.", "ex_en": "As the city grew, the value of Biddy''s land increased significantly."}, {"name": "~게", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "adverbializer suffix. Forms adverbs from adjectives. 크다 (big) → 크게 (greatly / significantly). Modifies the following verb.", "ex_ko": "도시가 성장하면서 비디의 토지 가치는 크게 올랐다.", "ex_en": "As the city grew, the value of Biddy''s land increased significantly."}, {"name": "~이/가 되다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "''Become (something)''. 여성 + 이 되다 → 여성이 되었다 (became a woman).", "ex_ko": "그 결과 그는 매우 부유한 여성이 되었다.", "ex_en": "As a result, she became a very wealthy woman."}, {"name": "~는 것", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Turns a verb phrase into a noun. 쌓다 → 쌓는 것 (building up, accumulating).", "ex_ko": "그는 부를 쌓는 것에 그치지 않고 저명한 자선 사업가로도 활동했다.", "ex_en": "She not only accumulated wealth but also worked as a renowned philanthropist."}, {"name": "~에 그치다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "only / merely / stop at. Limitation marker. <action/state> + 에 그치다 = stops at / is limited to. 쌓는 것에 그치다 (only stopped at accumulating).", "ex_ko": "그는 부를 쌓는 것에 그치지 않고 저명한 자선 사업가로도 활동했다.", "ex_en": "She not only accumulated wealth but also worked as a renowned philanthropist."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mpe7t30dx82r' and md5(translation) = '4c7807a075671de80fba500121b61460';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["During World War II, Britain hid vast treasures in the basement of the Sun Life Building in Montreal, Canada on the third underground level. The nation moved its wealth to a safe location in preparation for a German invasion.", "This vault was made with extreme sophistication. The walls were constructed from decommissioned railroad steel, and two people had to simultaneously enter a code to open the vault door. Both individuals had to operate without knowing each other''s passwords.", "A microphone alarm system was also installed inside the vault. Because an alarm could be triggered by even the slightest sound, the security level was extremely high.", "120 secret staff members participated in this operation. After taking strict confidentiality oaths, they worked to classify assets worth billions of dollars inside the vault. All employees maintained their oaths to ensure that the entire operation remained thoroughly concealed."], "sentences": [{"text": "제2차 세계대전 중, 영국은 막대한 재산을 캐나다 몬트리올의 선 라이프 빌딩 지하 3층에 숨겼다.", "translation": "During World War II, Britain hid a vast fortune on the third basement level of the Sun Life Building in Montreal, Canada.", "vocab": [{"ko": "제2차 세계대전", "en": "World War II", "note": "Sino-Korean: 第二次 世界大戰"}, {"ko": "막대하다", "en": "vast; enormous", "note": "adjective; can also be written 막대한"}, {"ko": "재산", "en": "wealth, property, treasure", "note": "Sino-Korean noun"}, {"ko": "숨기다", "en": "hide, conceal", "note": "past tense: 숨겼다"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "독일의 침공에 대비하기 위해 국가의 부를 안전한 곳으로 옮긴 것이다.", "translation": "Britain moved the nation''s wealth to a safe place to prepare for a German invasion.", "vocab": [{"ko": "침공", "en": "invasion, attack", "note": "Sino-Korean noun"}, {"ko": "대비하다", "en": "prepare for, be ready for", "note": "verb; 대비 (preparation) + 하다"}, {"ko": "국가", "en": "nation, country, state", "note": "Sino-Korean noun"}, {"ko": "옮기다", "en": "move, transfer, shift", "note": "past participle: 옮긴"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~기 위해(서)", "exp": "''In order to''. 대비하다 → 대비하기 위해 (in order to prepare for).", "example_in_sentence": "대비하기 위해"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)로 (direction)", "exp": "Marks direction: ''to''. 안전한 곳 → 안전한 곳으로 (to a safe place).", "example_in_sentence": "안전한 곳으로"}]}, {"text": "이 금고는 매우 정교하게 만들어졌다.", "translation": "This vault was made with extreme sophistication.", "vocab": [{"ko": "금고", "en": "vault, safe", "note": "compound: 금 (metal/gold) + 고 (safe)"}, {"ko": "정교하다", "en": "sophisticated, elaborate, intricate", "note": "adjective; Sino-Korean"}, {"ko": "만들다", "en": "make, construct, build", "note": "past participle: 만들어졌다"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어지다 (passive)", "exp": "만들다 (make) → 만들어지다 (be made) → 만들어졌다 (was made). 정교하게 = elaborately.", "example_in_sentence": "만들어졌다"}]}, {"text": "벽은 폐철도 강철로 만들어졌으며, 금고 문을 열기 위해서는 두 명이 동시에 암호를 입력해야 했다.", "translation": "The walls were constructed from decommissioned railroad steel, and two people had to simultaneously enter a code to open the vault door.", "vocab": [{"ko": "벽", "en": "wall", "note": "native Korean noun"}, {"ko": "폐철도", "en": "decommissioned railroad", "note": "Sino-Korean: 廃 (disused) + 鐵道 (railroad)"}, {"ko": "강철", "en": "steel", "note": "Sino-Korean: 鋼鐵"}, {"ko": "암호", "en": "code, password, cipher", "note": "Sino-Korean: 暗號"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)로 (means/direction)", "exp": "instrumental postposition. <noun> + 으로/로 = ''with / by means of / from''. 강철 + 로 = ''with steel / from steel''.", "example_in_sentence": "강철로 만들어졌으며"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~기 위해(서) (in order to)", "exp": "purposive connector. <verb-stem> + 기 위해 = ''in order to / for the purpose of''. 열다 → 열기 위해 = ''in order to open''.", "example_in_sentence": "열기 위해서는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어야 하다/되다 (must)", "exp": "obligation/necessity modal. <verb-stem> + 아/어야 하다 = ''must / have to''. 입력하다 → 입력해야 했다 = ''had to enter'' (vowel contraction: -하다 → -해야).", "example_in_sentence": "입력해야 했다"}]}, {"text": "두 명 모두 서로의 암호를 알지 못한 채 작동해야 했다.", "translation": "Both individuals had to operate without knowing each other''s passwords.", "vocab": [{"ko": "모두", "en": "all, both, everyone", "note": "native Korean; can follow noun + particle"}, {"ko": "서로", "en": "each other, mutually, reciprocally", "note": "native Korean adverb"}, {"ko": "작동하다", "en": "operate, function, work", "note": "Sino-Korean verb: 作動"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~지 못하다 (inability/negation)", "exp": "negative ability marker. <verb-stem> + 지 못하다 = ''cannot / fail to / unable to''. 알다 → 알지 못하다 = ''unable to know / did not know''. Different from 못 + verb.", "example_in_sentence": "알지 못한 채"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어야 하다/되다 (must)", "exp": "obligation modal. <verb-stem> + 아/어야 하다 = ''must / have to''. 작동하다 → 작동해야 했다 = ''had to operate'' (vowel contraction: -하다 → -해야).", "example_in_sentence": "작동해야 했다"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~(으)ㄴ 채(로)", "exp": "''In the state of / while still ~''. 알지 못하다 → 알지 못한 채 (without knowing).", "example_in_sentence": "알지 못한 채"}]}, {"text": "금고 내부에는 마이크로폰 경보 장치도 설치되어 있었다.", "translation": "A microphone alarm system was also installed inside the vault.", "vocab": [{"ko": "내부", "en": "interior, inside", "note": "Sino-Korean: 內部"}, {"ko": "마이크로폰", "en": "microphone", "note": "English loanword"}, {"ko": "경보", "en": "alarm, warning", "note": "Sino-Korean: 警報"}, {"ko": "장치", "en": "device, apparatus, system", "note": "Sino-Korean: 裝置"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어 있다 (resulting state)", "exp": "Shows a state that continues after an action. 설치되다 (be installed) → 설치되어 있었다 (was installed, was in place).", "example_in_sentence": "설치되어 있었다"}]}, {"text": "아주 작은 소리에도 경보가 울릴 수 있었기 때문에 보안 수준이 매우 높았다.", "translation": "Because an alarm could be triggered by even the slightest sound, the security level was extremely high.", "vocab": [{"ko": "소리", "en": "sound, noise, voice", "note": "native Korean noun"}, {"ko": "울리다", "en": "ring, sound, be triggered", "note": "causative of 울다; past potential: 울릴 수 있었다"}, {"ko": "보안", "en": "security", "note": "Sino-Korean: 保安"}, {"ko": "수준", "en": "level, standard, degree", "note": "Sino-Korean: 水準"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다/없다 (ability/possibility)", "exp": "potentiality modal. <verb-stem> + ㄹ/을 수 있다 = ''can / be able to / possible''. 울리다 → 울릴 수 있었다 = ''could be triggered / was able to be triggered''.", "example_in_sentence": "울릴 수 있었기"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~기 때문에", "exp": "''Because''. 있다 → 있었기 때문에; 울릴 수 있었기 때문에 (because it could go off).", "example_in_sentence": "울릴 수 있었기 때문에"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에도 (even)", "exp": "도 here means ''even''. 아주 작은 소리에도 (even at a very small sound).", "example_in_sentence": "소리에도"}]}, {"text": "이 작전에는 120명의 비밀 직원이 참여했다.", "translation": "120 secret staff members participated in this operation.", "vocab": [{"ko": "작전", "en": "operation, mission, plan", "note": "Sino-Korean: 作戰"}, {"ko": "비밀", "en": "secret, confidential", "note": "Sino-Korean: 秘密"}, {"ko": "직원", "en": "staff member, employee", "note": "Sino-Korean: 職員"}, {"ko": "참여하다", "en": "participate, take part", "note": "Sino-Korean verb: 參與"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "이들은 엄격한 비밀 서약을 한 후에 금고 안에서 수십억 달러 규모의 자산을 분류하는 작업을 했다.", "translation": "After taking strict confidentiality oaths, they worked to classify assets worth billions of dollars inside the vault.", "vocab": [{"ko": "엄격하다", "en": "strict, severe, rigid", "note": "Sino-Korean adjective: 嚴格"}, {"ko": "서약", "en": "oath, pledge, vow", "note": "Sino-Korean: 誓約"}, {"ko": "규모", "en": "scale, scope, size", "note": "Sino-Korean: 規模"}, {"ko": "자산", "en": "asset, property, wealth", "note": "Sino-Korean: 資産"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서 (location/source)", "exp": "locational/source postposition. <noun> + 에서 = ''at / in / from (location of action)''. 금고 안 + 에서 = ''inside the vault / from within the vault''.", "example_in_sentence": "금고 안에서"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~(으)ㄴ 후에", "exp": "''After doing''. 하다 → 한 후에; 서약을 한 후에 (after taking an oath).", "example_in_sentence": "서약을 한 후에"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~ 규모의 N", "exp": "''Of (a size / scale)'' before a noun. 수십억 달러 규모의 자산 (assets worth billions of dollars).", "example_in_sentence": "수십억 달러 규모의 자산"}]}, {"text": "작전 전체가 철저히 숨겨지도록 하기 위해 모든 직원이 서약을 지켰다.", "translation": "All employees maintained their oaths to ensure that the entire operation remained thoroughly concealed.", "vocab": [{"ko": "전체", "en": "whole, entire, all", "note": "Sino-Korean: 全體"}, {"ko": "철저히", "en": "thoroughly, completely, strictly", "note": "Sino-Korean adverb: 徹底"}, {"ko": "숨겨지다", "en": "to be hidden", "note": "infinitive: 숨겨지다 (passive)"}, {"ko": "지키다", "en": "keep, maintain, observe, follow", "note": "native Korean verb"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~기 위해(서) (in order to)", "exp": "purposive connector. <verb-stem> + 기 위해 = ''in order to / for the sake of''. 하다 → 하기 위해 = ''in order to do''.", "example_in_sentence": "숨겨지도록 하기 위해"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~도록 하다", "exp": "''Make sure that / so that ~''. 숨겨지다 → 숨겨지도록 하다 (make sure it stays hidden).", "example_in_sentence": "숨겨지도록 하기"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~히 (adverb ending)", "exp": "Adverb ending for many Sino-Korean words. 철저하다 → 철저히 (thoroughly).", "example_in_sentence": "철저히"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "제2차 세계대전", "en": "World War II", "note": "Sino-Korean: 第二次 世界大戰"}, {"ko": "막대하다", "en": "vast; enormous", "note": "adjective; can also be written 막대한"}, {"ko": "재산", "en": "wealth, property, treasure", "note": "Sino-Korean noun"}, {"ko": "숨기다", "en": "hide, conceal", "note": "past tense: 숨겼다"}, {"ko": "침공", "en": "invasion, attack", "note": "Sino-Korean noun"}, {"ko": "대비하다", "en": "prepare for, be ready for", "note": "verb; 대비 (preparation) + 하다"}, {"ko": "국가", "en": "nation, count