ex_ko": "두 명 모두 서로의 암호를 알지 못한 채 작동해야 했다.", "ex_en": "Both individuals had to operate without knowing each other''s passwords."}, {"name": "~아/어 있다 (resulting state)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Shows a state that continues after an action. 설치되다 (be installed) → 설치되어 있었다 (was installed, was in place).", "ex_ko": "금고 내부에는 마이크로폰 경보 장치도 설치되어 있었다.", "ex_en": "A microphone alarm system was also installed inside the vault."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다/없다 (ability/possibility)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "potentiality modal. <verb-stem> + ㄹ/을 수 있다 = ''can / be able to / possible''. 울리다 → 울릴 수 있었다 = ''could be triggered / was able to be triggered''.", "ex_ko": "아주 작은 소리에도 경보가 울릴 수 있었기 때문에 보안 수준이 매우 높았다.", "ex_en": "Because an alarm could be triggered by even the slightest sound, the security level was extremely high."}, {"name": "~기 때문에", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "''Because''. 있다 → 있었기 때문에; 울릴 수 있었기 때문에 (because it could go off).", "ex_ko": "아주 작은 소리에도 경보가 울릴 수 있었기 때문에 보안 수준이 매우 높았다.", "ex_en": "Because an alarm could be triggered by even the slightest sound, the security level was extremely high."}, {"name": "~에도 (even)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "도 here means ''even''. 아주 작은 소리에도 (even at a very small sound).", "ex_ko": "아주 작은 소리에도 경보가 울릴 수 있었기 때문에 보안 수준이 매우 높았다.", "ex_en": "Because an alarm could be triggered by even the slightest sound, the security level was extremely high."}, {"name": "~에서 (location/source)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "locational/source postposition. <noun> + 에서 = ''at / in / from (location of action)''. 금고 안 + 에서 = ''inside the vault / from within the vault''.", "ex_ko": "이들은 엄격한 비밀 서약을 한 후에 금고 안에서 수십억 달러 규모의 자산을 분류하는 작업을 했다.", "ex_en": "After taking strict confidentiality oaths, they worked to classify assets worth billions of dollars inside the vault."}, {"name": "~도록 하다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "''Make sure that / so that ~''. 숨겨지다 → 숨겨지도록 하다 (make sure it stays hidden).", "ex_ko": "작전 전체가 철저히 숨겨지도록 하기 위해 모든 직원이 서약을 지켰다.", "ex_en": "All employees maintained their oaths to ensure that the entire operation remained thoroughly concealed."}, {"name": "~히 (adverb ending)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Adverb ending for many Sino-Korean words. 철저하다 → 철저히 (thoroughly).", "ex_ko": "작전 전체가 철저히 숨겨지도록 하기 위해 모든 직원이 서약을 지켰다.", "ex_en": "All employees maintained their oaths to ensure that the entire operation remained thoroughly concealed."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mpe7uvc34r28' and md5(translation) = '851e7ec2a2aa367508f82fca3eb37c54';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["Nakahama Manjiro is known as the first Japanese person to visit the United States. At the age of 14, he set out to sea on a fishing boat and was shipwrecked.", "It was an American whaling ship that rescued the drifting Manjiro. After being saved, he came to join the crew of that ship.", "While working as a crew member, Manjiro experienced life in the United States. He later took part in the California Gold Rush as well.", "After ten years had passed, Manjiro returned to Japan. Upon his return, he was granted samurai status and was also appointed as an official interpreter."], "sentences": [{"text": "나카하마 만지로는 미국을 방문한 최초의 일본인으로 알려져 있다.", "translation": "Nakahama Manjiro is known as the first Japanese person to visit the United States.", "vocab": [{"ko": "방문하다", "en": "to visit", "note": "used for visiting places or people"}, {"ko": "최초", "en": "the very first; the earliest", "note": "Sino-Korean noun, often used in formal/news writing"}, {"ko": "알려지다", "en": "to be known; to become known", "note": "passive form of 알리다 (to make known)"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)로 알려지다 / 알려져 있다 (be known as)", "exp": "~(으)로 알려져 있다 = ''to be known as''. 알리다 → passive 알려지다 + 있다 (resultant state). The particle (으)로 marks the role or title.", "example_in_sentence": "일본인으로 알려져 있다"}]}, {"text": "그는 14세에 어선을 타고 바다에 나갔다가 난파를 당했다.", "translation": "At the age of 14, he set out to sea on a fishing boat and was shipwrecked.", "vocab": [{"ko": "어선", "en": "fishing boat", "note": "Sino-Korean compound: 어(漁) fish + 선(船) boat"}, {"ko": "나가다", "en": "to go out; to head out", "note": "directional verb away from a base point"}, {"ko": "난파", "en": "shipwreck", "note": "난파를 당하다 = to be shipwrecked (suffer a shipwreck)"}, {"ko": "당하다", "en": "to suffer; to undergo (something bad)", "note": "used when the subject is the victim of an event"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었다가", "exp": "One action is done, then something else happens. 나가다 → 나갔다가 (went out (to sea), and then ...).", "example_in_sentence": "나갔다가"}]}, {"text": "표류 중이던 만지로를 구한 것은 미국의 포경선이었다.", "translation": "It was an American whaling ship that rescued the drifting Manjiro.", "vocab": [{"ko": "표류", "en": "drifting; being adrift", "note": "표류 중이다 = to be drifting (at sea)"}, {"ko": "구하다", "en": "to rescue; to save", "note": "here means physical rescue, not ''to obtain''"}, {"ko": "포경선", "en": "whaling ship", "note": "포경(捕鯨) = whale hunting + 선(船) = ship"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~던 (retrospective modifier)", "exp": "Verb/adj stem + 던 describes a past state or habitual action that the speaker recalls. 표류 중이다 → 표류 중이던 (that was drifting), modifying 만지로.", "example_in_sentence": "표류 중이던 만지로"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ 것은 N이다", "exp": "Puts the focus on the answer: ''the one that ~ed was N''. 구하다 → 구한 것은 포경선이었다 (the one that rescued him was a whaling ship).", "example_in_sentence": "구한 것은"}]}, {"text": "구조된 후 그는 그 배의 선원으로 합류하게 되었다.", "translation": "After being saved, he came to join the crew of that ship.", "vocab": [{"ko": "구조되다", "en": "to be rescued; to be saved", "note": "passive of 구조하다 (to rescue)"}, {"ko": "선원", "en": "crew member; sailor", "note": "일반적으로 배에서 일하는 사람"}, {"ko": "합류하다", "en": "to join; to merge into a group", "note": "합류하다 + ~게 되다 = came to join"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄴ/은 후에 / 뒤에 (after V-ing)", "exp": "Verb stem + ㄴ/은 후(에) means ''after doing ~''. 구조되다 → 구조된 후 (after being rescued). Marks temporal sequence.", "example_in_sentence": "구조된 후"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~게 되다 (come to / passive)", "exp": "Verb stem + 게 되다 expresses that a situation came about, often beyond the subject''s full control. 합류하다 → 합류하게 되었다 (came to join). Signals a natural or circumstantial change.", "example_in_sentence": "합류하게 되었다"}]}, {"text": "만지로는 선원으로 일하면서 미국 생활을 경험했다.", "translation": "While working as a crew member, Manjiro experienced life in the United States.", "vocab": [{"ko": "일하다", "en": "to work", "note": "general verb for working"}, {"ko": "생활", "en": "life; daily living", "note": "미국 생활 = life in the US"}, {"ko": "경험하다", "en": "to experience", "note": "can also be used as a noun: 경험 (experience)"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)면서 (while)", "exp": "Verb stem + (으)면서 means ''while doing ~'', indicating two actions happening simultaneously. 일하다 → 일하면서 (while working).", "example_in_sentence": "선원으로 일하면서"}]}, {"text": "이후 캘리포니아 골드러시에도 참여했다.", "translation": "He later took part in the California Gold Rush as well.", "vocab": [{"ko": "이후", "en": "after that; subsequently", "note": "used to indicate a later time"}, {"ko": "참여하다", "en": "to participate; to take part", "note": "formal verb for participation"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~도 (also)", "exp": "The particle ~도 added to a noun phrase means ''also'' or ''as well'', expanding the scope of the action. 골드러시에도 = in the Gold Rush too.", "example_in_sentence": "골드러시에도 참여했다"}]}, {"text": "10년이 지난 후에 만지로는 일본으로 돌아갔다.", "translation": "After ten years had passed, Manjiro returned to Japan.", "vocab": [{"ko": "지나다", "en": "to pass (of time); to go by", "note": "10년이 지나다 = for 10 years to pass"}, {"ko": "돌아가다", "en": "to return; to go back", "note": "돌아가다 = go back (away from speaker); cf. 돌아오다 = come back"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄴ/은 후에 / 뒤에 (after V-ing)", "exp": "Verb stem + ㄴ/은 후에 = ''after V-ing''. 지나다 → 지난 후에 (after passing). Marks what happened once the prior event was complete.", "example_in_sentence": "10년이 지난 후에"}]}, {"text": "귀국 후 그는 무사 신분을 받았으며, 공식 통역사로도 임명되었다.", "translation": "Upon his return, he was granted samurai status and was also appointed as an official interpreter.", "vocab": [{"ko": "귀국", "en": "return to one''s home country", "note": "귀국하다 = to return home (to one''s country)"}, {"ko": "무사", "en": "samurai; warrior", "note": "Japanese feudal military class"}, {"ko": "신분", "en": "social status; rank", "note": "신분을 받다 = to be granted a status/rank"}, {"ko": "임명되다", "en": "to be appointed", "note": "passive of 임명하다 (to appoint); 통역사로 임명되다 = to be appointed as interpreter"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)며", "exp": "Formal written connector meaning ''and''. 받다 → 받았으며 (received, and).", "example_in_sentence": "무사 신분을 받았으며"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~되다 (passive)", "exp": "Many 하다 verbs become passive with 되다. 임명하다 (appoint) → 임명되다 → 임명되었다 (was appointed).", "example_in_sentence": "임명되었다"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "방문하다", "en": "to visit", "note": "used for visiting places or people"}, {"ko": "최초", "en": "the very first; the earliest", "note": "Sino-Korean noun, often used in formal/news writing"}, {"ko": "알려지다", "en": "to be known; to become known", "note": "passive form of 알리다 (to make known)"}, {"ko": "어선", "en": "fishing boat", "note": "Sino-Korean compound: 어(漁) fish + 선(船) boat"}, {"ko": "나가다", "en": "to go out; to head out", "note": "directional verb away from a base point"}, {"ko": "난파", "en": "shipwreck", "note": "난파를 당하다 = to be shipwrecked (suffer a shipwreck)"}, {"ko": "당하다", "en": "to suffer; to undergo (something bad)", "note": "used when the subject is the victim of an event"}, {"ko": "표류", "en": "drifting; being adrift", "note": "표류 중이다 = to be drifting (at sea)"}, {"ko": "구하다", "en": "to rescue; to save", "note": "here means physical rescue, not ''to obtain''"}, {"ko": "포경선", "en": "whaling ship", "note": "포경(捕鯨) = whale hunting + 선(船) = ship"}, {"ko": "구조되다", "en": "to be rescued; to be saved", "note": "passive of 구조하다 (to rescue)"}, {"ko": "선원", "en": "crew member; sailor", "note": "일반적으로 배에서 일하는 사람"}, {"ko": "합류하다", "en": "to join; to merge into a group", "note": "합류하다 + ~게 되다 = came to join"}, {"ko": "일하다", "en": "to work", "note": "general verb for working"}, {"ko": "생활", "en": "life; daily living", "note": "미국 생활 = life in the US"}, {"ko": "경험하다", "en": "to experience", "note": "can also be used as a noun: 경험 (experience)"}, {"ko": "이후", "en": "after that; subsequently", "note": "used to indicate a later time"}, {"ko": "참여하다", "en": "to participate; to take part", "note": "formal verb for participation"}, {"ko": "지나다", "en": "to pass (of time); to go by", "note": "10년이 지나다 = for 10 years to pass"}, {"ko": "돌아가다", "en": "to return; to go back", "note": "돌아가다 = go back (away from speaker); cf. 돌아오다 = come back"}, {"ko": "귀국", "en": "return to one''s home country", "note": "귀국하다 = to return home (to one''s country)"}, {"ko": "무사", "en": "samurai; warrior", "note": "Japanese feudal military class"}, {"ko": "신분", "en": "social status; rank", "note": "신분을 받다 = to be granted a status/rank"}, {"ko": "임명되다", "en": "to be appointed", "note": "passive of 임명하다 (to appoint); 통역사로 임명되다 = to be appointed as interpreter"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~(으)로 알려지다 / 알려져 있다 (be known as)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "~(으)로 알려져 있다 = ''to be known as''. 알리다 → passive 알려지다 + 있다 (resultant state). The particle (으)로 marks the role or title.", "ex_ko": "나카하마 만지로는 미국을 방문한 최초의 일본인으로 알려져 있다.", "ex_en": "Nakahama Manjiro is known as the first Japanese person to visit the United States."}, {"name": "~았/었다가", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "One action is done, then something else happens. 나가다 → 나갔다가 (went out (to sea), and then ...).", "ex_ko": "그는 14세에 어선을 타고 바다에 나갔다가 난파를 당했다.", "ex_en": "At the age of 14, he set out to sea on a fishing boat and was shipwrecked."}, {"name": "~던 (retrospective modifier)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Verb/adj stem + 던 describes a past state or habitual action that the speaker recalls. 표류 중이다 → 표류 중이던 (that was drifting), modifying 만지로.", "ex_ko": "표류 중이던 만지로를 구한 것은 미국의 포경선이었다.", "ex_en": "It was an American whaling ship that rescued the drifting Manjiro."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄴ 것은 N이다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Puts the focus on the answer: ''the one that ~ed was N''. 구하다 → 구한 것은 포경선이었다 (the one that rescued him was a whaling ship).", "ex_ko": "표류 중이던 만지로를 구한 것은 미국의 포경선이었다.", "ex_en": "It was an American whaling ship that rescued the drifting Manjiro."}, {"name": "~ㄴ/은 후에 / 뒤에 (after V-ing)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Verb stem + ㄴ/은 후에 = ''after V-ing''. 지나다 → 지난 후에 (after passing). Marks what happened once the prior event was complete.", "ex_ko": "구조된 후 그는 그 배의 선원으로 합류하게 되었다.", "ex_en": "After being saved, he came to join the crew of that ship."}, {"name": "~게 되다 (come to / passive)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Verb stem + 게 되다 expresses that a situation came about, often beyond the subject''s full control. 합류하다 → 합류하게 되었다 (came to join). Signals a natural or circumstantial change.", "ex_ko": "구조된 후 그는 그 배의 선원으로 합류하게 되었다.", "ex_en": "After being saved, he came to join the crew of that ship."}, {"name": "~(으)면서 (while)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Verb stem + (으)면서 means ''while doing ~'', indicating two actions happening simultaneously. 일하다 → 일하면서 (while working).", "ex_ko": "만지로는 선원으로 일하면서 미국 생활을 경험했다.", "ex_en": "While working as a crew member, Manjiro experienced life in the United States."}, {"name": "~도 (also)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "The particle ~도 added to a noun phrase means ''also'' or ''as well'', expanding the scope of the action. 골드러시에도 = in the Gold Rush too.", "ex_ko": "이후 캘리포니아 골드러시에도 참여했다.", "ex_en": "He later took part in the California Gold Rush as well."}, {"name": "~(으)며", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Formal written connector meaning ''and''. 받다 → 받았으며 (received, and).", "ex_ko": "귀국 후 그는 무사 신분을 받았으며, 공식 통역사로도 임명되었다.", "ex_en": "Upon his return, he was granted samurai status and was also appointed as an official interpreter."}, {"name": "~되다 (passive)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Many 하다 verbs become passive with 되다. 임명하다 (appoint) → 임명되다 → 임명되었다 (was appointed).", "ex_ko": "귀국 후 그는 무사 신분을 받았으며, 공식 통역사로도 임명되었다.", "ex_en": "Upon his return, he was granted samurai status and was also appointed as an official interpreter."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mpepg80vamtl' and md5(translation) = 'cbb1d6abda27e935b8557a610ba6fdc1';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"sentences": [{"text": "나카하마 만지로는 미국을 방문한 최초의 일본인으로 알려져 있습니다.", "translation": "Nakahama Manjiro is known as the first Japanese person to visit the United States.", "vocab": [{"ko": "방문하다", "en": "to visit"}, {"ko": "최초", "en": "the first; earliest"}, {"ko": "알려지다", "en": "to be known"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)로 알려져 있다", "exp": "''Is known as''. 알리다 → passive 알려지다 → 알려져 있습니다. 일본인으로 = as a Japanese person.", "example_in_sentence": "일본인으로 알려져 있습니다"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (past verb modifier)", "exp": "Lets a past action describe a noun. 방문하다 → 방문한 일본인 (a Japanese person who visited).", "example_in_sentence": "방문한 최초의 일본인"}]}, {"text": "그는 14세에 배가 난파되면서 표류하게 되었고, 미국 포경선에 구조되었습니다.", "translation": "At age 14, as his ship was wrecked, he drifted at sea, and was rescued by an American whaling ship.", "vocab": [{"ko": "난파되다", "en": "to be wrecked; to sink"}, {"ko": "표류하다", "en": "to drift"}, {"ko": "포경선", "en": "whaling ship"}, {"ko": "구조되다", "en": "to be rescued"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)면서", "exp": "''While / as'' — two things happen together. 난파되다 → 난파되면서 (as (the ship) was wrecked).", "example_in_sentence": "난파되면서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~게 되다", "exp": "Shows a change that happened to someone. 표류하다 → 표류하게 되었고 (came to drift, and).", "example_in_sentence": "표류하게 되었고"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 (sequential)", "exp": "Connective ending linking two past events in sequence. Here, 되었고 and 구조되었습니다 show two consecutive events without a causal relationship.", "example_in_sentence": "표류하게 되었고, 미국 포경선에 구조되었습니다"}]}, {"text": "구조된 만지로는 그 배의 선원으로 합류하게 되었습니다.", "translation": "After being rescued, Manjiro came to join that ship''s crew.", "vocab": [{"ko": "구조되다", "en": "to be rescued"}, {"ko": "선원", "en": "crew member; sailor"}, {"ko": "합류하다", "en": "to join; to become part of"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (past verb modifier)", "exp": "Lets a past action describe a noun. 구조되다 → 구조된 만지로 (Manjiro, who had been rescued).", "example_in_sentence": "구조된 만지로는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)로 (as)", "exp": "Marks a role: ''as''. 선원 → 선원으로 (as a crew member).", "example_in_sentence": "선원으로"}]}, {"text": "이후 그는 캘리포니아 골드러시에도 참여한 것으로 전해집니다.", "translation": "Subsequently, it is said that he also participated in the California Gold Rush.", "vocab": [{"ko": "참여하다", "en": "to participate; to take part in"}, {"ko": "골드러시", "en": "Gold Rush"}, {"ko": "전해지다", "en": "to be transmitted; to be said; to be handed down"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ 것으로 전해지다", "exp": "News phrase: ''it is reported / said that ~''. 참여하다 → 참여한 것으로 전해집니다 (he is said to have taken part).", "example_in_sentence": "참여한 것으로 전해집니다"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에도 (inclusive particle)", "exp": "Postposition ~에 (locative/target) + ~도 (inclusive particle) meaning ''also, in addition, even in.'' Shows participation in the Gold Rush as one of multiple activities.", "example_in_sentence": "캘리포니아 골드러시에도"}]}, {"text": "고국을 떠난 지 10년 만에 만지로는 일본으로 돌아왔습니다.", "translation": "Ten years after leaving his homeland, Manjiro returned to Japan.", "vocab": [{"ko": "고국", "en": "homeland; native country"}, {"ko": "떠나다", "en": "to leave; to depart"}, {"ko": "돌아오다", "en": "to return; to come back"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~(으)ㄴ 지 N 만에", "exp": "''After (a length of time) since ~''. 떠나다 → 떠난 지 10년 만에 (ten years after leaving).", "example_in_sentence": "고국을 떠난 지 10년 만에"}]}, {"text": "귀국한 후에 그는 사무라이 신분을 받았으며, 공식 통역사로도 임명되었습니다.", "translation": "After his return, he received samurai status and was also appointed as an official interpreter.", "vocab": [{"ko": "귀국하다", "en": "to return home; to repatriate"}, {"ko": "사무라이", "en": "samurai"}, {"ko": "신분", "en": "status; social position"}, {"ko": "통역사", "en": "interpreter"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ 후에", "exp": "''After doing''. 귀국하다 → 귀국한 후에 (after returning home).", "example_in_sentence": "귀국한 후에"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)며", "exp": "Formal written connector meaning ''and''. 받다 → 받았으며 (received, and).", "example_in_sentence": "받았으며"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)로도", "exp": "Marks a role (''as'') plus 도 (''also''): 통역사로도 (also as an interpreter).", "example_in_sentence": "공식 통역사로도"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "방문하다", "en": "to visit", "note": ""}, {"ko": "최초", "en": "the first; earliest", "note": ""}, {"ko": "알려지다", "en": "to be known", "note": ""}, {"ko": "난파되다", "en": "to be wrecked; to sink", "note": ""}, {"ko": "표류하다", "en": "to drift", "note": ""}, {"ko": "포경선", "en": "whaling ship", "note": ""}, {"ko": "구조되다", "en": "to be rescued", "note": ""}, {"ko": "선원", "en": "crew member; sailor", "note": ""}, {"ko": "합류하다", "en": "to join; to become part of", "note": ""}, {"ko": "참여하다", "en": "to participate; to take part in", "note": ""}, {"ko": "골드러시", "en": "Gold Rush", "note": ""}, {"ko": "전해지다", "en": "to be transmitted; to be said; to be handed down", "note": ""}, {"ko": "고국", "en": "homeland; native country", "note": ""}, {"ko": "떠나다", "en": "to leave; to depart", "note": ""}, {"ko": "돌아오다", "en": "to return; to come back", "note": ""}, {"ko": "귀국하다", "en": "to return home; to repatriate", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사무라이", "en": "samurai", "note": ""}, {"ko": "신분", "en": "status; social position", "note": ""}, {"ko": "통역사", "en": "interpreter", "note": ""}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~(으)로 알려져 있다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "''Is known as''. 알리다 → passive 알려지다 → 알려져 있습니다. 일본인으로 = as a Japanese person.", "ex_ko": "나카하마 만지로는 미국을 방문한 최초의 일본인으로 알려져 있습니다.", "ex_en": "Nakahama Manjiro is known as the first Japanese person to visit the United States."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄴ (past verb modifier)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Lets a past action describe a noun. 방문하다 → 방문한 일본인 (a Japanese person who visited).", "ex_ko": "나카하마 만지로는 미국을 방문한 최초의 일본인으로 알려져 있습니다.", "ex_en": "Nakahama Manjiro is known as the first Japanese person to visit the United States."}, {"name": "~(으)면서", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "''While / as'' — two things happen together. 난파되다 → 난파되면서 (as (the ship) was wrecked).", "ex_ko": "그는 14세에 배가 난파되면서 표류하게 되었고, 미국 포경선에 구조되었습니다.", "ex_en": "At age 14, as his ship was wrecked, he drifted at sea, and was rescued by an American whaling ship."}, {"name": "~게 되다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Shows a change that happened to someone. 표류하다 → 표류하게 되었고 (came to drift, and).", "ex_ko": "그는 14세에 배가 난파되면서 표류하게 되었고, 미국 포경선에 구조되었습니다.", "ex_en": "At age 14, as his ship was wrecked, he drifted at sea, and was rescued by an American whaling ship."}, {"name": "~고 (sequential)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Connective ending linking two past events in sequence. Here, 되었고 and 구조되었습니다 show two consecutive events without a causal relationship.", "ex_ko": "그는 14세에 배가 난파되면서 표류하게 되었고, 미국 포경선에 구조되었습니다.", "ex_en": "At age 14, as his ship was wrecked, he drifted at sea, and was rescued by an American whaling ship."}, {"name": "~(으)로 (as)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Marks a role: ''as''. 선원 → 선원으로 (as a crew member).", "ex_ko": "구조된 만지로는 그 배의 선원으로 합류하게 되었습니다.", "ex_en": "After being rescued, Manjiro came to join that ship''s crew."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄴ 것으로 전해지다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "News phrase: ''it is reported / said that ~''. 참여하다 → 참여한 것으로 전해집니다 (he is said to have taken part).", "ex_ko": "이후 그는 캘리포니아 골드러시에도 참여한 것으로 전해집니다.", "ex_en": "Subsequently, it is said that he also participated in the California Gold Rush."}, {"name": "~에도 (inclusive particle)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Postposition ~에 (locative/target) + ~도 (inclusive particle) meaning ''also, in addition, even in.'' Shows participation in the Gold Rush as one of multiple activities.", "ex_ko": "이후 그는 캘리포니아 골드러시에도 참여한 것으로 전해집니다.", "ex_en": "Subsequently, it is said that he also participated in the California Gold Rush."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄴ 후에", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "''After doing''. 귀국하다 → 귀국한 후에 (after returning home).", "ex_ko": "귀국한 후에 그는 사무라이 신분을 받았으며, 공식 통역사로도 임명되었습니다.", "ex_en": "After his return, he received samurai status and was also appointed as an official interpreter."}, {"name": "~(으)며", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Formal written connector meaning ''and''. 받다 → 받았으며 (received, and).", "ex_ko": "귀국한 후에 그는 사무라이 신분을 받았으며, 공식 통역사로도 임명되었습니다.", "ex_en": "After his return, he received samurai status and was also appointed as an official interpreter."}, {"name": "~(으)로도", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Marks a role (''as'') plus 도 (''also''): 통역사로도 (also as an interpreter).", "ex_ko": "귀국한 후에 그는 사무라이 신분을 받았으며, 공식 통역사로도 임명되었습니다.", "ex_en": "After his return, he received samurai status and was also appointed as an official interpreter."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mpf1e915j3ob' and md5(translation) = 'c0c86181fec1022bbeebfeebd2d06769';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["In 2010, a man held a gun and stole chips worth 1.5 million dollars from the Bellagio Casino in Las Vegas, USA. This man was the son of a sitting judge. After the robbery, he was not caught by police. However, this man stayed at the very hotel he had robbed for a week. The hotel provided him with a free room and free drinks. This was because the hotel treated this man as a high-roller guest. Later, this man tried to sell the stolen chips on the internet. After that, police arrested him inside the hotel.", "Serious Teacher Shortage in Korea, School Classes Disrupted", "What is an \"Anxiety Bag\"? A Popular Trend", "The United States and China Discuss Trade Issues Again", "\"Talking Pig\" SNS Star", "\"Doing Nothing\" ''Nothing Maxing'' Trend Spreading"], "sentences": [{"text": "2010년에 한 남자가 미국 라스베이거스의 벨라지오 카지노에서 총을 들고 칩을 훔쳤어요.", "translation": "In 2010, a man stole chips while holding a gun at the Bellagio casino in Las Vegas, USA.", "vocab": [{"ko": "들다", "en": "to hold; to carry"}, {"ko": "훔치다", "en": "to steal"}, {"ko": "칩", "en": "chip"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고", "exp": "Connective ending linking two actions performed simultaneously or sequentially by the same subject. From 들다 → 들고.", "example_in_sentence": "총을 들고 칩을 훔쳤어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense polite ending. From 훔치다 → 훔쳤어요.", "example_in_sentence": "훔쳤어요"}]}, {"text": "훔친 칩의 가치는 150만 달러였어요.", "translation": "The value of the stolen chips was 1.5 million dollars.", "vocab": [{"ko": "가치", "en": "value; worth"}, {"ko": "달러", "en": "dollar"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (past verb modifier)", "exp": "Lets a past action describe a noun. 훔치다 → 훔친 칩 (the stolen chips).", "example_in_sentence": "훔친 칩"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~였어요 (past of 이다)", "exp": "Past polite form of 이다 (to be). After a vowel, 이었어요 shortens to 였어요: 달러였어요 (was ... dollars).", "example_in_sentence": "였어요"}]}, {"text": "이 남자는 현직 판사의 아들이었어요.", "translation": "This man was the son of a sitting judge.", "vocab": [{"ko": "현직", "en": "active duty; in office"}, {"ko": "판사", "en": "judge"}, {"ko": "아들", "en": "son"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~의 (possessive)", "exp": "Shows possession: ''s / of. 판사의 아들 (the judge''s son).", "example_in_sentence": "현직 판사의 아들"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이었어요 (past of 이다)", "exp": "Past polite form of 이다 (to be). After a consonant it stays 이었어요: 아들 + 이었어요 = was the son.", "example_in_sentence": "아들이었어요"}]}, {"text": "강도 사건 후에 경찰에게 잡히지 않았어요.", "translation": "After the robbery incident, he was not caught by police.", "vocab": [{"ko": "강도", "en": "robbery; robber"}, {"ko": "사건", "en": "incident; case"}, {"ko": "경찰", "en": "police"}, {"ko": "잡히다", "en": "to be caught; to be arrested"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~ 후에 (after)", "exp": "Temporal expression indicating a time point following a prior event.", "example_in_sentence": "강도 사건 후에"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~지 않다", "exp": "Negation auxiliary. From 잡히다 → 잡히지 않다.", "example_in_sentence": "잡히지 않았어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense polite ending.", "example_in_sentence": "않았어요"}]}, {"text": "그런데 이 남자는 자신이 강도한 바로 그 호텔에서 일주일 동안 머물렀어요.", "translation": "However, this man stayed for a week at the very hotel he had robbed.", "vocab": [{"ko": "자신", "en": "oneself; himself"}, {"ko": "머무르다", "en": "to stay; to remain"}, {"ko": "일주일", "en": "one week"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~ 동안 (during; for)", "exp": "Duration marker indicating a time span or period.", "example_in_sentence": "일주일 동안"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (past verb modifier)", "exp": "Lets a past action describe a noun. 강도하다 → 강도한 호텔 (the hotel he robbed).", "example_in_sentence": "강도한 바로 그 호텔"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요 (past polite)", "exp": "Past polite ending. 머무르다 (to stay) is 르-irregular: 머무르다 → 머물렀어요 (stayed).", "example_in_sentence": "머물렀어요"}]}, {"text": "호텔은 이 남자에게 무료 방과 무료 음료를 제공했어요.", "translation": "The hotel provided him with a free room and complimentary beverages.", "vocab": [{"ko": "무료", "en": "free (of charge)"}, {"ko": "음료", "en": "beverage; drink"}, {"ko": "제공하다", "en": "to provide; to offer"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~과/와", "exp": "Coordinating particle joining two noun objects of equal status.", "example_in_sentence": "무료 방과 무료 음료를"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense polite ending. From 제공하다 → 제공했어요.", "example_in_sentence": "제공했어요"}]}, {"text": "호텔이 이 남자를 큰손 손님으로 대우했기 때문이에요.", "translation": "It was because the hotel treated this man as a high-roller guest.", "vocab": [{"ko": "큰손", "en": "high-roller; big spender"}, {"ko": "손님", "en": "guest; customer"}, {"ko": "대우하다", "en": "to treat"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~기 때문이다 (because; due to the fact that)", "exp": "Causal expression explaining the reason for a preceding action or state. ~기: nominalizing suffix; 때문: reason.", "example_in_sentence": "대우했기 때문이에요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)로 (as)", "exp": "Marks a role: ''as''. 손님 → 손님으로 (as a guest).", "example_in_sentence": "큰손 손님으로"}]}, {"text": "나중에 이 남자는 훔친 칩을 인터넷에서 팔려고 했어요.", "translation": "Later, this man tried to sell the stolen chips on the internet.", "vocab": [{"ko": "나중에", "en": "later; afterwards"}, {"ko": "팔다", "en": "to sell"}, {"ko": "인터넷", "en": "internet"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)려고 하다", "exp": "Shows an attempt or plan: ''try to''. 팔다 → 팔려고 했어요 (tried to sell).", "example_in_sentence": "팔려고 했어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (past verb modifier)", "exp": "Lets a past action describe a noun. 훔치다 → 훔친 칩 (the stolen chips).", "example_in_sentence": "훔친 칩"}]}, {"text": "그 후에 경찰이 호텔 안에서 이 남자를 체포했어요.", "translation": "After that, police arrested this man inside the hotel.", "vocab": [{"ko": "그 후에", "en": "after that; afterwards"}, {"ko": "체포하다", "en": "to arrest; to apprehend"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~ 안에서 (inside; within)", "exp": "Spatial expression indicating location or scope within a boundary.", "example_in_sentence": "호텔 안에서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense polite ending. From 체포하다 → 체포했어요.", "example_in_sentence": "체포했어요"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "들다", "en": "to hold; to carry", "note": ""}, {"ko": "훔치다", "en": "to steal", "note": ""}, {"ko": "칩", "en": "chip", "note": ""}, {"ko": "가치", "en": "value; worth", "note": ""}, {"ko": "달러", "en": "dollar", "note": ""}, {"ko": "현직", "en": "active duty; in office", "note": ""}, {"ko": "판사", "en": "judge", "note": ""}, {"ko": "아들", "en": "son", "note": ""}, {"ko": "강도", "en": "robbery; robber", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사건", "en": "incident; case", "note": ""}, {"ko": "경찰", "en": "police", "note": ""}, {"ko": "잡히다", "en": "to be caught; to be arrested", "note": ""}, {"ko": "자신", "en": "oneself; himself", "note": ""}, {"ko": "머무르다", "en": "to stay; to remain", "note": ""}, {"ko": "일주일", "en": "one week", "note": ""}, {"ko": "무료", "en": "free (of charge)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "음료", "en": "beverage; drink", "note": ""}, {"ko": "제공하다", "en": "to provide; to offer", "note": ""}, {"ko": "큰손", "en": "high-roller; big spender", "note": ""}, {"ko": "손님", "en": "guest; customer", "note": ""}, {"ko": "대우하다", "en": "to treat", "note": ""}, {"ko": "나중에", "en": "later; afterwards", "note": ""}, {"ko": "팔다", "en": "to sell", "note": ""}, {"ko": "인터넷", "en": "internet", "note": ""}, {"ko": "그 후에", "en": "after that; afterwards", "note": ""}, {"ko": "체포하다", "en": "to arrest; to apprehend", "note": ""}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~고", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Connective ending linking two actions performed simultaneously or sequentially by the same subject. From 들다 → 들고.", "ex_ko": "2010년에 한 남자가 미국 라스베이거스의 벨라지오 카지노에서 총을 들고 칩을 훔쳤어요.", "ex_en": "In 2010, a man stole chips while holding a gun at the Bellagio casino in Las Vegas, USA."}, {"name": "~았/었어요 (past polite)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Past polite ending. 머무르다 (to stay) is 르-irregular: 머무르다 → 머물렀어요 (stayed).", "ex_ko": "2010년에 한 남자가 미국 라스베이거스의 벨라지오 카지노에서 총을 들고 칩을 훔쳤어요.", "ex_en": "In 2010, a man stole chips while holding a gun at the Bellagio casino in Las Vegas, USA."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄴ (past verb modifier)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Lets a past action describe a noun. 강도하다 → 강도한 호텔 (the hotel he robbed).", "ex_ko": "훔친 칩의 가치는 150만 달러였어요.", "ex_en": "The value of the stolen chips was 1.5 million dollars."}, {"name": "~였어요 (past of 이다)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Past polite form of 이다 (to be). After a vowel, 이었어요 shortens to 였어요: 달러였어요 (was ... dollars).", "ex_ko": "훔친 칩의 가치는 150만 달러였어요.", "ex_en": "The value of the stolen chips was 1.5 million dollars."}, {"name": "~의 (possessive)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Shows possession: ''s / of. 판사의 아들 (the judge''s son).", "ex_ko": "이 남자는 현직 판사의 아들이었어요.", "ex_en": "This man was the son of a sitting judge."}, {"name": "~이었어요 (past of 이다)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Past polite form of 이다 (to be). After a consonant it stays 이었어요: 아들 + 이었어요 = was the son.", "ex_ko": "이 남자는 현직 판사의 아들이었어요.", "ex_en": "This man was the son of a sitting judge."}, {"name": "~지 않다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Negation auxiliary. From 잡히다 → 잡히지 않다.", "ex_ko": "강도 사건 후에 경찰에게 잡히지 않았어요.", "ex_en": "After the robbery incident, he was not caught by police."}, {"name": "~과/와", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Coordinating particle joining two noun objects of equal status.", "ex_ko": "호텔은 이 남자에게 무료 방과 무료 음료를 제공했어요.", "ex_en": "The hotel provided him with a free room and complimentary beverages."}, {"name": "~(으)로 (as)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Marks a role: ''as''. 손님 → 손님으로 (as a guest).", "ex_ko": "호텔이 이 남자를 큰손 손님으로 대우했기 때문이에요.", "ex_en": "It was because the hotel treated this man as a high-roller guest."}, {"name": "~(으)려고 하다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Shows an attempt or plan: ''try to''. 팔다 → 팔려고 했어요 (tried to sell).", "ex_ko": "나중에 이 남자는 훔친 칩을 인터넷에서 팔려고 했어요.", "ex_en": "Later, this man tried to sell the stolen chips on the internet."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mpfls6covxxs' and md5(translation) = 'e9bc72ee51c9841e5cabc19a7c5b1393';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"sentences": [{"text": "디즈니가 테마파크에 안면 인식 기술을 도입한 후 소송에 직면하게 되었습니다.", "translation": "After Disney introduced facial recognition technology to its theme park, it faced a lawsuit.", "vocab": [{"ko": "안면 인식", "en": "facial recognition"}, {"ko": "도입하다", "en": "to introduce; to adopt"}, {"ko": "소송", "en": "lawsuit; litigation"}, {"ko": "직면하다", "en": "to face; to confront"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ 후(에)", "exp": "''After doing''. 도입하다 → 도입한 후 (after introducing).", "example_in_sentence": "도입한 후"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~게 되다", "exp": "Shows a situation that came about, often not by choice. 직면하다 → 직면하게 되었습니다 (came to face).", "example_in_sentence": "직면하게 되었습니다"}]}, {"text": "이 기술은 지난달 말부터 적용되기 시작했습니다.", "translation": "This technology began to be applied from the end of last month.", "vocab": [{"ko": "지난달", "en": "last month"}, {"ko": "적용되다", "en": "to be applied; to be implemented"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~부터", "exp": "Particle marking the starting point in time or space. ''From the end of last month onwards.''", "example_in_sentence": "지난달 말부터"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~기 시작하다", "exp": "Auxiliary construction marking the beginning of an action or state. Root: 적용되다 → 적용되기 시작했다.", "example_in_sentence": "적용되기 시작했습니다"}]}, {"text": "디즈니 측은 이 기술이 입장 절차를 빠르게 처리하기 위해 도입된 것이라고 밝혔습니다.", "translation": "Disney stated that this technology was introduced to quickly process entry procedures.", "vocab": [{"ko": "입장", "en": "entry; admission"}, {"ko": "절차", "en": "procedure; process"}, {"ko": "처리하다", "en": "to process; to handle"}, {"ko": "밝히다", "en": "to state; to clarify"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~기 위해(서)", "exp": "Connective expressing purpose or intention. ''In order to / for the purpose of.'' Root: 처리하다 → 처리하기 위해.", "example_in_sentence": "처리하기 위해"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ 것이다", "exp": "States or explains a fact: ''it is that ~''. 도입되다 → 도입된 것이다 (it was introduced (for this)).", "example_in_sentence": "도입된 것이라고"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(이)라고 밝히다", "exp": "Reports a statement: ''state that ~''. 것이다 → 것이라고 밝혔습니다 (stated that it was).", "example_in_sentence": "도입된 것이라고 밝혔습니다"}]}, {"text": "방문객들이 더 편리하게 입장할 수 있도록 설계된 것이라고 합니다.", "translation": "It is said to be designed so that visitors can enter more conveniently.", "vocab": [{"ko": "방문객", "en": "visitor"}, {"ko": "편리하다", "en": "convenient; comfortable"}, {"ko": "설계되다", "en": "to be designed"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~도록", "exp": "Connective marking purpose or result state. ''In order that / so that.'' Root: 입장할 수 있다 → 입장할 수 있도록.", "example_in_sentence": "입장할 수 있도록"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ 것이라고 하다", "exp": "Reports what was said: ''it is said that ~''. 설계되다 → 설계된 것이라고 합니다 (it is said that it was designed).", "example_in_sentence": "설계된 것이라고 합니다"}]}, {"text": "그러나 이 기술의 도입은 논란을 불러일으키면서 법적 분쟁으로까지 이어졌습니다.", "translation": "However, the introduction of this technology sparked controversy and even led to a legal dispute.", "vocab": [{"ko": "논란", "en": "controversy; dispute"}, {"ko": "불러일으키다", "en": "to trigger; to cause; to spark"}, {"ko": "법적", "en": "legal"}, {"ko": "분쟁", "en": "conflict; dispute"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)면서", "exp": "''While / as'' — two things happen together. 불러일으키다 → 불러일으키면서 (while sparking).", "example_in_sentence": "불러일으키면서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)로까지", "exp": "''Even (as far as)'': direction 으로 + 까지. 분쟁으로까지 (even into a dispute).", "example_in_sentence": "분쟁으로까지"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~(으)로 이어지다", "exp": "''Lead to / develop into''. 분쟁으로 이어졌습니다 (led to a dispute).", "example_in_sentence": "분쟁으로까지 이어졌습니다"}]}, {"text": "생체 인식 데이터 수집에 반발하는 소송이 제기된 상황입니다.", "translation": "A lawsuit challenging the collection of biometric data has been filed.", "vocab": [{"ko": "생체 인식", "en": "biometric identification"}, {"ko": "데이터", "en": "data"}, {"ko": "수집", "en": "collection; gathering"}, {"ko": "반발하다", "en": "to resist; to object; to oppose"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 (present verb modifier)", "exp": "Lets an action describe a noun. 반발하다 → 반발하는 소송 (a lawsuit opposing ~).", "example_in_sentence": "반발하는 소송"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ 상황이다", "exp": "News style: ''the situation is that ~''. 제기되다 → 제기된 상황입니다 (a lawsuit has been filed).", "example_in_sentence": "제기된 상황입니다"}]}, {"text": "소송이 제기된 만큼 디즈니는 향후 법적 절차를 밟아야 할 것입니다.", "translation": "Since a lawsuit has been filed, Disney will have to go through legal proceedings from now on.", "vocab": [{"ko": "향후", "en": "going forward; in the future; henceforth"}, {"ko": "절차", "en": "procedure; process"}, {"ko": "밟다", "en": "to step; to follow; to take (steps)"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~(으)ㄴ 만큼", "exp": "''Since / given that ~''. 제기되다 → 제기된 만큼 (since a lawsuit has been filed).", "example_in_sentence": "제기된 만큼"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어야 하다", "exp": "Modal auxiliary expressing obligation or necessity. Root: 밟다 → 밟아야 하다. ''Must follow / will have to follow.''", "example_in_sentence": "밟아야 할"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 것이다", "exp": "Shows a prediction: ''will (probably)''. 밟아야 하다 → 밟아야 할 것입니다 (will have to go through).", "example_in_sentence": "밟아야 할 것입니다"}]}, {"text": "이번 사안이 어떻게 결론 날지는 아직 알 수 없습니다.", "translation": "It is still unknown how this matter will conclude.", "vocab": [{"ko": "사안", "en": "matter; issue; case"}, {"ko": "결론", "en": "conclusion; outcome"}, {"ko": "결론(이) 나다", "en": "to be concluded; to be settled"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ지", "exp": "Embeds an uncertain question: ''how / whether ~ will''. 결론 나다 → 결론 날지 (how it will end).", "example_in_sentence": "결론 날지는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 수 없다", "exp": "''Cannot''. 알다 → 알 수 없습니다 (cannot know).", "example_in_sentence": "알 수 없습니다"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "안면 인식", "en": "facial recognition", "note": ""}, {"ko": "도입하다", "en": "to introduce; to adopt", "note": ""}, {"ko": "소송", "en": "lawsuit; litigation", "note": ""}, {"ko": "직면하다", "en": "to face; to confront", "note": ""}, {"ko": "지난달", "en": "last month", "note": ""}, {"ko": "적용되다", "en": "to be applied; to be implemented", "note": ""}, {"ko": "입장", "en": "entry; admission", "note": ""}, {"ko": "절차", "en": "procedure; process", "note": ""}, {"ko": "처리하다", "en": "to process; to handle", "note": ""}, {"ko": "밝히다", "en": "to state; to clarify", "note": ""}, {"ko": "방문객", "en": "visitor", "note": ""}, {"ko": "편리하다", "en": "convenient; comfortable", "note": ""}, {"ko": "설계되다", "en": "to be designed", "note": ""}, {"ko": "논란", "en": "controversy; dispute", "note": ""}, {"ko": "불러일으키다", "en": "to trigger; to cause; to spark", "note": ""}, {"ko": "법적", "en": "legal", "note": ""}, {"ko": "분쟁", "en": "conflict; dispute", "note": ""}, {"ko": "생체 인식", "en": "biometric identification", "note": ""}, {"ko": "데이터", "en": "data", "note": ""}, {"ko": "수집", "en": "collection; gathering", "note": ""}, {"ko": "반발하다", "en": "to resist; to object; to oppose", "note": ""}, {"ko": "향후", "en": "going forward; in the future; henceforth", "note": ""}, {"ko": "밟다", "en": "to step; to follow; to take (steps)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사안", "en": "matter; issue; case", "note": ""}, {"ko": "결론", "en": "conclusion; outcome", "note": ""}, {"ko": "결론(이) 나다", "en": "to be concluded; to be settled", "note": ""}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~(으)ㄴ 후(에)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "''After doing''. 도입하다 → 도입한 후 (after introducing).", "ex_ko": "디즈니가 테마파크에 안면 인식 기술을 도입한 후 소송에 직면하게 되었습니다.", "ex_en": "After Disney introduced facial recognition technology to its theme park, it faced a lawsuit."}, {"name": "~게 되다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Shows a situation that came about, often not by choice. 직면하다 → 직면하게 되었습니다 (came to face).", "ex_ko": "디즈니가 테마파크에 안면 인식 기술을 도입한 후 소송에 직면하게 되었습니다.", "ex_en": "After Disney introduced facial recognition technology to its theme park, it faced a lawsuit."}, {"name": "~부터", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Particle marking the starting point in time or space. ''From the end of last month onwards.''", "ex_ko": "이 기술은 지난달 말부터 적용되기 시작했습니다.", "ex_en": "This technology began to be applied from the end of last month."}, {"name": "~기 시작하다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Auxiliary construction marking the beginning of an action or state. Root: 적용되다 → 적용되기 시작했다.", "ex_ko": "이 기술은 지난달 말부터 적용되기 시작했습니다.", "ex_en": "This technology began to be applied from the end of last month."}, {"name": "~기 위해(서)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Connective expressing purpose or intention. ''In order to / for the purpose of.'' Root: 처리하다 → 처리하기 위해.", "ex_ko": "디즈니 측은 이 기술이 입장 절차를 빠르게 처리하기 위해 도입된 것이라고 밝혔습니다.", "ex_en": "Disney stated that this technology was introduced to quickly process entry procedures."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄴ 것이다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "States or explains a fact: ''it is that ~''. 도입되다 → 도입된 것이다 (it was introduced (for this)).", "ex_ko": "디즈니 측은 이 기술이 입장 절차를 빠르게 처리하기 위해 도입된 것이라고 밝혔습니다.", "ex_en": "Disney stated that this technology was introduced to quickly process entry procedures."}, {"name": "~(이)라고 밝히다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Reports a statement: ''state that ~''. 것이다 → 것이라고 밝혔습니다 (stated that it was).", "ex_ko": "디즈니 측은 이 기술이 입장 절차를 빠르게 처리하기 위해 도입된 것이라고 밝혔습니다.", "ex_en": "Disney stated that this technology was introduced to quickly process entry procedures."}, {"name": "~도록", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Connective marking purpose or result state. ''In order that / so that.'' Root: 입장할 수 있다 → 입장할 수 있도록.", "ex_ko": "방문객들이 더 편리하게 입장할 수 있도록 설계된 것이라고 합니다.", "ex_en": "It is said to be designed so that visitors can enter more conveniently."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄴ 것이라고 하다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Reports what was said: ''it is said that ~''. 설계되다 → 설계된 것이라고 합니다 (it is said that it was designed).", "ex_ko": "방문객들이 더 편리하게 입장할 수 있도록 설계된 것이라고 합니다.", "ex_en": "It is said to be designed so that visitors can enter more conveniently."}, {"name": "~(으)면서", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "''While / as'' — two things happen together. 불러일으키다 → 불러일으키면서 (while sparking).", "ex_ko": "그러나 이 기술의 도입은 논란을 불러일으키면서 법적 분쟁으로까지 이어졌습니다.", "ex_en": "However, the introduction of this technology sparked controversy and even led to a legal dispute."}, {"name": "~(으)로까지", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "''Even (as far as)'': direction 으로 + 까지. 분쟁으로까지 (even into a dispute).", "ex_ko": "그러나 이 기술의 도입은 논란을 불러일으키면서 법적 분쟁으로까지 이어졌습니다.", "ex_en": "However, the introduction of this technology sparked controversy and even led to a legal dispute."}, {"name": "~는 (present verb modifier)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Lets an action describe a noun. 반발하다 → 반발하는 소송 (a lawsuit opposing ~).", "ex_ko": "생체 인식 데이터 수집에 반발하는 소송이 제기된 상황입니다.", "ex_en": "A lawsuit challenging the collection of biometric data has been filed."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄴ 상황이다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "News style: ''the situation is that ~''. 제기되다 → 제기된 상황입니다 (a lawsuit has been filed).", "ex_ko": "생체 인식 데이터 수집에 반발하는 소송이 제기된 상황입니다.", "ex_en": "A lawsuit challenging the collection of biometric data has been filed."}, {"name": "~아/어야 하다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Modal auxiliary expressing obligation or necessity. Root: 밟다 → 밟아야 하다. ''Must follow / will have to follow.''", "ex_ko": "소송이 제기된 만큼 디즈니는 향후 법적 절차를 밟아야 할 것입니다.", "ex_en": "Since a lawsuit has been filed, Disney will have to go through legal proceedings from now on."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 것이다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Shows a prediction: ''will (probably)''. 밟아야 하다 → 밟아야 할 것입니다 (will have to go through).", "ex_ko": "소송이 제기된 만큼 디즈니는 향후 법적 절차를 밟아야 할 것입니다.", "ex_en": "Since a lawsuit has been filed, Disney will have to go through legal proceedings from now on."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mpg49x62ok9g' and md5(translation) = '68e40f1d3adea06db32a9f257cebc961';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["John Wayne Gacy, a serial killer from the United States, actively participated in political activities even while committing his crimes. He actively engaged in local community activities and attended various events in order to interact with politicians.", "While attending a Polish Constitution Day parade, Gacy came to meet the former First Lady Rosalynn Carter directly. It is said that at this event, he even received special security clearance.", "The granting of security clearance to Gacy at that time is known to have later become a great embarrassment to the Secret Service. Even after the fact that he was a serial killer was revealed, this incident continued to be discussed for some time.", "This case remains as an example that demonstrates how difficult identity verification can be while a criminal engages in normal social activities."], "sentences": [{"text": "미국의 연쇄 살인범 존 웨인 게이시는 범행을 저지르는 동안 정치 활동에도 적극적으로 참여했습니다.", "translation": "John Wayne Gacy, a serial killer from the United States, actively participated in political activities even while committing his crimes.", "vocab": [{"ko": "연쇄 살인범", "en": "serial killer", "note": ""}, {"ko": "범행", "en": "crime; criminal act", "note": ""}, {"ko": "저지르다", "en": "to commit (wrongdoing)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "정치 활동", "en": "political activity", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "범행을 저지르다", "exp": "Collocation: ''commit a crime''. 저지르다 → 저지르는 (committing).", "example_in_sentence": "범행을 저지르는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄴ/는 동안(에)", "exp": "Duration marker. -는 동안 = \"while / during the time that\"; marks the temporal frame in which political participation happened.", "example_in_sentence": "범행을 저지르는 동안"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~도", "exp": "Additive particle. 정치 활동에도 = \"also in political activity\"; adds political participation to the set of things Gacy did.", "example_in_sentence": "정치 활동에도"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~적으로", "exp": "Adverb form of ~적 words: ''in a ~ way''. 적극적 (active) → 적극적으로 (actively).", "example_in_sentence": "적극적으로"}]}, {"text": "그는 지역 사회에서 활발하게 활동하면서 정치인들과 교류하기 위해 다양한 행사에 참석했습니다.", "translation": "He actively engaged in local community activities and attended various events in order to interact with politicians.", "vocab": [{"ko": "지역 사회", "en": "local community", "note": ""}, {"ko": "활발하다", "en": "to be active; lively", "note": ""}, {"ko": "활동하다", "en": "to engage in activity; to work", "note": ""}, {"ko": "정치인", "en": "politician", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~게", "exp": "Adverbializer. 활발하다 (active) → 활발하게 (actively); forms manner adverb.", "example_in_sentence": "활발하게"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)면서", "exp": "''While / as'' — two actions at the same time. 활동하다 → 활동하면서 (while being active).", "example_in_sentence": "활동하면서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~과/와", "exp": "Comitative marker. 정치인들과 = \"with politicians\"; marks accompaniment/togetherness in interaction.", "example_in_sentence": "정치인들과"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~기 위해(서)", "exp": "Purpose clause. 교류하기 위해 = \"in order to interact\"; marks the intentional goal of attending events.", "example_in_sentence": "교류하기 위해"}]}, {"text": "게이시는 폴란드 헌법 기념일 퍼레이드에 참석하면서 당시 전 영부인 로절린 카터를 직접 만나게 되었습니다.", "translation": "While attending a Polish Constitution Day parade, Gacy got to meet former First Lady Rosalynn Carter in person.", "vocab": [{"ko": "폴란드", "en": "Poland", "note": ""}, {"ko": "헌법", "en": "constitution", "note": ""}, {"ko": "기념일", "en": "commemorative day; anniversary", "note": ""}, {"ko": "퍼레이드", "en": "parade", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)면서", "exp": "Simultaneous action. 참석하면서 = \"while attending\"; marks temporal overlap between attending the parade and meeting Carter.", "example_in_sentence": "참석하면서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~게 되다", "exp": "Shows something that came about, often unplanned. 만나다 → 만나게 되었습니다 (got to meet).", "example_in_sentence": "만나게 되었습니다"}]}, {"text": "이 자리에서 그는 특별 보안 허가까지 받았다고 합니다.", "translation": "It is said that at this event, he even received special security clearance.", "vocab": [{"ko": "자리", "en": "place; occasion; seat", "note": ""}, {"ko": "보안", "en": "security", "note": ""}, {"ko": "허가", "en": "permit; authorization", "note": ""}, {"ko": "받다", "en": "to receive", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었다고 하다", "exp": "Reports hearsay: ''it is said that ~''. 받다 → 받았다고 합니다 (he reportedly received).", "example_in_sentence": "받았다고 합니다"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~까지", "exp": "Emphatic extreme. 허가까지 = \"even security clearance\"; pushes the permit to the extreme end of unexpected benefits.", "example_in_sentence": "허가까지"}]}, {"text": "당시 게이시에게 보안 허가를 내준 것은 나중에 비밀경호국에 큰 망신이 된 일로 알려져 있습니다.", "translation": "The granting of security clearance to Gacy at that time is known to have later become a great embarrassment to the Secret Service.", "vocab": [{"ko": "보안 허가", "en": "security clearance", "note": ""}, {"ko": "내주다", "en": "to issue; to grant", "note": ""}, {"ko": "비밀경호국", "en": "Secret Service", "note": ""}, {"ko": "망신", "en": "shame; disgrace", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에게/한테", "exp": "Indirect object marker for animate. 게이시에게 = \"to Gacy\"; marks the recipient of the permit.", "example_in_sentence": "게이시에게"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)로 알려지다", "exp": "Passive of 알리다. X + (으)로 알려지다 = \"is known/understood/reported as X\"; marks public knowledge or reporting.", "example_in_sentence": "일로 알려져"}]}, {"text": "그가 연쇄 살인범이었다는 사실이 밝혀진 후에도 한동안 이 일은 계속 거론되었습니다.", "translation": "Even after the fact that he was a serial killer was revealed, this incident continued to be discussed for some time.", "vocab": [{"ko": "연쇄 살인범", "en": "serial killer", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사실", "en": "fact; truth", "note": ""}, {"ko": "밝혀지다", "en": "to be revealed; to come to light", "note": ""}, {"ko": "한동안", "en": "for a while; for some time", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었다는 N", "exp": "Quotes a fact to describe a noun: ''the N that ~''. 살인범이었다 → 살인범이었다는 사실 (the fact that he was a serial killer).", "example_in_sentence": "연쇄 살인범이었다는 사실"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~도", "exp": "Emphatic particle. 후에도 = \"even after\"; emphasizes persistence despite completion of revelation.", "example_in_sentence": "후에도"}]}, {"text": "이 사건은 범죄자가 정상적인 사회 활동을 하는 동안 신원 확인이 얼마나 어려울 수 있는지를 보여 주는 사례로 남아 있습니다.", "translation": "This case remains as an example that demonstrates how difficult identity verification can be while a criminal engages in normal social activities.", "vocab": [{"ko": "사건", "en": "case; incident; affair", "note": ""}, {"ko": "범죄자", "en": "criminal", "note": ""}, {"ko": "정상적", "en": "normal; ordinary", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사회 활동", "en": "social activity", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄴ/는 동안(에)", "exp": "Duration frame. 하는 동안 = \"while / during the time that\"; marks the temporal context in which verification becomes difficult.", "example_in_sentence": "하는 동안"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다/없다", "exp": "Ability/possibility. 어려울 수 있다 = \"can be difficult\"; marks potential or capacity.", "example_in_sentence": "어려울 수 있는지"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~적", "exp": "Sino-Korean adjectival suffix. 정상 + 적 = 정상적 (normal/ordinary); modifies the type of activities.", "example_in_sentence": "정상적인"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)로", "exp": "Categorical transformation. 사례로 = \"as an example\"; marks the classification or categorization.", "example_in_sentence": "사례로"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어 있다", "exp": "Resultant state. 남아 있다 = \"remains (in a state of being left)\"; marks the persistent result of a past action.", "example_in_sentence": "남아 있습니다"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "보여 주다", "exp": "''Show (something to someone)''. 보이다 + 주다 → 보여 주는 사례 (a case that shows).", "example_in_sentence": "보여 주는"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "연쇄 살인범", "en": "serial killer", "note": ""}, {"ko": "범행", "en": "crime; criminal act", "note": ""}, {"ko": "저지르다", "en": "to commit (wrongdoing)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "정치 활동", "en": "political activity", "note": ""}, {"ko": "지역 사회", "en": "local community", "note": ""}, {"ko": "활발하다", "en": "to be active; lively", "note": ""}, {"ko": "활동하다", "en": "to engage in activity; to work", "note": ""}, {"ko": "정치인", "en": "politician", "note": ""}, {"ko": "폴란드", "en": "Poland", "note": ""}, {"ko": "헌법", "en": "constitution", "note": ""}, {"ko": "기념일", "en": "commemorative day; anniversary", "note": ""}, {"ko": "퍼레이드", "en": "parade", "note": ""}, {"ko": "자리", "en": "place; occasion; seat", "note": ""}, {"ko": "보안", "en": "security", "note": ""}, {"ko": "허가", "en": "permit; authorization", "note": ""}, {"ko": "받다", "en": "to receive", "note": ""}, {"ko": "보안 허가", "en": "security clearance", "note": ""}, {"ko": "내주다", "en": "to issue; to grant", "note": ""}, {"ko": "비밀경호국", "en": "Secret Service", "note": ""}, {"ko": "망신", "en": "shame; disgrace", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사실", "en": "fact; truth", "note": ""}, {"ko": "밝혀지다", "en": "to be revealed; to come to light", "note": ""}, {"ko": "한동안", "en": "for a while; for some time", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사건", "en": "case; incident; affair", "note": ""}, {"ko": "범죄자", "en": "criminal", "note": ""}, {"ko": "정상적", "en": "normal; ordinary", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사회 활동", "en": "social activity", "note": ""}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "범행을 저지르다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Collocation: ''commit a crime''. 저지르다 → 저지르는 (committing).", "ex_ko": "미국의 연쇄 살인범 존 웨인 게이시는 범행을 저지르는 동안 정치 활동에도 적극적으로 참여했습니다.", "ex_en": "John Wayne Gacy, a serial killer from the United States, actively participated in political activities even while committing his crimes."}, {"name": "~ㄴ/는 동안(에)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Duration marker. -는 동안 = \"while / during the time that\"; marks the temporal frame in which political participation happened.", "ex_ko": "미국의 연쇄 살인범 존 웨인 게이시는 범행을 저지르는 동안 정치 활동에도 적극적으로 참여했습니다.", "ex_en": "John Wayne Gacy, a serial killer from the United States, actively participated in political activities even while committing his crimes."}, {"name": "~도", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Additive particle. 정치 활동에도 = \"also in political activity\"; adds political participation to the set of things Gacy did.", "ex_ko": "미국의 연쇄 살인범 존 웨인 게이시는 범행을 저지르는 동안 정치 활동에도 적극적으로 참여했습니다.", "ex_en": "John Wayne Gacy, a serial killer from the United States, actively participated in political activities even while committing his crimes."}, {"name": "~적으로", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Adverb form of ~적 words: ''in a ~ way''. 적극적 (active) → 적극적으로 (actively).", "ex_ko": "미국의 연쇄 살인범 존 웨인 게이시는 범행을 저지르는 동안 정치 활동에도 적극적으로 참여했습니다.", "ex_en": "John Wayne Gacy, a serial killer from the United States, actively participated in political activities even while committing his crimes."}, {"name": "~게", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Adverbializer. 활발하다 (active) → 활발하게 (actively); forms manner adverb.", "ex_ko": "그는 지역 사회에서 활발하게 활동하면서 정치인들과 교류하기 위해 다양한 행사에 참석했습니다.", "ex_en": "He actively engaged in local community activities and attended various events in order to interact with politicians."}, {"name": "~(으)면서", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Simultaneous action. 참석하면서 = \"while attending\"; marks temporal overlap between attending the parade and meeting Carter.", "ex_ko": "그는 지역 사회에서 활발하게 활동하면서 정치인들과 교류하기 위해 다양한 행사에 참석했습니다.", "ex_en": "He actively engaged in local community activities and attended various events in order to interact with politicians."}, {"name": "~과/와", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Comitative marker. 정치인들과 = \"with politicians\"; marks accompaniment/togetherness in interaction.", "ex_ko": "그는 지역 사회에서 활발하게 활동하면서 정치인들과 교류하기 위해 다양한 행사에 참석했습니다.", "ex_en": "He actively engaged in local community activities and attended various events in order to interact with politicians."}, {"name": "~기 위해(서)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Purpose clause. 교류하기 위해 = \"in order to interact\"; marks the intentional goal of attending events.", "ex_ko": "그는 지역 사회에서 활발하게 활동하면서 정치인들과 교류하기 위해 다양한 행사에 참석했습니다.", "ex_en": "He actively engaged in local community activities and attended various events in order to interact with politicians."}, {"name": "~게 되다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Shows something that came about, often unplanned. 만나다 → 만나게 되었습니다 (got to meet).", "ex_ko": "게이시는 폴란드 헌법 기념일 퍼레이드에 참석하면서 당시 전 영부인 로절린 카터를 직접 만나게 되었습니다.", "ex_en": "While attending a Polish Constitution Day parade, Gacy got to meet former First Lady Rosalynn Carter in person."}, {"name": "~았/었다고 하다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Reports hearsay: ''it is said that ~''. 받다 → 받았다고 합니다 (he reportedly received).", "ex_ko": "이 자리에서 그는 특별 보안 허가까지 받았다고 합니다.", "ex_en": "It is said that at this event, he even received special security clearance."}, {"name": "~까지", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Emphatic extreme. 허가까지 = \"even security clearance\"; pushes the permit to the extreme end of unexpected benefits.", "ex_ko": "이 자리에서 그는 특별 보안 허가까지 받았다고 합니다.", "ex_en": "It is said that at this event, he even received special security clearance."}, {"name": "~에게/한테", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Indirect object marker for animate. 게이시에게 = \"to Gacy\"; marks the recipient of the permit.", "ex_ko": "당시 게이시에게 보안 허가를 내준 것은 나중에 비밀경호국에 큰 망신이 된 일로 알려져 있습니다.", "ex_en": "The granting of security clearance to Gacy at that time is known to have later become a great embarrassment to the Secret Service."}, {"name": "~(으)로 알려지다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Passive of 알리다. X + (으)로 알려지다 = \"is known/understood/reported as X\"; marks public knowledge or reporting.", "ex_ko": "당시 게이시에게 보안 허가를 내준 것은 나중에 비밀경호국에 큰 망신이 된 일로 알려져 있습니다.", "ex_en": "The granting of security clearance to Gacy at that time is known to have later become a great embarrassment to the Secret Service."}, {"name": "~았/었다는 N", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Quotes a fact to describe a noun: ''the N that ~''. 살인범이었다 → 살인범이었다는 사실 (the fact that he was a serial killer).", "ex_ko": "그가 연쇄 살인범이었다는 사실이 밝혀진 후에도 한동안 이 일은 계속 거론되었습니다.", "ex_en": "Even after the fact that he was a serial killer was revealed, this incident continued to be discussed for some time."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다/없다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Ability/possibility. 어려울 수 있다 = \"can be difficult\"; marks potential or capacity.", "ex_ko": "이 사건은 범죄자가 정상적인 사회 활동을 하는 동안 신원 확인이 얼마나 어려울 수 있는지를 보여 주는 사례로 남아 있습니다.", "ex_en": "This case remains as an example that demonstrates how difficult identity verification can be while a criminal engages in normal social activities."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mpg4ar02ltbu' and md5(translation) = 'c1436ce969541b688f3e37ae8333c945';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["Soap is a very old thing. It was first made around 2800 BCE.", "At that time, Babylonian people made soap. This is the oldest record.", "People have used soap since very ancient times. There are records that remain up to the present."], "sentences": [{"text": "비누는 아주 오래된 것이에요.", "translation": "Soap is a very old thing.", "vocab": [{"ko": "비누", "en": "soap", "note": ""}, {"ko": "오래되다", "en": "to be old; to date back", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는 (topic marker)", "exp": "Topic particle marking the subject of discussion. 비누 → 비누는 (as for soap).", "example_in_sentence": "비누는"}]}, {"text": "기원전 2800년쯤에 처음 만들었어요.", "translation": "It was first made around 2800 BCE.", "vocab": [{"ko": "기원전", "en": "BCE; before Christ", "note": ""}, {"ko": "쯤", "en": "around; approximately", "note": ""}, {"ko": "처음", "en": "first; the first time", "note": ""}, {"ko": "만들다", "en": "to make; to create", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에 (location / time / direction / target)", "exp": "Time point marker. 2800년쯤 → 2800년쯤에 (at around 2800 BCE).", "example_in_sentence": "2800년쯤에"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었/였어요 (past polite)", "exp": "Past polite ending. 만들다 → 만들었어요 (made).", "example_in_sentence": "만들었어요"}]}, {"text": "그때 바빌론 사람들이 비누를 만들었어요.", "translation": "At that time, Babylonian people made soap.", "vocab": [{"ko": "바빌론", "en": "Babylon", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사람", "en": "person; people", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가 (subject marker)", "exp": "Subject particle marking the agent. 사람들 → 사람들이 (the people).", "example_in_sentence": "사람들이"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를 (object marker)", "exp": "Direct object particle. 비누 → 비누를 (soap [accusative]).", "example_in_sentence": "비누를"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었/였어요 (past polite)", "exp": "Past polite ending. 만들다 + 었어요 → 만들었어요.", "example_in_sentence": "만들었어요"}]}, {"text": "이것이 